","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"`{\"type\": \"function_call\", \"call_id\", \"name\", \"arguments\"}`","locale":"en"},"8978":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-89","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"An assistant tool call","locale":"en"},"8979":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-90","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"`{\"type\": \"function_call_output\", \"call_id\", \"output\"}`","locale":"en"},"8980":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-91","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"A tool result","locale":"en"},"8981":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-92","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"`{\"type\": \"custom_tool_call\", \"call_id\", \"name\", \"input\"}`","locale":"en"},"8982":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-93","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"An assistant tool call carrying raw text","locale":"en"},"8983":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-94","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"`{\"type\": \"custom_tool_call_output\", \"call_id\", \"output\"}`","locale":"en"},"8984":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-95","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"A custom tool result","locale":"en"},"8985":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-96","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"`{\"type\": \"reasoning\", …}`","locale":"en"},"8986":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-97","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Reasoning data from the previous turn, handed back to the upstream (its `provider_details` when present)","locale":"en"},"8987":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-98","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Put the previous response's `output` items back into `input` unchanged, then append the matching `function_call_output` or `custom_tool_call_output` items, to carry tool calls and reasoning forward.","locale":"en"},"8988":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-99","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Tool outputs may be strings or arrays of `input_text` and `input_image` blocks. Text remains in the matching tool reply. Images, including their URL and optional `detail`, are attached to a user message immediately after the consecutive tool replies, with labels identifying their call IDs. This preserves image input for tools such as `view_image` while keeping parallel tool replies together; image bytes are never flattened into text. Image support still depends on the selected upstream model.","locale":"en"},"8989":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-100","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Custom tools such as `apply_patch` travel upstream as functions with a required string field named `input`. Hoshimi unwraps that field into the original raw text on return, including in streaming events. A grammar in `format` is passed as model guidance; the Chat transport does not enforce it with constrained decoding. Custom input is emitted after the complete JSON arguments arrive and decode successfully.","locale":"en"},"8990":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-101","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Consecutive assistant text, reasoning and function-call items form one Chat assistant message. In particular, parallel function calls share one `tool_calls` array before their results; a tool result, user message or system message ends that group. This keeps each call paired with its result when the upstream validates Chat history.","locale":"en"},"8991":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-102","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#request-fields","content":"Namespace function tools are flattened for the upstream Chat transport and restored to their exact `namespace` and `name` in both streaming and non-streaming Responses calls. Send these identities unchanged in follow-up `input` items; a named `tool_choice` may also include `namespace`. Long transport aliases are fitted to 64 characters with a stable hash; ambiguous aliases are rejected. Native `tool_search` and `tool_search_output` are not translated: clients should expose discovery as an ordinary function, return schemas in its result, and include selected tools in the next request.","locale":"en"},"8992":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-103","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#response","content":"`output` may hold, in order:","locale":"en"},"8993":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-104","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#response","content":"`reasoning`: present when the model reasoned, with the reasoning text in `summary`; structured reasoning data from the upstream rides along in `provider_details`, and an upstream that itself speaks Responses has its own `reasoning` items passed through.","locale":"en"},"8994":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-105","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#response","content":"`message`: the answer text. Left out when there are tool calls and no text.","locale":"en"},"8995":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-106","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#response","content":"`function_call`: one item per tool call, with `call_id`, `name` and `arguments`.","locale":"en"},"8996":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-107","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#response","content":"`custom_tool_call`: one item per custom tool call, with `call_id`, `name` and the raw `input` string.","locale":"en"},"8997":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-108","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Each event is a `data: {...}` line with a `type` and a `sequence_number` counting from 0, followed at the end by `data: [DONE]`:","locale":"en"},"8998":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-109","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"8999":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-110","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"When","locale":"en"},"9000":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-111","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.created`, `response.in_progress`","locale":"en"},"9001":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-112","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"At the start","locale":"en"},"9002":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-113","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.output_item.added`","locale":"en"},"9003":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-114","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"A reasoning, message or tool-call item begins","locale":"en"},"9004":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-115","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.reasoning_summary_text.delta` / `.done`","locale":"en"},"9005":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-116","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Reasoning text","locale":"en"},"9006":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-117","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.output_text.delta` / `.done`","locale":"en"},"9007":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-118","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Answer text","locale":"en"},"9008":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-119","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.function_call_arguments.delta` / `.done`","locale":"en"},"9009":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-120","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Tool-call arguments","locale":"en"},"9010":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-121","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.custom_tool_call_input.delta` / `.done`","locale":"en"},"9011":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-122","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Raw custom tool input, after unwrapping the upstream function arguments","locale":"en"},"9012":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-123","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.output_item.done`","locale":"en"},"9013":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-124","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"An item ends","locale":"en"},"9014":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-125","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.completed`","locale":"en"},"9015":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-126","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"The full response object, with `usage`","locale":"en"},"9016":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-127","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"`response.failed`","locale":"en"},"9017":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-128","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"The upstream failed; `response.error` says why","locale":"en"},"9018":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-129","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#stream-events","content":"Content-part events such as `response.content_part.added` are not sent, so client helpers that need them (the OpenAI Python SDK's `responses.stream()`, for one) do not work; iterate the events directly.","locale":"en"},"9019":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-130","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`GET /v1/models`","locale":"en"},"9020":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-131","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Response structure (capability fields omitted from this example):","locale":"en"},"9021":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-132","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"9022":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-133","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"9023":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-134","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`id`","locale":"en"},"9024":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-135","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The upstream's model name; a name several providers share is listed once (the first provider in order)","locale":"en"},"9025":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-136","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`owned_by`","locale":"en"},"9026":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-137","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The id of the provider that serves it","locale":"en"},"9027":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-138","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`free`","locale":"en"},"9028":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-139","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`true` when the station says calls are free, `false` when it says they cost, `null` when it says nothing (the usual case)","locale":"en"},"9029":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-140","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`display_name`","locale":"en"},"9030":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-141","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The display name; equal to `id` when unknown","locale":"en"},"9031":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-142","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`vision`, `reasoning`, `tools`","locale":"en"},"9032":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-143","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Image input, thinking and tool support (`tools: null` means unknown)","locale":"en"},"9033":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-144","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`context_window`, `max_output`","locale":"en"},"9034":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-145","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Context capacity and maximum output, in tokens","locale":"en"},"9035":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-146","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`can_disable_thinking`","locale":"en"},"9036":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-147","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Whether thinking can be disabled","locale":"en"},"9037":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-148","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`efforts`, `effort_default`","locale":"en"},"9038":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-149","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Thinking levels (`id`, `name`, `description`, `is_default`, `tokens`) and the default level","locale":"en"},"9039":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-150","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"`wire`, `region_sensitive`","locale":"en"},"9040":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Upstream protocol and whether availability depends on region","locale":"en"},"9041":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"The `limit` query parameter (1–1000) returns the first `limit` models and caps the wait for providers to refresh their catalogues at two seconds: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while the refresh continues in the background. Claude Code's model discovery uses `?limit=1000`. Without `limit`, the full catalogue is returned.","locale":"en"},"9042":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-list","content":"Capability fields share their definitions and conversion logic with `GET /api/v1/models` and `GET /api/v1/catalog/stream` (Management API). These extend the OpenAI response format. When model metadata is unavailable, defaults apply: `vision` and `reasoning` are `false`, `context_window` is `131072`, and `max_output` is `32768`; defaults are not upstream-confirmed capabilities. Requests with `limit` may initially return these defaults, then return known metadata once catalogue discovery completes.","locale":"en"},"9043":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"The `model` of a request is resolved like this:","locale":"en"},"9044":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"`provider/model`, where `provider` is an enabled provider id: that provider serves it, and everything after the first slash (further slashes included) is the upstream model name.","locale":"en"},"9045":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-156","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise the first provider, in provider order, whose catalogue has the name.","locale":"en"},"9046":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"If none has it and only one provider is enabled, the name goes to that provider as is.","locale":"en"},"9047":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise `404`, code `model_not_found`.","locale":"en"},"9048":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"When `model` is absent, `server.default_model` is used (**Settings** › **General** › **Default model**, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`).","locale":"en"},"9049":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Once a provider is chosen, Hoshimi rotates and retries across its accounts. When the station answers 404/410 for a model on every account, the model is held out for a while (`503`, `model_unavailable`). See Model and account behaviour.","locale":"en"},"9050":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`reasoning_effort` (Chat) and `reasoning.effort` (Responses) follow these rules. A request without an effort level is not touched, and a caller's own `max_tokens` stays as it is.","locale":"en"},"9051":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Models with their own thinking menu** (the **Models** page shows several levels, for example `disabled` / `low` / `high` / `max`): a level on the menu is used as is; anything else goes through these aliases:","locale":"en"},"9052":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Request","locale":"en"},"9053":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Becomes","locale":"en"},"9054":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`minimal`, `light`","locale":"en"},"9055":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`low`","locale":"en"},"9056":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`","locale":"en"},"9057":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`medium`","locale":"en"},"9058":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-169","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"9059":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-170","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"9060":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-171","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`xhigh`","locale":"en"},"9061":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-172","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`max`","locale":"en"},"9062":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-173","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"If the result is still not on the menu, the model's default level is used. The chosen level is written into the upstream request the way the model declares; the output ceiling is then the smaller of the model's capacity and the request's own value, whatever the level.","locale":"en"},"9063":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-174","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Other reasoning models** use Hoshimi's three output budgets (one ceiling shared by thinking and the answer):","locale":"en"},"9064":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-175","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"9065":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-176","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Written in the request as","locale":"en"},"9066":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-177","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Output ceiling","locale":"en"},"9067":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-178","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`","locale":"en"},"9068":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-179","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`, `minimal`, `low`","locale":"en"},"9069":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-180","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"2048","locale":"en"},"9070":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-181","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced` (default)","locale":"en"},"9071":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-182","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`, `medium`, and anything unrecognised","locale":"en"},"9072":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-183","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"8192","locale":"en"},"9073":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-184","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"9074":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-185","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"9075":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-186","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The model's maximum output","locale":"en"},"9076":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-187","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model whose thinking cannot be turned off, each ceiling is doubled.","locale":"en"},"9077":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-188","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The ceiling never exceeds the model's maximum output or the request's own `max_tokens`, and never drops below 512.","locale":"en"},"9078":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-189","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For these models the `reasoning_effort` / `reasoning` fields are not sent upstream; only `max_tokens` controls the budget.","locale":"en"},"9079":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-190","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model that neither reasons nor has a thinking menu, Hoshimi leaves the effort fields alone and passes them to the upstream as they are. Each model's levels and default are on the **Models** page, or in `efforts` and `effort_default` of `GET /api/v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"9080":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-191","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"TypeSafe classifiers are not chat models. They are not in `/v1/models` and are used through their own endpoints (with an account on the `typesafe` provider).","locale":"en"},"9081":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-192","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The body sent to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"9082":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-193","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`model` must be an id from `/v1/classifiers`; otherwise the answer is `404` (`Select a classifier from /v1/classifiers.`).","locale":"en"},"9083":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-194","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","conten