ntication","content":"`x-api-key` works only on `/v1/*`, and is read only when the request has no `Authorization` header.","locale":"en"},"9573":{"id":"/en/docs/api-57","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#authentication","content":"A browser's CORS preflight (`OPTIONS` with `Origin` and `Access-Control-Request-Method`) needs no key; the real request that follows is checked as usual.","locale":"en"},"9574":{"id":"/en/docs/api-58","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#authentication","content":"Keys are compared in constant time. How to set them is in Access control.","locale":"en"},"9575":{"id":"/en/docs/api-59","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Every request passes these checks, in this order, before it reaches an endpoint. A request that fails one gets:","locale":"en"},"9576":{"id":"/en/docs/api-60","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"9577":{"id":"/en/docs/api-61","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Condition","locale":"en"},"9578":{"id":"/en/docs/api-62","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Status","locale":"en"},"9579":{"id":"/en/docs/api-63","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"9580":{"id":"/en/docs/api-64","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Message","locale":"en"},"9581":{"id":"/en/docs/api-65","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Client address","locale":"en"},"9582":{"id":"/en/docs/api-66","page_id":"/en/docs/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api#request-checks","content":"Not loopback and not in `security.allow_cidrs`","locale":