:"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--refresh`","locale":"en"},"9738":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Renew credentials on a timer (off: rotate tokens by hand)","locale":"en"},"9739":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--checkin / --no-checkin`","locale":"en"},"9740":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--checkin`","locale":"en"},"9741":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Daily check-in timer for free credits (off: claim by hand)","locale":"en"},"9742":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--ui / --no-ui`","locale":"en"},"9743":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--ui`","locale":"en"},"9744":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Serve the Web UI next to the API; `--no-ui` serves the API only","locale":"en"},"9745":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"These options apply to this start only and are not written to `config.json`. An empty string for `--access-token`, `--model-api-key` or `--default-model` has no effect; the configured value is kept.","locale":"en"},"9746":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`serve` always sets credential renewal and daily check-in from these two switches, and both default to on. So even with `server.auto_refresh: false` or `server.auto_checkin: false` in `config.json` (or after turning them off under **Settings › Automation**), they are on again after a start with plain `hoshimi serve`. To keep them off at start, add `--no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`.","locale":"en"},"9747":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"What happens at start:","locale":"en"},"9748":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The configuration is read, the options above are applied on top, and the channels are built from it.","locale":"en"},"9749":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"If the address is not a loopback address (`127.*`, `localhost`, `::1`), a warning is printed. Without a tool access key the server refuses to start (exit code 4); without a model API key it warns that external model APIs accept requests without a key. `security.allow_cidrs` must also be configured, or the server refuses to start (exit code 4). See Security.","locale":"en"},"9750":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The port is bound. If it is taken, the next port is tried, up to 65535, then wrapping around from 1024; a move is logged as `Port 10600 is unavailable. Using port 10601.` With `--strict-port` only the one port is tried. If no port can be bound, the command ends with exit code 3.","locale":"en"},"9751":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The address is written to `server.json` in the data folder, the line `SERVER_READY url=<address>` is printed on standard output, and `Hoshimi running on <address>` is logged. When listening on `0.0.0.0` or `::`, the printed address uses `127.0.0.1`.","locale":"en"},"9752":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"With `--open`, the address is opened in a browser a moment later.","locale":"en"},"9753":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Press Ctrl+C to stop; `server.json` is removed on exit. Without a built Web UI (a source install that was not built), the server logs a warning and serves the API only.","locale":"en"},"9754":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Validate the configuration and report which channels and accounts would be served, without starting the server.","locale":"en"},"9755":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9756":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9757":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9758":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Print JSON","locale":"en"},"9759":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"It applies the same checks as saving settings in the Web UI: the network policy and proxy URLs, the port range, the limits, the Playground settings, and the security rules (for example, listening on a non-local address needs both `security.allow_cidrs` and `server.access_token`; `security.allow_origins` needs `server.access_token`). A problem ends the command with exit code 2 and the reason.","locale":"en"},"9760":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Each channel is written `<id>:<accounts>`; a channel that needs no account is marked `(keyless)` while it has none. With no channel enabled at all, it prints an error line and exits with code 2.","locale":"en"},"9761":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"The `--json` fields:","locale":"en"},"9762":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"9763":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"9764":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`config_path`","locale":"en"},"9765":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Path of the configuration file","locale":"en"},"9766":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`providers`","locale":"en"},"9767":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`{channel id: account count}`","locale":"en"},"9768":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/