ntent":"Default data folder","locale":"en"},"9899":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"9900":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`$XDG_DATA_HOME/hoshimi`; `~/.local/share/hoshimi` when `XDG_DATA_HOME` is not set","locale":"en"},"9901":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"9902":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`%APPDATA%\\hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9903":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"9904":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`~/Library/Application Support/hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9905":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"Typical uses: several independent instances on one machine (each with its own data folder and port), keeping the data on another disk, giving a system service a fixed location, or experimenting without touching your everyday data:","locale":"en"},"9906":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-45","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`hoshimi config set`, `hoshimi login` and the other commands change the data folder they see. When the server runs with `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR`, set the same value in any other terminal where you run these commands, or they change a different configuration.","locale":"en"},"9907":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"The files in the data folder and migration from older releases are covered in Data folder.","locale":"en"},"9908":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_log_level","content":"Controls Hoshimi's own logging (written to standard error). The `--debug` option has the same effect as `DEBUG`, for that one command:","locale":"en"},"9909":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#seeing-the-current-values","content":"The first table lists the two variables above with their meaning; when any variable starting with `HOSHIMI_` is set in the current environment, a second table, **Set now**, shows their values (`***` for names containing `TOKEN` or `KEY`). `hoshimi env --json` prints `{\"known\": {…}, \"set\": {…}}`. See the Command reference.","locale":"en"},"9910":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"9911":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"When it is read","locale":"en"},"9912":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9913":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`XDG_DATA_HOME`","locale":"en"},"9914":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On Linux, when `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is not set","locale":"en"},"9915":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"The default data folder becomes `$XDG_DATA_HOME/hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9916":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`APPDATA`","locale":"en"},"9917":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On Windows, when `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is not set","locale":"en"},"9918":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"The default data folder is `%APPDATA%\\hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9919":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`HTTPS_PROXY`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY`, `NO_PROXY`","locale":"en"},"9920":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On every upstream connection while the network mode is `auto` (the default)","locale":"en"},"9921":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"Choose a proxy, see below","locale":"en"},"9922":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With the network mode `auto` (the default), Hoshimi reads the proxy variables for each upstream request:","locale":"en"},"9923":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"`https://` addresses use `HTTPS_PROXY`, `http://` addresses `HTTP_PROXY`; when that is not set, `ALL_PROXY`.","locale":"en"},"9924":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"Hosts listed in `NO_PROXY` are reached directly: host names, domain suffixes, hosts with a port, CIDR networks, or `*` (everything direct), separated by commas or semicolons.","locale":"en"},"9925":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"The lowercase forms (`https_proxy` and so on) take precedence over the uppercase ones.","locale":"en"},"9926":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"Loopback (this machine) is always reached directly.","locale":"en"},"9927":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"A proxy address must be a valid HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 URL; a mistake is reported as an error, not silently ignored.","locale":"en"},"9928":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With no proxy variable at all, `network.system_proxy: true` falls back to the system proxy on Windows.","locale":"en"},"9929":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With the network mode `direct` or `proxy` (a configured proxy), these variables are not read, and `NO_PROXY` applies to automatic mode only. Global and per-channel network settings are in Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"9930":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"Two cloud platforms leave authentication to the official SDK, which reads environment variables by its own rules:","locale":"en"},"9931":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"**Vertex with `auth: \"adc\"`**: Google's application default credentials (ADC), such as a service account file named by `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`. Needs `hoshimi[google]`.","locale":"en"},"9932":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"**Amazon Bedrock with AWS default credentials** (no access keys or profile in the account): the AWS SDK's default credential chain, such as `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_PROFILE` and the shared configuration files. Needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`.","locale":"en"},"9933":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"These variables must be in the environment of the process that runs Hoshimi, which matters especially for a system service. The account formats are in Cloud platforms.","locale":"en"},"9934":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"The Playground's **Run commands** and **Background commands** tools add these variables on top of the server process's environment, so command output suits a model and nothing stops to wait for input:","locale":"en"},"9935":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"9936":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"9937":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Why","locale":"en"},"9938":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`PAGER`","locale":"en"},"9939":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`cat`","locale":"en"},"9940":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No pager","locale":"en"},"9941":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`GIT_PAGER`","locale":"en"},"9942":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`cat`","locale":"en"},"9943":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No pager for git","locale":"en"},"9944":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`NO_COLOR`","locale":"en"},"9945":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-84","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`1`","locale":"en"},"9946":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-85","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No colour","locale":"en"},"9947":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-86","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`CLICOLOR`","locale":"en"},"9948":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-87","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"9949":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-88","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No colour","locale":"en"},"9950":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-89","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`TERM`","locale":"en"},"9951":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-90","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`dumb`","locale":"en"},"9952":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-91","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No terminal control sequences","locale":"en"},"9953":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-92","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT`","locale":"en"},"9954":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-93","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"9955":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-94","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"git does not prompt for a user name or password","locale":"en"},"9956":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-95","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Commands run in the shell the model names, or else in **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Shell** (`playground.shell`). Its default, **Automatic**, is `bash -c` on Linux and macOS (`sh -c` when there is no bash) and PowerShell on Windows (`cmd` without it). No shell is started as a login shell, and PowerShell reads no profile. The tools are covered in full in Playground tools.","locale":"en"},"9957":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-96","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"No encoding variable is set: commands print in the encoding of the terminal Hoshimi was started from, and their output is read as UTF-8. When non-English output comes back as `�`, start Hoshimi from a UTF-8 terminal; see Output that is not UTF-8.","locale":"en"},"9958":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-97","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-hoshimi-does-not-read","content":"**Channel key variables.** The **Key env** column of `hoshimi stations` (such as `ZENMUX_API_KEY`) and other key variables upstream tools use are not read. Channel credentials come only from the accounts in `config.json`, so there is no second source.","locale":"en"},"9959":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-98","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-hoshimi-does-not-read","content":"**`HOSHIMI_CONFIG`.** Older releases used it to name the configuration file; it has been removed, and the configuration file is always `<data folder>/config.json`. Leaving it set has no effect.","locale":"en"},"9960":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-99","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-hoshimi-does-not-read","content":"**Settings.** No environment variable maps to a `config.json` key (there is no `HOSHIMI_PORT`, for example). To change the port, keys and so on for one start, use the `hoshimi serve` options; to change them for good, use `hoshimi config set` or the Web UI.","locale":"en"},"9961":{"id":"/en/docs/cli","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"page","content":"Command line overview","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Command line"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli","locale":"en"},"9962":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"How the hoshimi command is organised, its global options, how commands read the configuration, output and --json, exit codes and logging, and common command sequences.","locale":"en"},"9963":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#commands-at-a-glance","content":"Commands at a glance","locale":"en"},"9964":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Global options","locale":"en"},"9965":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#how-commands-work","content":"How commands work","locale":"en"},"9966":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Output and `--json`","locale":"en"},"9967":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Exit codes","locale":"en"},"9968":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-6","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#logging","content":"Logging","locale":"en"},"9969":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-7","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#common-sequences","content":"Common sequences","locale":"en"},"9970":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-8","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#when-the-configuration-file-is-broken","content":"When the configuration file is broken","locale":"en"},"9971":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-9","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"The `hoshimi` command starts the server, and without a browser it can also check the configuration, list channels and models, sign into free stations and change settings. `python -m hoshimi` is exactly the same as `hoshimi`.","locale":"en"},"9972":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-10","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"This page covers the shared conventions; every command's arguments are in the Command reference, environment variables in Environment variables.","locale":"en"},"9973":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-11","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#commands-at-a-glance","content":"Typing just `hoshimi` or `hoshimi config` shows that level's help (exit code 2). Help lists commands alphabetically.","locale":"en"},"9974":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-12","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9975":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-13","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Where","locale":"en"},"9976":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-14","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9977":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-15","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`--debug`","locale":"en"},"9978":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-16","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Any level, e.g. `hoshimi --debug check` or `hoshimi check --debug`","locale":"en"},"9979":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-17","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Print debug logs","locale":"en"},"9980":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-18","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`--help`","locale":"en"},"9981":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-19","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Any level","locale":"en"},"9982":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-20","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Show the help and exit","locale":"en"},"9983":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-21","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`--install-completion`","locale":"en"},"9984":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-22","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`hoshimi` only","locale":"en"},"9985":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Install shell completion for the current shell","locale":"en"},"9986":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`--show-completion`","locale":"en"},"9987":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"`hoshimi` only","locale":"en"},"9988":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Print the completion script for the current shell, to copy or install yourself","locale":"en"},"9989":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-commands-work","content":"**Every command uses the same configuration.** Each command reads `config.json` in the data folder (its path is printed by `hoshimi config path`), whatever the working directory. The Web UI reads and writes the same file. `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` moves the data folder elsewhere, see Environment variables.","locale":"en"},"9990":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-commands-work","content":"**The server does not need to be running.** `check`, `models`, `providers`, `login`, `config` and the rest build the channels from the configuration in their own process and exit when done; they do not talk to a running server.","locale":"en"},"9991":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-commands-work","content":"**A running server needs a restart to see changes.** `hoshimi config set` and `hoshimi login` only write `config.json`; a running server does not reread the file. Restart the server after such changes, or make them in the Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages instead, where they apply at once (except the listening address and port).","locale":"en"},"9992":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#how-commands-work","content":"**`serve` options apply to that start only.** For example, `hoshimi serve --port 11000 --access-token …` writes nothing to the configuration file. Precedence: `serve` options, then `config.json`, then the defaults.","locale":"en"},"9993":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Listing commands print tables by default; add `--json` for JSON to use in scripts. The commands that take `--json` are `check`, `models`, `providers`, `stations`, `version`, `env` and `config show`. `config get` always prints JSON.","locale":"en"},"9994":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Data goes to standard output and logs and errors to standard error, so a pipe receives only the data.","locale":"en"},"9995":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-and---json","content":"Commands that read the configuration hide credentials: `config show` and `config get` print `server.access_token`, `server.model_api_key`, and API keys, tokens, secrets and proxy URLs in channel and network settings as `***`; `env` prints `***` for the value of any variable whose name contains `TOKEN` or `KEY`.","locale":"en"},"9996":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"9997":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"9998":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"9999":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Success","locale":"en"},"10000":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`1`","locale":"en"},"10001":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"General failure: the command failed, was cancelled, a login failed or timed out, the configuration file could not be read","locale":"en"},"10002":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`2`","locale":"en"},"10003":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Usage error or invalid value (unknown option, a `config set` value that fails the checks); `check` found no enabled channel; `login` named a station without an interactive login; help shown because no command was given","locale":"en"},"10004":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`3`","locale":"en"},"10005":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`serve` found no free port (or, with `--strict-port`, the port was taken)","locale":"en"},"10006":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`4`","locale":"en"},"10007":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-45","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Invalid input: `config get` named a key that does not exist; `serve` was asked to listen on a non-local address without a tool access key or allowed networks","locale":"en"},"10008":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`5`","locale":"en"},"10009":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"An upstream service failed","locale":"en"},"10010":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"`130`","locale":"en"},"10011":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"Interrupted with Ctrl+C","locale":"en"},"10012":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#exit-codes","content":"While `serve` runs, Ctrl+C shuts the server down cleanly: it ends long-lived connections such as the live usage stream first, then exits.","locale":"en"},"10013":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#logging","content":"Logs go to standard error. The default level is `INFO`; `--debug` turns on debug logs, and the `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable accepts `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING` or `ERROR`:","locale":"en"},"10014":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#when-the-configuration-file-is-broken","content":"When `config.json` cannot be parsed, every command that reads the configuration (including `serve`) refuses to run, and first copies the file to `config.json.corrupt-<timestamp>`; the error message gives the copy's path. Fix or delete `config.json` and try again. The file's location and format are in Configuration.","locale":"en"},"10015":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"page","content":"Anthropic SDK","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","locale":"en"},"10016":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","content":"Call Hoshimi's Messages endpoint with the Anthropic Python and TypeScript SDKs and with curl: non-streaming and streaming, tool calls, thinking and effort, token counting, and native forwarding versus protocol conversion.","locale":"en"},"10017":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"Connection settings","locale":"en"},"10018":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#python","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"10019":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#streaming","content":"Streaming","locale":"en"},"10020":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#tool-calls","content":"Tool calls","locale":"en"},"10021":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"Thinking and effort","locale":"en"},"10022":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#token-counting","content":"Token counting","locale":"en"},"10023":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#typescript","content":"TypeScript","locale":"en"},"10024":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#curl","content":"curl","locale":"en"},"10025":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#native-forwarding-and-protocol-conversion","content":"Native forwarding and protocol conversion","locale":"en"},"10026":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"10027":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","content":"Hoshimi's `/v1/messages` is compatible with Anthropic Messages, so the official Anthropic SDKs only need a different Base URL. The model catalogue is the same one the OpenAI endpoints use, and any model can be called through Messages. Every example here was run against a local server; replace `<model-id>` with an `id` from `GET /v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"10028":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"10029":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"10030":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"Base URL","locale":"en"},"10031":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"`http://127.0.0.1:10600` (no `/v1`; the SDK adds `/v1/messages` itself)","locale":"en"},"10032":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"API key","locale":"en"},"10033":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"The gateway's model API key, sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer`; any non-empty string when none is set","locale":"en"},"10034":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"Model","locale":"en"},"10035":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"An `id` from `/v1/models`, or `provider/model`; Messages requires it and does not use the default model","locale":"en"},"10036":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#connection-settings","content":"The SDK's `api_key` parameter sends `x-api-key` and its `auth_token` parameter sends `Authorization: Bearer`; Hoshimi accepts both. When both are present, `Authorization` wins.","locale":"en"},"10037":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#python","content":"`max_tokens` is required. As with Anthropic, a request without `stream` returns one JSON message.","locale":"en"},"10038":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-22","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#streaming","content":"The SDK's streaming helper works as is:","locale":"en"},"10039":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-23","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#streaming","content":"While waiting on the upstream, Hoshimi inserts a `ping` event between complete events every 15 seconds; the SDK skips it.","locale":"en"},"10040":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-24","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#tool-calls","content":"`tool_choice` takes `{\"type\": \"auto\"}`, `{\"type\": \"any\"}`, `{\"type\": \"none\"}` or `{\"type\": \"tool\", \"name\": \"...\"}` (the name must be a declared tool).","locale":"en"},"10041":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-25","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#tool-calls","content":"Tool results go in the next user message, with `tool_use_id` matching the earlier call; put the `tool_result` blocks before any text or images in that message.","locale":"en"},"10042":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-26","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#tool-calls","content":"Put the previous `reply.content` back unchanged as the `assistant` message, thinking blocks and signatures included (see below).","locale":"en"},"10043":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-27","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"Either form works:","locale":"en"},"10044":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-28","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"`thinking.type` is `enabled`, `disabled` or `adaptive`. An `enabled` `budget_tokens` must be at least 1024 and less than `max_tokens`.","locale":"en"},"10045":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-29","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"`output_config.effort` is `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh` or `max`.","locale":"en"},"10046":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-30","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"When the upstream does not speak Anthropic's protocol, these settings become the model's own effort controls; the rules are in Anthropic-compatible API.","locale":"en"},"10047":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-31","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#thinking-and-effort","content":"In a multi-turn conversation, send the assistant's `thinking` / `redacted_thinking` blocks back with their original `signature`. Do not edit or invent signatures, and do not reuse one model's signature with another.","locale":"en"},"10048":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-32","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#token-counting","content":"When the upstream has a native counting endpoint (Anthropic accounts do by default), you get its count; otherwise Hoshimi returns a local estimate with the header `x-hoshimi-token-count: estimate`. The estimate approximates from the UTF-8 size of the request and runs no tokenizer. Counting generates no reply and adds no usage record.","locale":"en"},"10049":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-33","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#curl","content":"Add `\"stream\": true` for SSE (with `curl -N`). Leave out `x-api-key` when no model API key is set.","locale":"en"},"10050":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-34","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#native-forwarding-and-protocol-conversion","content":"Hoshimi decides per request, from the account that will serve it:","locale":"en"},"10051":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-35","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#native-forwarding-and-protocol-conversion","content":"**Native forwarding**: when the account's provider has a Messages endpoint of its own (for example `anthropic`), the request is forwarded unchanged except for the model name. System arrays, content order, signatures, cache markers, `context_management`, structured output and fields added in the future are left for the upstream to validate; `anthropic-*` headers and query parameters go along. Upstream errors come back as they are: status, body, `request-id`, `retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*` and so on.","locale":"en"},"10052":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-36","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#native-forwarding-and-protocol-conversion","content":"**Protocol conversion**: for other providers, Messages is converted to the internal Chat format first. Text, images, system prompts, tools and thinking convert; features only a native upstream has (the MCP connector, containers, `context_management`, server tools, `task_budget`, non-text documents and the like) return `400` naming the field.","locale":"en"},"10053":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-37","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#native-forwarding-and-protocol-conversion","content":"The full comparison is in Anthropic-compatible API.","locale":"en"},"10054":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-38","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#errors","content":"Messages errors use Anthropic's shape, and the SDK raises the matching exception (`anthropic.NotFoundError` and so on):","locale":"en"},"10055":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic-39","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-anthropic#errors","content":"A streaming request opens the upstream before sending response headers, so authentication and rate-limit failures still carry their real HTTP status; failures after the stream has begun arrive as an `error` event.","locale":"en"},"10056":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"page","content":"Claude Code","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","locale":"en"},"10057":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"Run Claude Code through Hoshimi: set ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and the key, choose the main and background models, use model discovery, and know the current limits of upstreams reached through protocol conversion.","locale":"en"},"10058":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#setup","content":"Setup","locale":"en"},"10059":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#get-a-model-and-the-key","content":"Get a model and the key","locale":"en"},"10060":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#set-the-environment-and-start","content":"Set the environment and start","locale":"en"},"10061":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#pin-the-background-models","content":"Pin the background models","locale":"en"},"10062":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#keep-it-in-settingsjson","content":"Keep it in settings.json","locale":"en"},"10063":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#model-discovery","content":"Model discovery","locale":"en"},"10064":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables","locale":"en"},"10065":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"How Claude Code's requests are handled","locale":"en"},"10066":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"10067":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"Claude Code speaks Anthropic Messages. Point its Base URL at Hoshimi and its requests go to Hoshimi's `/v1/messages`, authenticated with the gateway's model API key; upstream account credentials stay in Hoshimi.","locale":"en"},"10068":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"When a model's provider has a Messages endpoint of its own (the `anthropic` provider, for example), Hoshimi forwards the request unchanged except for the model name, and the upstream handles every field Claude Code sends. Models on other providers go through protocol conversion, and recent Claude Code versions send things the conversion does not support. Tested locally with Claude Code 2.1.308 (`claude -p`), converted models answered:","locale":"en"},"10069":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"`400 <provider>: context_management requires a native Messages upstream.`","locale":"en"},"10070":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"with `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1`: `400 <provider>: Messages roles must be user or assistant; use top-level system.` (this version puts a `system`-role message inside `messages`)","locale":"en"},"10071":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","content":"For now, choose models on a native Messages provider for Claude Code. The two paths are compared in Anthropic-compatible API.","locale":"en"},"10072":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#get-a-model-and-the-key","content":"Start Hoshimi and add an account on a provider with a Messages endpoint (such as an Anthropic API key) on the **Channels** page; see Channels.","locale":"en"},"10073":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#get-a-model-and-the-key","content":"Find the model id on the **Models** page or with `curl http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1/models`. Writing it as `anthropic/<model-id>` makes sure that provider serves it.","locale":"en"},"10074":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#get-a-model-and-the-key","content":"If a **Model API key** is set (**Settings** › **Access** › **Keys**), have it ready; otherwise any non-empty string works.","locale":"en"},"10075":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#set-the-environment-and-start","content":"`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` has no `/v1`.","locale":"en"},"10076":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#set-the-environment-and-start","content":"`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is sent as `x-api-key`. A stale `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` is sent as an `Authorization` header, which Hoshimi prefers when both are present, so clear it, or put the model API key in `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` instead.","locale":"en"},"10077":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#set-the-environment-and-start","content":"This is the **Model API key**, not the tool access key and not an upstream Anthropic key.","locale":"en"},"10078":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#pin-the-background-models","content":"Claude Code's background requests use its Haiku alias, and it has Sonnet and Opus aliases as well. When an alias points to a model id Hoshimi does not have, the request fails with a routing error. Point `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL` at a model the gateway has to pin background requests to it, and do the same for the Sonnet and Opus aliases when you use them:","locale":"en"},"10079":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-22","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#keep-it-in-settingsjson","content":"Instead of exporting variables each time, put them in the `env` block of Claude Code's user settings `~/.claude/settings.json`, with `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` in place of `--model`:","locale":"en"},"10080":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-23","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#model-discovery","content":"With `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY=1`, Claude Code asks the gateway for its model list to fill the model picker. Hoshimi waits at most two seconds on the `GET /v1/models?limit=1000` it sends: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while discovery finishes in the background, and each entry carries a `display_name`.","locale":"en"},"10081":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-24","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#model-discovery","content":"Claude Code's picker only shows ids that contain `claude` or `anthropic`. Name other models explicitly with `--model`, `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` or the alias variables above; Hoshimi does not rename other models to pass them off as Claude.","locale":"en"},"10082":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-25","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"10083":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-26","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"10084":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-27","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`","locale":"en"},"10085":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-28","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"The gateway, `http://127.0.0.1:10600`","locale":"en"},"10086":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-29","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`","locale":"en"},"10087":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-30","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"The model API key, sent as `x-api-key`","locale":"en"},"10088":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-31","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`","locale":"en"},"10089":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-32","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"Sent as `Authorization: Bearer`; use this or the previous one, this one wins","locale":"en"},"10090":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-33","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`ANTHROPIC_MODEL`","locale":"en"},"10091":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-34","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"The default main model, same as `--model`","locale":"en"},"10092":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-35","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL` / `_SONNET_MODEL` / `_OPUS_MODEL`","locale":"en"},"10093":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-36","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"The gateway model ids behind the three aliases","locale":"en"},"10094":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-37","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY`","locale":"en"},"10095":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-38","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`1` discovers models from the gateway's `/v1/models`","locale":"en"},"10096":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-39","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS`","locale":"en"},"10097":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-40","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#environment-variables","content":"`1` turns off experimental beta features, useful to diagnose an upstream without beta support; the effect depends on the Claude Code version, it does not remove every beta header, effort or adaptive thinking, and it is no substitute for native forwarding","locale":"en"},"10098":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-41","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"Claude Code sends `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}` and `output_config.effort`. Native forwarding passes them to the upstream; conversion maps them onto the model's effort levels.","locale":"en"},"10099":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-42","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"Native forwarding keeps `anthropic-beta` and the other `anthropic-*` headers, merged with the beta capabilities an OAuth account requires. The upstream's rate-limit headers (`retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*`, `x-should-retry`) come back unchanged so Claude Code can retry on them. An explicit `x-should-retry: false` from the upstream also stops Hoshimi from retrying on another account.","locale":"en"},"10100":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-43","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"While waiting on the upstream, a streaming response gets a `ping` event every 15 seconds, only ever between complete events.","locale":"en"},"10101":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-44","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"Hoshimi keeps no history; Claude Code sends the whole conversation every turn.","locale":"en"},"10102":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-45","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#how-claude-codes-requests-are-handled","content":"When Claude Code does not recognise a model id it prints a notice that it assumes a 200k context window; that notice comes from Claude Code itself.","locale":"en"},"10103":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-46","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom","locale":"en"},"10104":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-47","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix","locale":"en"},"10105":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-48","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"`401`, `A model API key is required`","locale":"en"},"10106":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-49","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"A model API key is set but not sent, or a stale `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` overrides `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`","locale":"en"},"10107":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-50","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"`404`, `Model '…' not found`","locale":"en"},"10108":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-51","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"The main model or an alias points to an id missing from the catalogue; check `--model` and the three `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL`","locale":"en"},"10109":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-52","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"`400`, `… requires a native Messages upstream` or `Messages roles must be user or assistant`","locale":"en"},"10110":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-53","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"The model goes through protocol conversion; see the top of this page","locale":"en"},"10111":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-54","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"Connection refused, or `Host not allowed`","locale":"en"},"10112":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-55","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"The port is not 10600 (use the address the server printed), or you connect from another machine or a container; see Access control","locale":"en"},"10113":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code-56","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-claude-code#troubleshooting","content":"Every call, failed ones included, appears on the **Usage** page with its error and the provider and account that served it.","locale":"en"},"10114":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"page","content":"Codex","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex","locale":"en"},"10115":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex","content":"Add Hoshimi as a model provider in the Codex CLI's config.toml and use any gateway model through the Responses API; covers reasoning effort, tool calls and common problems.","locale":"en"},"10116":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#setup","content":"Setup","locale":"en"},"10117":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#find-a-model-id","content":"Find a model id","locale":"en"},"10118":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#edit-configtoml","content":"Edit config.toml","locale":"en"},"10119":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#set-the-key-and-run","content":"Set the key and run","locale":"en"},"10120":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#reasoning-effort","content":"Reasoning effort","locale":"en"},"10121":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#tool-calls","content":"Tool calls","locale":"en"},"10122":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"Common problems","locale":"en"},"10123":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex","content":"The Codex CLI calls models over the OpenAI Responses protocol and lets you add your own model providers. With Hoshimi added, Codex can use any model in the gateway's catalogue: Hoshimi converts each Responses request to the upstream's own protocol.","locale":"en"},"10124":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex","content":"This page is about the Codex CLI as a client of Hoshimi. Hoshimi also has a provider called `codex`, which signs in with a ChatGPT account and offers Codex's models to the gateway; that is a different thing, see Provider concepts.","locale":"en"},"10125":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#find-a-model-id","content":"Pick a model on the **Models** page or with `curl http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1/models`. Codex leans on tools heavily, so prefer models marked **Tools** on the **Models** page.","locale":"en"},"10126":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#edit-configtoml","content":"Codex reads `~/.codex/config.toml` (or the one in `CODEX_HOME` when that is set). Add a provider and make it the default:","locale":"en"},"10127":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#edit-configtoml","content":"`base_url` includes `/v1`.","locale":"en"},"10128":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#edit-configtoml","content":"`env_key` names the environment variable holding the key; Codex sends its value as `Authorization: Bearer`.","locale":"en"},"10129":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#edit-configtoml","content":"`wire_api = \"responses\"` makes Codex call `/v1/responses`.","locale":"en"},"10130":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#set-the-key-and-run","content":"To switch models for one run:","locale":"en"},"10131":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#reasoning-effort","content":"Set it in `config.toml`, or override it on the command line with `-c`:","locale":"en"},"10132":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#reasoning-effort","content":"Codex sends it as `reasoning.effort`, and Hoshimi maps it onto the model's own levels; the rules are in OpenAI-compatible API. The model's reasoning comes back as a `reasoning` item, which Codex shows as its thinking.","locale":"en"},"10133":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#tool-calls","content":"Codex's tools for running commands and the like are `function` tools; Hoshimi converts them for the upstream and converts the model's calls back for Codex. The built-in tools Codex also sends, such as `web_search`, and tools of type `namespace` are not `function` tools, so Hoshimi drops them and the model never sees them.","locale":"en"},"10134":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#tool-calls","content":"Codex sends the whole `input` every turn with `store: false`, which suits Hoshimi's stateless Responses endpoint.","locale":"en"},"10135":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"Symptom","locale":"en"},"10136":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"Explanation","locale":"en"},"10137":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-22","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`Model metadata for '<id>' not found. Defaulting to fallback metadata`","locale":"en"},"10138":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-23","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"A warning Codex prints for model names it does not know; requests go out as usual","locale":"en"},"10139":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-24","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`stream disconnected before completion: stream closed before response.completed`","locale":"en"},"10140":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-25","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"The upstream returned an error after the stream began, Hoshimi ended the stream with an error event, and Codex gave up after reconnecting a few times. Open the **Usage** page to read the call's error. In local tests the same tool-calling task finished on some models while others were refused by the upstream with `HTTP 400` on the second turn; another model usually works","locale":"en"},"10141":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-26","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`401`","locale":"en"},"10142":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-27","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"A model API key is set, but the variable named by `env_key` is empty or wrong","locale":"en"},"10143":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-28","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`404`, `Model '…' not found`","locale":"en"},"10144":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-29","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`model` is not in the catalogue; `provider/model` names the provider","locale":"en"},"10145":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-30","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"`400`, `previous_response_id`","locale":"en"},"10146":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-codex-31","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-codex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-codex#common-problems","content":"Does not happen with Codex's default configuration; Hoshimi keeps no responses, see Connecting clients","locale":"en"},"10147":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"page","content":"OpenAI SDKs and curl","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai","locale":"en"},"10148":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai","content":"Call Hoshimi's Chat Completions and Responses with the OpenAI Python and JavaScript SDKs and with curl: non-streaming and streaming, reasoning content, reasoning effort, tool calls, images and errors.","locale":"en"},"10149":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"Connection settings","locale":"en"},"10150":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#python","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"10151":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#non-streaming","content":"Non-streaming","locale":"en"},"10152":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#streaming","content":"Streaming","locale":"en"},"10153":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#reasoning-content-and-effort","content":"Reasoning content and effort","locale":"en"},"10154":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#tool-calls","content":"Tool calls","locale":"en"},"10155":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#images","content":"Images","locale":"en"},"10156":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#responses","content":"Responses","locale":"en"},"10157":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#javascript--typescript","content":"JavaScript / TypeScript","locale":"en"},"10158":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"curl","locale":"en"},"10159":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"10160":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai","content":"The official OpenAI SDKs work with Hoshimi once you change the Base URL. Every example on this page was run against a local server; replace `<model-id>` with an `id` from `GET /v1/models` (see Connecting clients).","locale":"en"},"10161":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"10162":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"10163":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"Base URL","locale":"en"},"10164":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"`http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1`","locale":"en"},"10165":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"API key","locale":"en"},"10166":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"The gateway's model API key; any non-empty string when none is set","locale":"en"},"10167":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"Model","locale":"en"},"10168":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"An `id` from `/v1/models`, or `provider/model`","locale":"en"},"10169":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#connection-settings","content":"The examples read the key from an environment variable:","locale":"en"},"10170":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-22","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#non-streaming","content":"Hoshimi streams when a request has no `stream` field. The SDK leaves the field out when you do not pass `stream`, and `create()` then returns the raw SSE text (a `str`) instead of an object. The same holds for `client.responses.create()`.","locale":"en"},"10171":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-23","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#streaming","content":"When the upstream reports usage, the stream carries one chunk with empty `choices` and a `usage` object, without `stream_options`; that is why the loop checks `chunk.choices` first.","locale":"en"},"10172":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-24","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#reasoning-content-and-effort","content":"A reasoning model's thinking arrives in `reasoning_content`, which the SDK keeps as an extra attribute:","locale":"en"},"10173":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-25","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#reasoning-content-and-effort","content":"When streaming, read it from `chunk.choices[0].delta` with `getattr(delta, \"reasoning_content\", None)`. `reasoning_effort` takes `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, or a model's own level name; the **Models** page lists each model's levels, and OpenAI-compatible API has the mapping.","locale":"en"},"10174":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-26","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#tool-calls","content":"`tool_choice` takes `auto`, `none`, `required` or a named function. Send the whole `messages` list every round; Hoshimi keeps no history.","locale":"en"},"10175":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-27","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#images","content":"Send images as `image_url` content parts; a `data:` URL works:","locale":"en"},"10176":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-28","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#images","content":"Only models that read images understand them; look for the **Vision** mark on the **Models** page.","locale":"en"},"10177":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-29","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#responses","content":"To stream, pass `stream=True` and read the events one by one:","locale":"en"},"10178":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-30","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#responses","content":"Hoshimi's Responses stream sends no content-part events such as `response.content_part.added`. The Python SDK's `client.responses.stream()` helper relies on them and raises `IndexError`. Use `responses.create(..., stream=True)` as above.","locale":"en"},"10179":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-31","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#responses","content":"A Responses tool loop puts every `output` item of the previous turn back into `input`, followed by a `function_call_output` per call:","locale":"en"},"10180":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-32","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#responses","content":"Responses is stateless: `previous_response_id` and structured output (`text.format`) are refused with `400`, and only `type: \"function\"` tools are accepted. All fields are in OpenAI-compatible API.","locale":"en"},"10181":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-33","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#javascript--typescript","content":"As in Python, `create()` without `stream` returns the raw SSE text as a string.","locale":"en"},"10182":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-34","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"Non-streaming:","locale":"en"},"10183":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-35","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"Streaming (`-N` turns off curl's buffering):","locale":"en"},"10184":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-36","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"Each event is a `data: {...}` line, and the last one is `data: [DONE]`.","locale":"en"},"10185":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-37","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"Responses:","locale":"en"},"10186":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-38","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"Leave out the `Authorization` header when no model API key is set; `x-api-key: <key>` works in its place.","locale":"en"},"10187":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-39","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#curl","content":"In the Playground, **Copy as API request** in a reply's **More actions** menu copies the Chat Completions request behind that reply as a curl command that reads the key from `$HOSHIMI_API_KEY`, a handy starting point.","locale":"en"},"10188":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-40","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#errors","content":"Errors on `/v1` use OpenAI's shape, and the SDK raises the matching exception (`openai.NotFoundError`, `openai.BadRequestError` and so on):","locale":"en"},"10189":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-openai-41","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-openai#errors","content":"Once a stream has started, an upstream failure can no longer change the HTTP status: Chat Completions sends one `data: {\"error\": {...}}` event and ends (without `data: [DONE]`); Responses sends a `response.failed` event or the same `error` event. Failed calls are recorded on the **Usage** page, where you can read the error. All error codes are listed in API overview.","locale":"en"},"10190":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"page","content":"OpenCode","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","locale":"en"},"10191":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","content":"Add Hoshimi as an OpenAI-compatible provider in opencode.json so OpenCode can use the gateway's models; covers the key, the model list, reasoning effort, and how this differs from Hoshimi's OpenCode Zen provider.","locale":"en"},"10192":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#setup","content":"Setup","locale":"en"},"10193":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"Write opencode.json","locale":"en"},"10194":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#set-the-key-and-run","content":"Set the key and run","locale":"en"},"10195":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#reasoning-effort","content":"Reasoning effort","locale":"en"},"10196":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#tool-calls","content":"Tool calls","locale":"en"},"10197":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#free-models-through-the-opencode-zen-provider","content":"Free models through the OpenCode Zen provider","locale":"en"},"10198":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","content":"OpenCode reaches any OpenAI-compatible service through `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`. With Hoshimi configured as a provider, OpenCode calls the gateway over Chat Completions, and the gateway passes each request on to its providers.","locale":"en"},"10199":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","content":"This page is about the OpenCode coding agent as a client of Hoshimi. Hoshimi's built-in `opencode` provider works the other way round: it connects OpenCode Zen's free models and offers them to every client of the gateway; see Anonymous lanes. You can use both at once.","locale":"en"},"10200":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"Add this to `opencode.json` in the project root (for that project only) or to the global `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`:","locale":"en"},"10201":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"`baseURL` includes `/v1`.","locale":"en"},"10202":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"`apiKey` reads the model API key from an environment variable with `{env:HOSHIMI_API_KEY}`.","locale":"en"},"10203":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"The keys of `models` are Hoshimi model ids (an `id` from `/v1/models`, or `provider/model`); each `name` is what OpenCode displays. The models listed here appear in OpenCode's model list.","locale":"en"},"10204":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#write-opencodejson","content":"The top-level `model` is the default model as `provider/model`, where the provider is `hoshimi`.","locale":"en"},"10205":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#set-the-key-and-run","content":"For a single run, or another model:","locale":"en"},"10206":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#reasoning-effort","content":"Set `reasoningEffort` in a model's `options`; OpenCode sends it as `reasoning_effort`:","locale":"en"},"10207":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#reasoning-effort","content":"Use `low`, `medium`, `high` and so on, or a model's own level name. Hoshimi's mapping is in OpenAI-compatible API; each model's levels are on the **Models** page.","locale":"en"},"10208":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#tool-calls","content":"OpenCode's tools for reading files, searching, running commands and so on go out as Chat Completions `function` tools, and the model's calls are converted back for OpenCode to run. Choose models marked **Tools** on the **Models** page.","locale":"en"},"10209":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#free-models-through-the-opencode-zen-provider","content":"When you use models from Hoshimi's default `opencode` provider (those with `owned_by` set to `opencode` in `/v1/models`), two things concern the client:","locale":"en"},"10210":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#free-models-through-the-opencode-zen-provider","content":"The anonymous lane derives a session id per conversation from `session_id`, `conversation_id` or `user` in the request body, in that order, and from the first user message when none is set. Two separate conversations that open with the same message share a session.","locale":"en"},"10211":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#free-models-through-the-opencode-zen-provider","content":"The anonymous lane also declares the `read` and `shell` tools the upstream requires. A call to a tool the client did not declare never reaches the client: Hoshimi tells the model the tool is unavailable and lets it carry on answering.","locale":"en"},"10212":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients-opencode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients-opencode#free-models-through-the-opencode-zen-provider","content":"The provider's protocol details and the difference between anonymous and API-key accounts are in Anonymous lanes.","locale":"en"},"10213":{"id":"/en/docs/clients","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"page","content":"Connecting clients","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Connecting clients"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients","locale":"en"},"10214":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-0","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients","content":"What you need to point an SDK, curl or a coding agent at Hoshimi: the Base URL, which key to send, how to write model names, which API to use, and the conventions for streaming, reasoning effort and tool calls.","locale":"en"},"10215":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-1","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"What you need","locale":"en"},"10216":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-2","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Keys","locale":"en"},"10217":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-3","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"Model names","locale":"en"},"10218":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-4","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Which API to use","locale":"en"},"10219":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-5","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#streaming","content":"Streaming","locale":"en"},"10220":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-6","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#stateless","content":"Stateless","locale":"en"},"10221":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-7","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Reasoning effort","locale":"en"},"10222":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-8","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"Tool calls","locale":"en"},"10223":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-9","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#connecting-from-another-machine-or-a-container","content":"Connecting from another machine or a container","locale":"en"},"10224":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-10","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"Client guides","locale":"en"},"10225":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-11","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients","content":"Hoshimi speaks both the OpenAI and the Anthropic protocols. Any client that lets you set a Base URL can use it: upstream account credentials stay inside Hoshimi, and the client only needs the gateway's address, the gateway's key and a model name. This page covers what all clients have in common; the guides at the end give the exact configuration for each one.","locale":"en"},"10226":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-12","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"10227":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-13","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"10228":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-14","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Where to find it","locale":"en"},"10229":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-15","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Base URL","locale":"en"},"10230":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-16","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"`http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1` for OpenAI-compatible clients; `http://127.0.0.1:10600` for Anthropic-compatible clients","locale":"en"},"10231":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-17","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"The **Endpoints** section of the **Overview** page lists each endpoint with a copy button","locale":"en"},"10232":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-18","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"10233":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-19","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"The gateway's **Model API key**; any non-empty string when none is set","locale":"en"},"10234":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-20","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"**Settings** › **Access** › **Keys**","locale":"en"},"10235":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-21","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"Model name","locale":"en"},"10236":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-22","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"An `id` from `GET /v1/models`, or `provider/model`","locale":"en"},"10237":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-23","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"The **Models** page, or the curl command below","locale":"en"},"10238":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-24","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#what-you-need","content":"When port 10600 is taken, the server moves on to the next free port; use the address it prints at start-up. **Listening address** under **Settings** › **Access** shows the port in use.","locale":"en"},"10239":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-25","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Hoshimi has two independent keys, and a client uses only one of them:","locale":"en"},"10240":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-26","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"10241":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-27","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"10242":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-28","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Protects","locale":"en"},"10243":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-29","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"How to send it","locale":"en"},"10244":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-30","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Model API key","locale":"en"},"10245":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-31","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"`server.model_api_key`","locale":"en"},"10246":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-32","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"`/v1/*`: Chat Completions, Responses, Messages, the model list","locale":"en"},"10247":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-33","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <key>` or `x-api-key: <key>`","locale":"en"},"10248":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-34","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Tool access key","locale":"en"},"10249":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-35","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"`server.access_token`","locale":"en"},"10250":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-36","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"The `/api/*` management API, the Web UI, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`","locale":"en"},"10251":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-37","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"`Authorization: Bearer <key>`","locale":"en"},"10252":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-38","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Clients always use the **Model API key**. The tool access key does not open `/v1/*`, and the model key does not open `/api/*`.","locale":"en"},"10253":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-39","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"With no model API key set, `/v1/*` checks no key. Most SDKs and tools insist on a value; any non-empty string will do.","locale":"en"},"10254":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-40","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"When a request carries both `Authorization` and `x-api-key`, `Authorization` wins.","locale":"en"},"10255":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-41","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Provider account credentials (a station's API key, sign-in tokens) live only in Hoshimi. Never put them in a client.","locale":"en"},"10256":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-42","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#keys","content":"Setting the keys, LAN access and origin rules are covered in Access control.","locale":"en"},"10257":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-43","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"List the available models first:","locale":"en"},"10258":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-44","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"`id` is the upstream's own model name and `owned_by` the provider that serves it. The `model` field of a request takes either form:","locale":"en"},"10259":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-45","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"**The bare `id`**, such as `big-pickle`. Hoshimi picks the first provider, in provider order, that lists it. With only one provider enabled, a name missing from the catalogue is passed to that provider as is.","locale":"en"},"10260":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-46","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"**`provider/model`**, such as `opencode/big-pickle`, which names the provider. Everything after the first slash is sent as the upstream model name, further slashes included, e.g. `kilo/kilo-auto/free`. Use this form to choose between providers that list the same name.","locale":"en"},"10261":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-47","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"When a request has no `model`, Chat Completions and Responses use **Default model** from **Settings** › **General** (config key `server.default_model`, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`). Messages always requires `model`.","locale":"en"},"10262":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-48","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#model-names","content":"The **Models** page shows whether each model reads images, reasons, calls tools and which effort levels it has; see Models.","locale":"en"},"10263":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-49","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"API","locale":"en"},"10264":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-50","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Path","locale":"en"},"10265":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-51","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"For","locale":"en"},"10266":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-52","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Chat Completions","locale":"en"},"10267":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-53","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"`POST /v1/chat/completions`","locale":"en"},"10268":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-54","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Most OpenAI-compatible clients, the OpenAI SDKs, OpenCode","locale":"en"},"10269":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-55","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Responses","locale":"en"},"10270":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-56","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"`POST /v1/responses`","locale":"en"},"10271":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-57","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Clients that only speak Responses, such as Codex","locale":"en"},"10272":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-58","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"Messages","locale":"en"},"10273":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-59","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"`POST /v1/messages`","locale":"en"},"10274":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-60","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"The Anthropic SDKs, Claude Code","locale":"en"},"10275":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-61","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#which-api-to-use","content":"All three share one model catalogue, and any model can be called through any of them: Hoshimi converts between the client's protocol and the upstream's. Conversion does not add features the upstream lacks; a model without tool support will not call tools whichever API you use.","locale":"en"},"10276":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-62","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#streaming","content":"Chat Completions and Responses stream (SSE) when the request has no `stream` field, the opposite of OpenAI's own API. Send `\"stream\": false` explicitly to get one JSON object. The OpenAI Python and JavaScript SDKs leave the field out when you do not pass `stream`, and then return a string of SSE text instead of an object, so always pass `stream=False` for a non-streaming call.","locale":"en"},"10277":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-63","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#streaming","content":"Messages behaves like Anthropic's: JSON by default, SSE with `\"stream\": true`.","locale":"en"},"10278":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-64","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#stateless","content":"Hoshimi keeps no conversation. Send the whole history with every request:","locale":"en"},"10279":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-65","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#stateless","content":"Chat Completions and Messages: all of `messages`.","locale":"en"},"10280":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-66","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#stateless","content":"Responses: all of `input`; `previous_response_id` is refused with `400`.","locale":"en"},"10281":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-67","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#stateless","content":"Playground conversations are kept on the server, but through the Web UI's own API; see Playground API.","locale":"en"},"10282":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-68","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Each API has its own field, and Hoshimi reads all of them:","locale":"en"},"10283":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-69","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"API","locale":"en"},"10284":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-70","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"10285":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-71","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Example","locale":"en"},"10286":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-72","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Chat Completions","locale":"en"},"10287":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-73","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`reasoning_effort`","locale":"en"},"10288":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-74","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`\"reasoning_effort\": \"high\"`","locale":"en"},"10289":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-75","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Responses","locale":"en"},"10290":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-76","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`reasoning.effort`","locale":"en"},"10291":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-77","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`\"reasoning\": {\"effort\": \"low\"}`","locale":"en"},"10292":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-78","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Messages","locale":"en"},"10293":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-79","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`output_config.effort` or `thinking`","locale":"en"},"10294":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-80","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"`\"output_config\": {\"effort\": \"medium\"}`","locale":"en"},"10295":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-81","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#reasoning-effort","content":"Models differ in what they offer. A model with its own thinking menu (for example `disabled` / `low` / `high` / `max`) uses the level as named; other reasoning models use Hoshimi's three output budgets `light` / `balanced` / `deep`, and OpenAI's `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high` and the like are mapped onto them. A request that names no effort is left untouched. The mapping is in OpenAI-compatible API; what the budgets mean is in Model and account behaviour.","locale":"en"},"10296":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-82","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"The client runs the tools; Hoshimi converts definitions, calls and results between protocols:","locale":"en"},"10297":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-83","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"Chat Completions: `function` tools in `tools`, `tool_calls` in the reply, results sent back as `role: \"tool\"` messages.","locale":"en"},"10298":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-84","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"Responses: `type: \"function\"` tools, `function_call` items in the reply, results sent back as `function_call_output` items. Other tool types are ignored.","locale":"en"},"10299":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-85","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"Messages: tools with an `input_schema`, `tool_use` blocks in the reply, results sent back as `tool_result` blocks.","locale":"en"},"10300":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-86","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#tool-calls","content":"Each client page has a worked example. Whether a model actually calls tools depends on the upstream; the capability marks on the **Models** page are a guide.","locale":"en"},"10301":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-87","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#connecting-from-another-machine-or-a-container","content":"By default Hoshimi listens on `127.0.0.1` only and accepts only requests whose `Host` is `localhost`, `127.0.0.1` or `::1`, so a client on another machine or in a container (say via `host.docker.internal`) is refused. Clients running in a web page also face the origin check. Set the listening address, **Allowed CIDRs**, **Allowed hosts** and **Allowed origins** as described in Access control.","locale":"en"},"10302":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-88","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"OpenAI SDKs and curl\" href=\"/docs/clients-openai\" description=\"Python, JavaScript and curl: Chat Completions and Responses, streaming, reasoning and tool calls.\" />","locale":"en"},"10303":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-89","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"Anthropic SDK\" href=\"/docs/clients-anthropic\" description=\"Messages with the Anthropic SDK: streaming, tools, thinking and token counting.\" />","locale":"en"},"10304":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-90","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"Claude Code\" href=\"/docs/clients-claude-code\" description=\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and friends, model aliases and known limits.\" />","locale":"en"},"10305":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-91","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"Codex\" href=\"/docs/clients-codex\" description=\"Add Hoshimi as a model provider in config.toml.\" />","locale":"en"},"10306":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-92","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"OpenCode\" href=\"/docs/clients-opencode\" description=\"Add an OpenAI-compatible provider in opencode.json.\" />","locale":"en"},"10307":{"id":"/en/docs/clients-93","page_id":"/en/docs/clients","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/clients#client-guides","content":"<Card title=\"API reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" description=\"Authentication, error shapes and every endpoint's fields.\" />","locale":"en"},"10308":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"page","content":"Network and proxies","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Configuration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network","locale":"en"},"10309":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-0","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network","content":"Which route Hoshimi takes to upstream stations: environment proxies, direct or a configured proxy, per-channel overrides, which requests are covered, and how to read the network diagnostics.","locale":"en"},"10310":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-1","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Modes","locale":"en"},"10311":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-2","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"Setting the global policy","locale":"en"},"10312":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-3","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"Environment variables (auto mode)","locale":"en"},"10313":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-4","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#windows-system-proxy","content":"Windows system proxy","locale":"en"},"10314":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-5","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#per-channel-overrides","content":"Per-channel overrides","locale":"en"},"10315":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-6","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Which requests are covered","locale":"en"},"10316":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-7","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#when-changes-apply","content":"When changes apply","locale":"en"},"10317":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-8","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Network diagnostics","locale":"en"},"10318":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-9","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#provider-concurrency-and-waiting","content":"Provider concurrency and waiting","locale":"en"},"10319":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-10","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Shared capacity and business errors","locale":"en"},"10320":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-11","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network","content":"Every request Hoshimi sends upstream (model catalogues, inference, login, token refresh, balances, check-in) picks its route from a network policy: direct, or through a proxy. There is one global default and each channel can override it. This page shows how to write these policies, when they apply, and where to look when something fails.","locale":"en"},"10321":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-12","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network","content":"Login pages opened in your browser are not affected by these settings; they use the browser's own network configuration.","locale":"en"},"10322":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-13","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"10323":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-14","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"10324":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-15","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"`auto` (default)","locale":"en"},"10325":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-16","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Reads the `HTTPS_PROXY`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables to decide; direct when none is set","locale":"en"},"10326":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-17","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"`direct`","locale":"en"},"10327":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-18","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Always direct; environment variables are ignored","locale":"en"},"10328":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-19","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"`proxy`","locale":"en"},"10329":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-20","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Always through the proxy in `proxy`","locale":"en"},"10330":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-21","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"`inherit` (channels only)","locale":"en"},"10331":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-22","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Use the global policy; this is a channel's default","locale":"en"},"10332":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-23","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Two rules hold whatever the mode:","locale":"en"},"10333":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-24","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"Requests to this machine (`localhost`, `*.localhost`, `127.0.0.0/8`, `::1`) always go direct, so local model servers are never sent to a proxy.","locale":"en"},"10334":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-25","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#modes","content":"When a configured proxy cannot be reached, the request fails. It **never** falls back to a direct connection.","locale":"en"},"10335":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-26","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"In the Web UI, open **Settings** › **Network**, choose **Automatic (environment proxy)**, **Direct** or **Proxy**, fill in the **Proxy URL** and save. Or write it in `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"10336":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-27","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"On the command line, write the whole object at once (`network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL), then restart the server:","locale":"en"},"10337":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-28","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"A proxy URL must:","locale":"en"},"10338":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-29","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"use `http`, `https`, `socks5` or `socks5h`;","locale":"en"},"10339":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-30","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"have a host name, and no path, query or fragment (a trailing `/` is fine);","locale":"en"},"10340":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-31","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"may carry a user name and password, as in `http://user:pass@proxy.example.com:8080`.","locale":"en"},"10341":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-32","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#setting-the-global-policy","content":"Proxy URLs may contain passwords. They are stored in plain text in the local `config.json`; the settings API only says whether one is configured, `hoshimi config show` prints `***`, and the Web UI shows **Proxy configured; save to replace it.** Clearing the proxy URL in the Web UI and saving returns to automatic mode (or, for a channel, to inheritance).","locale":"en"},"10342":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-33","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`auto` mode picks the proxy by the target's scheme:","locale":"en"},"10343":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-34","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`https://` targets use `HTTPS_PROXY`, `http://` targets use `HTTP_PROXY`;","locale":"en"},"10344":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-35","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"when that variable is empty, `ALL_PROXY`;","locale":"en"},"10345":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-36","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"a target that matches `NO_PROXY` goes direct.","locale":"en"},"10346":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-37","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"For each variable the lowercase spelling wins (`https_proxy` over `HTTPS_PROXY`). Proxy URLs from the environment are validated too: a malformed one makes requests fail rather than being silently ignored.","locale":"en"},"10347":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-38","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`NO_PROXY` is separated by commas (or semicolons); each entry may be:","locale":"en"},"10348":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-39","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"Entry","locale":"en"},"10349":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-40","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"Matches","locale":"en"},"10350":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-41","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`example.com`, `.example.com`, `*.example.com`","locale":"en"},"10351":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-42","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"The domain and all its subdomains","locale":"en"},"10352":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-43","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`example.com:8443`","locale":"en"},"10353":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-44","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"The domain on that port","locale":"en"},"10354":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-45","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`10.0.0.0/8`","locale":"en"},"10355":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-46","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"IP address targets inside that network","locale":"en"},"10356":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-47","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`*`","locale":"en"},"10357":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-48","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"Every target","locale":"en"},"10358":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-49","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`<local>`","locale":"en"},"10359":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-50","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"Host names without a dot","locale":"en"},"10360":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-51","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#environment-variables-auto-mode","content":"`NO_PROXY` only affects automatic selection; a proxy configured in `proxy` mode does not consult it.","locale":"en"},"10361":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-52","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#windows-system-proxy","content":"With `network.system_proxy` set to `true` (**Use Windows system proxy when no environment proxy exists** in the Web UI), on Windows, `auto` mode reads the system proxy settings (including their exception list) when no environment proxy was found. The option has no effect on other systems.","locale":"en"},"10362":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-53","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#per-channel-overrides","content":"Each channel can have its own route. On the **Channels** page, open a channel and choose its route in its **Network** section; **Inherit global settings** follows **Settings** › **Network**. The matching configuration is `providers.<id>.options.network`:","locale":"en"},"10363":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-54","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#per-channel-overrides","content":"A channel with no `network`, or with `{\"mode\": \"inherit\"}`, uses the global policy.","locale":"en"},"10364":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-55","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#per-channel-overrides","content":"A channel with an explicit policy **replaces** the global one; the two are not merged. A channel with `{\"mode\": \"auto\"}`, for example, reads the environment even when the global mode is `proxy`.","locale":"en"},"10365":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-56","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#per-channel-overrides","content":"A channel's `network` object without `mode` means `inherit`.","locale":"en"},"10366":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-57","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Request","locale":"en"},"10367":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-58","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Policy used","locale":"en"},"10368":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-59","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Model catalogues, inference, token refresh and exchange, balances, check-in","locale":"en"},"10369":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-60","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The channel's policy","locale":"en"},"10370":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-61","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Requests the gateway itself makes during `hoshimi login` and the Web UI's **Sign in** (starting authorization, polling, exchanging tokens)","locale":"en"},"10371":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-62","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The channel's policy","locale":"en"},"10372":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-63","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Availability probes","locale":"en"},"10373":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-64","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The channel's policy","locale":"en"},"10374":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-65","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Vertex Google authentication calls","locale":"en"},"10375":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-66","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The channel's policy","locale":"en"},"10376":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-67","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Bedrock AWS SDK service calls","locale":"en"},"10377":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-68","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The HTTP(S) proxy the channel's policy selects; AWS credential discovery stays with the AWS SDK. SOCKS proxies do not apply to the Bedrock SDK","locale":"en"},"10378":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-69","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"models.dev capability metadata, the PyPI update check","locale":"en"},"10379":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-70","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The global policy","locale":"en"},"10380":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-71","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The Playground's `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools","locale":"en"},"10381":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-72","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The global policy","locale":"en"},"10382":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-73","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Login pages opened in a browser","locale":"en"},"10383":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-74","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"The browser's own network settings","locale":"en"},"10384":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-75","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#which-requests-are-covered","content":"Ordinary gateway requests do not keep cookies that responses set; each login has its own isolated cookie session. Hoshimi does not solve browser challenges (such as Cloudflare's) automatically and does not emulate TLS fingerprints.","locale":"en"},"10385":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-76","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#when-changes-apply","content":"After a save in the Web UI, new requests use the new route at once; streaming replies already running finish on their original connections. A network-only change does not rebuild a channel's account state: accounts held out of rotation and accounts marked as needing a login stay as they are. Changes made with `hoshimi config set` or by editing the file need a server restart. Environment variables are read on every request, but they are the ones the server process inherited when it started, so restart after changing them.","locale":"en"},"10386":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-77","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Each channel keeps the latest result of every kind of operation. On the **Channels** page, open a channel: its **Network** section lists the operations that failed most recently, with the error category and HTTP status; hover over an operation to see the target host and route.","locale":"en"},"10387":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-78","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"The management API returns the same data:","locale":"en"},"10388":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-79","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"A row holds only the operation, host, route source, time, status and error category: never request paths, query strings, headers, bodies, cookies or proxy URLs.","locale":"en"},"10389":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-80","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`operation` is one of: `catalog` (model catalogue), `inference`, `token_refresh`, `token_exchange`, `auth_start` (start authorization), `auth_poll` (authorization polling), `balance`, `checkin`, `request` (anything else).","locale":"en"},"10390":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-81","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`route` is one of: `direct`, `configured_proxy`, `environment_