_denied`","locale":"en"},"10429":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-120","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Permission denied","locale":"en"},"10430":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-121","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"HTTP 403","locale":"en"},"10431":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-122","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`quota_exhausted`","locale":"en"},"10432":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-123","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Quota exhausted","locale":"en"},"10433":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-124","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"HTTP 402","locale":"en"},"10434":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-125","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`rate_limited`","locale":"en"},"10435":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-126","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Rate limited","locale":"en"},"10436":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-127","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"HTTP 429","locale":"en"},"10437":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-128","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`upstream_error`","locale":"en"},"10438":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-129","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Upstream service error","locale":"en"},"10439":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-130","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"Any other error status","locale":"en"},"10440":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-131","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#network-diagnostics","content":"`challenge`, `edge_rejected`, `invalid_response`, `client_restricted`, `region_restricted` and `signature_rejected` are recognised before any token handling: they never invalidate an account's refresh token, rotate accounts or mark a model as gone. A bare HTTP 403 is not treated as an expired token either. When you see one of these, check the route first (another proxy, or direct), the region and the station's status. More steps are in Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"10441":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-132","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#provider-concurrency-and-waiting","content":"Inference requests share a concurrency limit per provider instance: two by default, one for Zcode. A stream holds its slot until it finishes or closes. Configure `providers.<id>.options.admission` to change the limit, minimum dispatch interval, or maximum queue wait:","locale":"en"},"10442":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-133","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#provider-concurrency-and-waiting","content":"`max_concurrency` must be a positive integer; the other values are finite, nonnegative seconds. Server-declared waits are preserved: a wait longer than the request's retry budget returns an error with `Retry-After` instead of sending an early retry. These limits are in memory per instance; separate processes do not share them.","locale":"en"},"10443":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-134","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#provider-concurrency-and-waiting","content":"OpenCode free limits and Cline daily model limits hold the account/model pair. Zcode concurrency errors and Qoder queue responses wait without invalidating credentials. Account-wide quota errors still hold the whole account. When no reset time is supplied for an exhausted quota, the conservative fallback is one hour.","locale":"en"},"10444":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-135","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Within one gateway, chat, native Messages and availability probes share provider capacity; probes also share account quota holds. Reconfiguring a provider preserves occupied slots. Lower limits take effect as existing streams finish. Cancelling a queued native Messages request prevents dispatch. Changing accounts or credentials clears account-specific temporary waits while retaining provider and model waits.","locale":"en"},"10445":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-136","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Waits can affect a provider, account, model, or account/model pair. Quotas are checked again after admission. Native Messages preserves original HTTP 200 and SSE business-error responses while recording limits for subsequent requests.","locale":"en"},"10446":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-137","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Provider","locale":"en"},"10447":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-138","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Handling","locale":"en"},"10448":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-139","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"MiniMax Agent / API","locale":"en"},"10449":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-140","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Temporary limits such as `1002`, `1039`, `1041`; account quotas such as `1008`, `2056`; authentication errors `1004`, `2049`. Supports `base_resp.status_code`; unknown nonzero values remain errors","locale":"en"},"10450":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-141","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Zhipu / Z.AI","locale":"en"},"10451":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-142","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Separates rate limits (`1302`, `1305`), quotas (`1113`, `1308`, `1310` and related codes), expired credentials (`1003`), and context overflow (`1261`). Plan permissions and fair-use restrictions are not retried automatically","locale":"en"},"10452":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-143","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"TRAE","locale":"en"},"10453":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-144","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"`4008` exhausted credits; `1005` with plan wording indicates plan allowance; `4011` is temporary throttling","locale":"en"},"10454":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-145","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"LobsterAI / Loomy / Raccoon","locale":"en"},"10455":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-146","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Recognizes insufficient credits/balance and business code `402`; LobsterAI `40100` / `40101` enter credential recovery","locale":"en"},"10456":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-147","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"ZCode","locale":"en"},"10457":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-148","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"`1002` rejects credentials; `3007` verification failures and `3012` risk rejections return without automatic retries","locale":"en"},"10458":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-149","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Qoder","locale":"en"},"10459":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-150","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"`105` authentication, `110` quota. Queue waits use the longer delay when both header and body specify one","locale":"en"},"10460":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-151","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Standard compatible error types such as `rate_limit_error`, `insufficient_quota` and `overloaded_error` also use shared recovery. An untyped HTTP 429 is temporary throttling unless the response explicitly reports an exhausted quota.","locale":"en"},"10461":{"id":"/en/docs/config-network-152","page_id":"/en/docs/config-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-network#shared-capacity-and-business-errors","content":"Mappings follow the MiniMax error reference, Z.AI error reference, and the local dsh-our-free-model reference. These are local recovery policies, not confirmation of live upstream availability.","locale":"en"},"10462":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"page","content":"Data directory and migration","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Configuration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths","locale":"en"},"10463":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-0","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths","content":"Where Hoshimi keeps its configuration, database and other files, what each holds and for how long, where the logs go, and how to back up, reset and migrate from older versions.","locale":"en"},"10464":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-1","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"Where the data directory is","locale":"en"},"10465":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-2","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#what-is-in-it","content":"What is in it","locale":"en"},"10466":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-3","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#the-database-hoshimidb","content":"The database, hoshimi.db","locale":"en"},"10467":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-4","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#schema-upgrades","content":"Schema upgrades","locale":"en"},"10468":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-5","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#logs","content":"Logs","locale":"en"},"10469":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-6","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#migrating-from-older-versions","content":"Migrating from older versions","locale":"en"},"10470":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-7","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#move-the-configuration-file","content":"Move the configuration file","locale":"en"},"10471":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-8","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#let-the-old-json-records-import-themselves","content":"Let the old JSON records import themselves","locale":"en"},"10472":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-9","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#check","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"10473":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-10","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/config-paths#backing-up-and-resetting","content":"Backing up and resetting","locale":"en"},"10474":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-11","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths","content":"All of Hoshimi's state lives in one data directory: the configuration file, the database that records usage and conversations, and a few files meant for people or other programs to read. Moving, backing up or resetting Hoshimi means dealing with this one folder.","locale":"en"},"10475":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-12","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"System","locale":"en"},"10476":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-13","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"Default location","locale":"en"},"10477":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-14","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"10478":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-15","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"`~/.local/share/hoshimi`, or `$XDG_DATA_HOME/hoshimi` when `XDG_DATA_HOME` is set","locale":"en"},"10479":{"id":"/en/docs/config-paths-16","page_id":"/en/docs/config-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config-paths#where-the-data-directory-is","content":"