e-command-line","content":"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL.","locale":"en"},"10937":{"id":"/en/docs/config-294","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"`show` and `get` print access keys, account credentials and proxy URLs as `***`. `get` reads what the file actually contains, and a key missing from the file gives `Unknown setting`.","locale":"en"},"10938":{"id":"/en/docs/config-295","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#reading-and-changing-it-from-the-command-line","content":"Restart the server afterwards. The full command reference is in Commands.","locale":"en"},"10939":{"id":"/en/docs/config-296","page_id":"/en/docs/config","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/config#how-the-file-is-written","content":"Each save writes a temporary file in the same folder and then replaces `config.json` atomically, so a half-written file never appears. The file holds refresh tokens in plain text, so after each save its permissions are restricted to the owner (`0600`) where the file system supports that; Windows and some network mounts do not. Treat it as a credential store and do not share a filled-in copy.","locale":"en"},"10940":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","locale":"en"},"10941":{"id":"/en/docs/development-architecture-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-architecture","content":"The core / api / cli / webui layers and the layering rule, how Services is assembled and updated whil