pe":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"The shared component library, exported from `ui/index.ts`; also `layers.ts` and `motion/`","locale":"en"},"11868":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-65","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`src/api/`","locale":"en"},"11869":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-66","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`client.ts` (the openapi-fetch client), `baseUrl.ts`, `sse.ts`, the generated `schema.d.ts`, `types.ts`, `queries/`","locale":"en"},"11870":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-67","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`src/stores/`","locale":"en"},"11871":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-68","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`auth` (the access key), `preferences` (theme, language, motion), `live` (live calls), `chat` (the Playground)","locale":"en"},"11872":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-69","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`src/i18n/`","locale":"en"},"11873":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-70","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`en.ts`, `zh-CN.ts`, `ja.ts` and `index.ts`","locale":"en"},"11874":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-71","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`src/theme/`","locale":"en"},"11875":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-72","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`scheme.ts`, `applyTheme.ts`, `tokens.css`, `scrollbars.ts`, `breakpoints.ts`","locale":"en"},"11876":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-73","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"`src/test/`","locale":"en"},"11877":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-74","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"The test environment: `setup.ts` (gives happy-dom an `ElementInternals`), `motion-zero.css` (every motion duration at zero)","locale":"en"},"11878":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-75","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#source-layout","content":"Modules always import each other through the `@/` alias (`@/` is `src/`), never by a relative path.","locale":"en"},"11879":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-76","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#deployment-root-and-routing","content":"No API address is compiled into the interface:","locale":"en"},"11880":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-77","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#deployment-root-and-routing","content":"Vite's `base` is `./`, so assets use relative paths and the same build works at the root or under a reverse proxy's sub-path.","locale":"en"},"11881":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-78","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#deployment-root-and-routing","content":"`src/api/baseUrl.ts` derives the deployment root from the URL of the running script: the script is under `<root>/assets/`, so the root is everything before `/assets/`. When the server uses `api_prefix` or sits behind a reverse proxy, the interface needs no change.","locale":"en"},"11882":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-79","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#deployment-root-and-routing","content":"Routing uses hash mode (`#/overview`) and needs no server-side rewrites. `/channels/:id` keeps the chosen channel in the address, so a reload or the back gesture returns to it.","locale":"en"},"11883":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-80","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"The interface's TypeScript types come from the server's OpenAPI document. After changing a management API request or response model, regenerate and commit:","locale":"en"},"11884":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-81","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"It writes the output of `scripts/generate_openapi.py` to a temporary `hoshimi/webui/openapi.json`, runs `bun x openapi-typescript` to produce `src/api/schema.d.ts`, then deletes the temporary file. The same by hand:","locale":"en"},"11885":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-82","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"`generate_openapi.py` builds the app with empty settings and a throwaway data folder, so the document describes shapes only, not this machine's configuration.","locale":"en"},"11886":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-83","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"`openapi.json` is excluded by `.gitignore`; `schema.d.ts` is committed.","locale":"en"},"11887":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-84","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"`python scripts/dev.py typegen-check` regenerates and then runs `git diff --exit-code`; CI uses it to fail when the types are stale.","locale":"en"},"11888":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-85","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#the-contract-with-the-server-generated-types","content":"Code refers to these types through the aliases in `src/api/types.ts` (`S['SettingsView']` and so on), sends requests with the `api` client (openapi-fetch) exported by `client.ts`, and uses `unwrap()` to turn a failure into an `ApiError` carrying the server's message.","locale":"en"},"11889":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-86","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-fetching","content":"**Authentication**: the `api` middleware adds `Authorization: Bearer <access key>` to every request. The key is kept in the browser's `localStorage` (`hoshimi:access-token`); when the server answers 401 with `auth_required`, the interface opens the access-key dialog.","locale":"en"},"11890":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-87","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-fetching","content":"**Queries**: `src/api/queries/` wraps Vue Query per area, with the query keys collected in `queries/keys.ts`, hierarchically, so invalidating a prefix invalidates every key under it. A 4xx `ApiError` is not retried, other failures at most twice; a window regaining focus does not refetch.","locale":"en"},"11891":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-88","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#data-fetching","content":"**Live data**: `stores/live.ts` keeps the one connection to `GET /api/v1/stats/live`, which drives the top bar's live-calls sheet, the **Usage** page and the **Overview** card. It is read with `fetch` (`api/sse.ts`), because `EventSource` cannot send the access key as a header. REST stays the source of truth: a finished call invalidates the usage and channel queries, which refetch; after a drop it reconnects at 1, 2, 4, 8, 15 and 30 second intervals and starts from a fresh snapshot.","locale":"en"},"11892":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-89","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#i18n","content":"The interface text lives in three files in `src/i18n/`: `en.ts` is the source, `zh-CN.ts` and `ja.ts` are the translations. In a component:","locale":"en"},"11893":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-90","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#i18n","content":"`t(key, params)` looks in the current language, then English, then returns the key itself; `{name}` placeholders are filled from `params`.","locale":"en"},"11894":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-91","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#i18n","content":"The language preference defaults to `auto`, which follows the browser's first language (`zh*` is Simplified Chinese, `ja*` Japanese, anything else English) and updates when the system language changes.","locale":"en"},"11895":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#i18n","content":"`src/i18n/i18n.test.ts` requires the three files to have exactly the same keys and every message the same placeholders. A new string goes into all three files.","locale":"en"},"11896":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-design-tokens","content":"**Colour**: every colour role is generated from one seed colour (`theme/scheme.ts`, `#5267d8` by default, which users can change) with Material's Tonal Spot scheme, at standard, medium or high contrast. `theme/applyTheme.ts` writes them as `--md-sys-color-*` on `:root` and follows the system's light or dark setting.","locale":"en"},"11897":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-design-tokens","content":"**Static tokens**: type, shape, elevation, motion durations and easing, state layers and the rest are in `theme/tokens.css`, named `--md-sys-*` and `--app-*`.","locale":"en"},"11898":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-95","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-design-tokens","content":"**The rule**: components use tokens only, never a literal colour, radius or duration. `src/tokens.test.ts` checks that no `.vue` or `.css` file outside `src/theme/` contains a hex colour.","locale":"en"},"11899":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-96","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#theme-and-design-tokens","content":"**Charts**: series take the eight colour-blind-checked slots `--app-chart-1` to `--app-chart-8` in a fixed order; charts carry a legend and a hover / focus tooltip.","locale":"en"},"11900":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-97","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#components-layers-and-motion","content":"**Shared components**: pages and composites take shared components from `@/ui` and do not restyle them (the convention stated in `ui/index.ts`). A page is a `Toolbar` row over one column of `PageSection`s, and adapts to the content area's width (`@container app-content`). A list that can grow without bound sits in a `ScrollArea` or a `DataTable` (sortable, rendering only what is in view past 200 rows). Channels is a `ListDetail` layout.","locale":"en"},"11901":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-98","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#components-layers-and-motion","content":"**Choices**: one choice out of a few (a list filter, a report range) is a `SegmentedControl`, which becomes a select where it does not fit; days are picked with `DatePicker`.","locale":"en"},"11902":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-99","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#components-layers-and-motion","content":"**Replies**: `ui/Markdown.vue` renders a reply block by block (only the block being written changes as it streams, so a drawn diagram or an open preview above it stays). Model text is untrusted: raw HTML stays text; math goes through KaTeX without `trust`; Mermaid draws in `strict` mode, loaded on first use (`ui/mermaid.ts`) and kept by source and theme; an `html` block previews only on request, in an `iframe` with `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` and a CSP that keeps it off the network; media on another site waits for a press unless the browser preference says otherwise (`ui/markdownRich.ts`). Any element marked `data-view` opens in `ImageViewer` through `useImageViewer`.","locale":"en"},"11903":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-100","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#components-layers-and-motion","content":"**Layers**: everything that opens over the page (dialogs, sheets, menus, an open picker) stacks through `ui/layers.ts`: what opened later paints above; Esc and an outside click close the topmost layer alone; while a modal layer is open, the page and every layer under it are `inert`; a closing layer gives focus back to what opened it.","locale":"en"},"11904":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-101","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#components-layers-and-motion","content":"**Motion**: navigation fades through with View Transitions; tabs and filters slide along a shared horizontal axis (`AxisPanes`); a list-detail pane moves vertically between items (`shared-axis-y`); one view replacing another fades through (`FadeSwap`), as one Playground chat replacing another does; moving to another version of a Playground turn slides that turn and what follows it along the horizontal axis (`components/chat/VersionPanes.vue`, over `AxisPanes`), keeping what is above in place; a control that comes and goes in a row (the composer's effort and approval chips, the context ring) opens and closes its width with the gap beside it (`chip-row`, `chipRowHooks`), so the others slide and a long model name narrows rather than jumping, and a chip whose words change eases to its new width (`useMorphWidth`); list items use the `list` motion. **Settings › Appearance › Motion** (or the system's reduced-motion setting) turns every transition into a short fade.","locale":"en"},"11905":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-102","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"`src/layout.test.ts` writes these rules as tests; breaking any of them fails `bun run test`:","locale":"en"},"11906":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-103","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"11907":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-104","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Why","locale":"en"},"11908":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-105","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"In a row pairing a name with a control, the text element has `min-width: 0` (the test lists the components and selectors)","locale":"en"},"11909":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-106","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"A model ID is often one long unbreakable word; without it, the buttons are pushed out of view","locale":"en"},"11910":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-107","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"The Models and Usage lists use `DataTable`; the channel details' account list uses `ScrollArea`","locale":"en"},"11911":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-108","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"A list that can grow without bound scrolls inside itself instead of stretching the page into an endless column","locale":"en"},"11912":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-109","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"No component style sets a scrolling `overflow: auto` / `scroll`, nor `scrollbar-width`, `scrollbar-color` or `scrollbar-gutter` (except `ui/NavigationRail.vue`, which hides its scrollbar on purpose)","locale":"en"},"11913":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-110","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Every scrolling area scrolls through `.app-scroll`; see below","locale":"en"},"11914":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-111","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"`.app-scroll` scrolls down and clips sideways; `.app-scroll.app-scroll-x` scrolls sideways, never down, and passes vertical swipes on","locale":"en"},"11915":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-112","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"An area scrolls in one direction","locale":"en"},"11916":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-113","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Markdown's code blocks, tables, display math and diagrams, and the `Stepper`, scroll sideways on their own (`app-scroll app-scroll-x`)","locale":"en"},"11917":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-114","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Content that is wider than its column on purpose","locale":"en"},"11918":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-115","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"`tokens.css` has no rule aimed at the children of `.app-scroll`","locale":"en"},"11919":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-116","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Such a rule overrides the components' own margins, and a page, a menu item and the Playground's column overflowed one after another","locale":"en"},"11920":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-117","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Components in `ui/` declare no `transition` on their root element (`AppCard` and `StackedBarChart` excepted)","locale":"en"},"11921":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-118","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"A pane switch moves the root through the motion system, and the component's own `transition` would replace it","locale":"en"},"11922":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-119","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Every page's root, the `.body` of `AppDialog` and `SideSheet`, and `DataTable`'s `.row` use `var(--app-scroll-lane)` in `padding-inline-end`","locale":"en"},"11923":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-120","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"The scrollbar lane is on the end side only, so the end padding takes it out and content sits evenly between both sides","locale":"en"},"11924":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-121","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"The Playground route has `meta: { fill: true }`, the shell then keeps no lane, and its `.thread` reaches into the padding with a negative `margin-inline-end`; `ListDetail`'s detail pane does the same","locale":"en"},"11925":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-122","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"A page that fills the frame scrolls inside itself","locale":"en"},"11926":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-123","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Bottom-bar destinations have `min-width: 0`, and the indicator `max-width: 64px` rather than a fixed `width: 64px`","locale":"en"},"11927":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-124","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Six 64px destinations are wider than a small phone","locale":"en"},"11928":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-125","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"No SVG with a `viewBox` uses `preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"`","locale":"en"},"11929":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-126","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#layout-rules","content":"Charts are drawn at their own size; a stretched one turns round points into ovals","locale":"en"},"11930":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-127","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"`.app-scroll` in `theme/tokens.css` gives an area's scrollbar a lane of its own beside the content rather than over it:","locale":"en"},"11931":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-128","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"Chromium and WebKit use a styled scrollbar that takes layout space even where the system draws overlay scrollbars (macOS, Windows 11, GTK). These engines ignore `::-webkit-scrollbar` once `scrollbar-width` or `scrollbar-color` is set, so neither is set anywhere.","locale":"en"},"11932":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-129","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"Firefox gets a thin scrollbar in the theme's colours; where Firefox's scrollbars float, `applyScrollbars()` in `theme/scrollbars.ts` sets `data-scrollbars` to `overlay` and the lane to 0.","locale":"en"},"11933":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-130","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"The scrollbar's place is kept while nothing overflows (`scrollbar-gutter: stable`), so content does not shift when a scrollbar appears; menus and pickers give it up with `app-scroll-auto`.","locale":"en"},"11934":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-131","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"`--app-scroll-lane` is the width the lane actually takes (measured at startup); `--app-scroll-head` starts the vertical track below a sticky header, and `--app-scroll-inset` keeps the thumb clear of rounded corners.","locale":"en"},"11935":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-132","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#app-scroll","content":"The unit tests read the source; sideways overflow in real browsers is checked by `scripts/check_layout.py`, see Testing.","locale":"en"},"11936":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-133","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#write-the-view","content":"Add a `<Name>View.vue` in `src/views/`. Its root class takes `var(--app-scroll-lane)` out of its `padding-inline-end`; the page is built from `Toolbar` and `PageSection`, with components from `@/ui`.","locale":"en"},"11937":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-134","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#add-the-route-and-the-navigation","content":"Add a lazily loaded route in `src/router.ts`, and a destination in `src/App.vue`, with an icon from the `icons` that `@/ui` exports.","locale":"en"},"11938":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-135","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#add-the-text","content":"Add `nav.<name>` and every key the page uses to `en.ts`, `zh-CN.ts` and `ja.ts`.","locale":"en"},"11939":{"id":"/en/docs/development-webui-136","page_id":"/en/docs/development-webui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-webui#check","content":"Run `python scripts/dev.py test-web`; add the new page's path to `PAGES` in `scripts/check_layout.py` and check it in real browsers; if the page uses a new API, run `typegen` first. Finally, give it a page in the Web UI guides, in both languages.","locale":"en"},"11940":{"id":"/en/docs/development","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"page","content":"Development","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development","locale":"en"},"11941":{"id":"/en/docs/development-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development","content":"The way in for contributors: what Hoshimi is made of, what is authoritative, the conventions that apply everywhere, and what each development page covers.","locale":"en"},"11942":{"id":"/en/docs/development-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#what-is-authoritative","content":"What is authoritative","locale":"en"},"11943":{"id":"/en/docs/development-2","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"One distribution, four layers","locale":"en"},"11944":{"id":"/en/docs/development-3","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"Pages","locale":"en"},"11945":{"id":"/en/docs/development-4","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"Conventions that apply everywhere","locale":"en"},"11946":{"id":"/en/docs/development-5","page_id":"/en/docs/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Reference projects","locale":"en"},"11947":{"id":"/en/docs/development-6","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development","content":"This section is for people who want to change Hoshimi: fix a bug, add a provider, add a page to the Web UI, change an API route, or maintain this documentation site. It describes what the code **is** today, the rules it keeps and why, not how to use it (for that, see the Web UI guides, the command line and the API reference).","locale":"en"},"11948":{"id":"/en/docs/development-7","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#what-is-authoritative","content":"**The code and its tests**: when anything else disagrees with them, they win. Many rules are tests themselves (the layering rule, the Web UI's layout and colour rules, matching i18n keys), so a change that breaks one does not pass CI.","locale":"en"},"11949":{"id":"/en/docs/development-8","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#what-is-authoritative","content":"**This site**: it replaces the repository's old `docs/` folder and is Hoshimi's only documentation. A change users can see (a command, an option, a config key, an endpoint, the interface) updates the matching pages, in Chinese and in English; see Documentation site.","locale":"en"},"11950":{"id":"/en/docs/development-9","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#what-is-authoritative","content":"**Reference projects**: protocols and behaviour come from local clones of a few outside repositories. They are excluded by `.gitignore` and are not runtime dependencies; see Reference projects below.","locale":"en"},"11951":{"id":"/en/docs/development-10","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Hoshimi is one Python distribution, `hoshimi`; the built Web UI (`hoshimi/webui/dist/`) ships inside the wheel. The package has four layers:","locale":"en"},"11952":{"id":"/en/docs/development-11","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Folder","locale":"en"},"11953":{"id":"/en/docs/development-12","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"11954":{"id":"/en/docs/development-13","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Frameworks","locale":"en"},"11955":{"id":"/en/docs/development-14","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"`hoshimi/core/`","locale":"en"},"11956":{"id":"/en/docs/development-15","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"All logic: configuration, credentials, provider adapters, routing, protocol translation, usage accounting, login flows, the Playground's tools","locale":"en"},"11957":{"id":"/en/docs/development-16","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Imports no web or command-line framework; reaches upstreams with httpx only","locale":"en"},"11958":{"id":"/en/docs/development-17","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"`hoshimi/api/`","locale":"en"},"11959":{"id":"/en/docs/development-18","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"The FastAPI app: middleware, routes (the `/v1` model API and the `/api/v1` management API), the Web UI's static files","locale":"en"},"11960":{"id":"/en/docs/development-19","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"FastAPI, Starlette","locale":"en"},"11961":{"id":"/en/docs/development-20","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"`hoshimi/cli/`","locale":"en"},"11962":{"id":"/en/docs/development-21","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Typer commands: `serve`, `check`, `models`, `providers`, `stations`, `login`, `version`, `env`, `config`","locale":"en"},"11963":{"id":"/en/docs/development-22","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Typer, Rich","locale":"en"},"11964":{"id":"/en/docs/development-23","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"`hoshimi/webui/`","locale":"en"},"11965":{"id":"/en/docs/development-24","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"The Vue 3 + Vite interface; `dist/` ships in the package","locale":"en"},"11966":{"id":"/en/docs/development-25","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"Built with Bun, not a Python dependency","locale":"en"},"11967":{"id":"/en/docs/development-26","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#one-distribution-four-layers","content":"The API and the command line start from the same place: `hoshimi.core.context.build_services()` builds every service once into a `Services`. `core` does not know who calls it: `tests/core/test_architecture.py` makes sure it imports none of FastAPI, Starlette, Typer, Click, Uvicorn or Rich, and never refers to `hoshimi.api` or `hoshimi.cli`. Architecture starts from that rule.","locale":"en"},"11968":{"id":"/en/docs/development-27","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Development setup\" href=\"/docs/development-setup\" description=\"The repository layout, the Python environment, bun, every scripts/dev.py task, and the dev mode that runs the API and Vite together.\" />","locale":"en"},"11969":{"id":"/en/docs/development-28","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Architecture\" href=\"/docs/development-architecture\" description=\"The core / api / cli / webui layers, how Services is assembled, the app factory, error mapping, and one request end to end.\" />","locale":"en"},"11970":{"id":"/en/docs/development-29","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Provider adapters\" href=\"/docs/development-providers\" description=\"The Provider contract, the normalized chunk protocol, errors and account rotation, catalogues and capabilities, and login flows.\" />","locale":"en"},"11971":{"id":"/en/docs/development-30","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Web UI\" href=\"/docs/development-webui\" description=\"How the Vue app is laid out, types generated from OpenAPI, i18n, theme and tokens, layers and motion, and the layout rules.\" />","locale":"en"},"11972":{"id":"/en/docs/development-31","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Testing\" href=\"/docs/development-testing\" description=\"The pytest layout and shared fixtures, the Vitest rule tests, the generated-type check, and check_layout.py for sideways overflow in real browsers.\" />","locale":"en"},"11973":{"id":"/en/docs/development-32","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"CI and releases\" href=\"/docs/development-release\" description=\"The CI workflows, the version, building and checking the wheel, publishing to PyPI and GitHub, and deploying the docs site.\" />","locale":"en"},"11974":{"id":"/en/docs/development-33","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#pages","content":"<Card title=\"Documentation site\" href=\"/docs/development-site\" description=\"How this site is organised, writing pages, previewing and building, deployment, analytics and comments.\" />","locale":"en"},"11975":{"id":"/en/docs/development-34","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"**Python**","locale":"en"},"11976":{"id":"/en/docs/development-35","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"Python 3.10 and newer; CI type-checks 3.10–3.14 on Linux, Windows and macOS and runs the tests on 3.10, 3.12 and 3.14.","locale":"en"},"11977":{"id":"/en/docs/development-36","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"Ruff lints and formats, with a line length of 180; only absolute imports are allowed (`ban-relative-imports = \"all\"`).","locale":"en"},"11978":{"id":"/en/docs/development-37","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"ty checks types, targeting Python 3.10; in CI a warning fails the check.","locale":"en"},"11979":{"id":"/en/docs/development-38","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"`import hoshimi` loads neither FastAPI nor httpx: the package's public names (`VERSION`, `Services`, `build_services`, `create_app`) are exported lazily, and `tests/test_package_api.py` checks it.","locale":"en"},"11980":{"id":"/en/docs/development-39","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"**Web UI**","locale":"en"},"11981":{"id":"/en/docs/development-40","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"Modules import each other through the `@/` alias, never by a relative path; no hex colours outside `src/theme/`; every scrolling area uses `.app-scroll`. All of these are tested; see Web UI.","locale":"en"},"11982":{"id":"/en/docs/development-41","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"The interface text exists in English, Simplified Chinese and Japanese, with the same keys and placeholders.","locale":"en"},"11983":{"id":"/en/docs/development-42","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"**The API contract**","locale":"en"},"11984":{"id":"/en/docs/development-43","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"The Web UI's TypeScript types are generated from the server's OpenAPI document (`src/api/schema.d.ts`) and committed; CI regenerates them and fails on a difference. A change to a management API model means running `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and committing the result.","locale":"en"},"11985":{"id":"/en/docs/development-44","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"**Documentation**","locale":"en"},"11986":{"id":"/en/docs/development-45","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#conventions-that-apply-everywhere","content":"A change users can see updates this site's pages in the same commit, in both languages.","locale":"en"},"11987":{"id":"/en/docs/development-46","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"These repositories sit as local clones in the repository root, to compare protocols and behaviour against. They are all in `.gitignore`: they never enter this repository and Hoshimi does not depend on them.","locale":"en"},"11988":{"id":"/en/docs/development-47","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Clone","locale":"en"},"11989":{"id":"/en/docs/development-48","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Used for","locale":"en"},"11990":{"id":"/en/docs/development-49","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"`codex-api`","locale":"en"},"11991":{"id":"/en/docs/development-50","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Reference for the server and its security","locale":"en"},"11992":{"id":"/en/docs/development-51","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"`dsh-our-free-model`","locale":"en"},"11993":{"id":"/en/docs/development-52","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Protocol reference for the free stations; the bundled EAC relay seal is ported from it (MIT)","locale":"en"},"11994":{"id":"/en/docs/development-53","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"`Hanaikada`","locale":"en"},"11995":{"id":"/en/docs/development-54","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"The layered Python + Vue skeleton Hoshimi follows; `scripts/dev.py` comes from it too","locale":"en"},"11996":{"id":"/en/docs/development-55","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"`pi`, `pi-free`, `free-claude-code`","locale":"en"},"11997":{"id":"/en/docs/development-56","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Sources of the provider definitions; the Provider inventory records their snapshots","locale":"en"},"11998":{"id":"/en/docs/development-57","page_id":"/en/docs/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development#reference-projects","content":"Development, tests and builds work without these clones: the tests never read them (`tests/core/test_provider_definitions.py` deliberately does not depend on reference checkouts).","locale":"en"},"11999":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"page","content":"First run","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run","locale":"en"},"12000":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-0","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run","content":"What you see after starting Hoshimi for the first time: what appears in the data folder, the layout of the interface, signing in when an access key is set, the two anonymous channels that are on by default, and where everything is.","locale":"en"},"12001":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-1","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#what-happens-at-start","content":"What happens at start","locale":"en"},"12002":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-2","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"Layout","locale":"en"},"12003":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-3","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Signing in (when a tool access key is set)","locale":"en"},"12004":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-4","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"The two default anonymous channels","locale":"en"},"12005":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-5","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"The pages","locale":"en"},"12006":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-6","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#where-things-are","content":"Where things are","locale":"en"},"12007":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-7","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/first-run#next-steps","content":"Next steps","locale":"en"},"12008":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-8","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run","content":"This page walks through the interface after the first start. If Hoshimi is not installed yet, begin with the Quick start.","locale":"en"},"12009":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-9","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#what-happens-at-start","content":"**No configuration file is needed.** Without `config.json`, Hoshimi uses every default: it listens on `127.0.0.1:10600`, sets no key, and enables only the two anonymous channels. `config.json` is created the first time you save a setting, add an account or run `hoshimi config set`.","locale":"en"},"12010":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-10","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#what-happens-at-start","content":"**The data folder.** The server creates `hoshimi.db` (usage, check-in records, probe verdicts and Playground conversations) and `server.json` (the running server's address and PID) in the data folder. Where that folder is, is covered in Data folder; it is also shown under **Settings › About**.","locale":"en"},"12011":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-11","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#what-happens-at-start","content":"**Background timers.** Credential renewal (every 30 minutes) and daily check-in start with the server, each with a line in the log. The server also asks PyPI in the background whether a newer release exists. All three can be turned off, see Configuration.","locale":"en"},"12012":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-12","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#what-happens-at-start","content":"**The browser.** About a second later the browser opens `http://127.0.0.1:10600`, and the address becomes `http://127.0.0.1:10600/#/overview`. Page addresses all live after the `#` and can be bookmarked, such as `#/playground` or `#/settings?tab=access`.","locale":"en"},"12013":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-13","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"Where","locale":"en"},"12014":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-14","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"What","locale":"en"},"12015":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-15","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"Navigation rail on the left","locale":"en"},"12016":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-16","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"**Overview**, **Models**, **Channels**, **Usage**, **Playground**; **Settings** sits at the foot of the rail. In a narrow window the rail becomes a bar at the bottom. When channels need attention, **Channels** carries a count badge","locale":"en"},"12017":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-17","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"Top right","locale":"en"},"12018":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-18","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"The **Live activity** button: shows how many calls are running, and opens today's tokens, calls and cache hit rate with the calls running now and just finished. Next to it, the theme button cycles **Light**, **Dark** and **System**","locale":"en"},"12019":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-19","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#layout","content":"The interface language follows the system (English, Simplified Chinese and Japanese are available); pin one under **Settings › General › Language**. Theme, colour, contrast and motion are under **Settings › Appearance**. These preferences are kept in this browser only, not on the server.","locale":"en"},"12020":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-20","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"By default there is no key and the interface opens straight away. The foot of the **Endpoints** section on the **Overview** page then says **No tool access key is set.**","locale":"en"},"12021":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-21","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Once a tool access key (`server.access_token`) is set, a browser's first visit shows the **Tool access key required** dialog:","locale":"en"},"12022":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-22","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Enter the key in **Tool access key**.","locale":"en"},"12023":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-23","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Click **Sign in** (or press Enter). A wrong key shows **The tool access key is incorrect.**, and a previously saved key is kept.","locale":"en"},"12024":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-24","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Once accepted, the key is saved in this browser's localStorage and not asked for again; another browser or device must sign in itself. When you change or clear the key under **Settings › Access › Keys**, the current browser updates on its own and other browsers must sign in again.","locale":"en"},"12025":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-25","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Three ways to set the key:","locale":"en"},"12026":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-26","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"Or save it under **Settings › Access › Keys › Tool access key**, which applies at once.","locale":"en"},"12027":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-27","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"The tool access key protects the Web UI and the management API (`/api/v1/*`, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`); the model API `/v1/*` is protected by a separate, independent **Model API key**. The Playground goes through the management API, so it needs only the tool access key. The two keys and LAN access are covered in Security.","locale":"en"},"12028":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-28","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#signing-in-when-a-tool-access-key-is-set","content":"The **API reference** button on **Overview** and under **Settings › About** appears only while no tool access key is set: `/docs` is a plain page and cannot send the key saved in the browser. With a key set, fetch `/openapi.json` with `Authorization: Bearer <tool-access-key>`, see API reference.","locale":"en"},"12029":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-29","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"With no configuration at all, Hoshimi enables two channels that need no account:","locale":"en"},"12030":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-30","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"12031":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-31","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"ID","locale":"en"},"12032":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-32","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"What it is","locale":"en"},"12033":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-33","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"OpenCode Zen","locale":"en"},"12034":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-34","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"`opencode`","locale":"en"},"12035":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-35","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"OpenCode's anonymous free entry point","locale":"en"},"12036":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-36","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"Kilo AI","locale":"en"},"12037":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-37","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"`kilo`","locale":"en"},"12038":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-38","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"Kilo's anonymous free entry point","locale":"en"},"12039":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-39","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"On **Overview** and **Channels** they show as **Ready**, with **No account needed** where the account count would be; a channel's page says **This channel works without an account; add one for a larger allowance.** Which models they offer, and how much, depends on the upstream catalogue and service state at the time and can change without notice; adding an account of your own can also change the catalogue the upstream returns.","locale":"en"},"12040":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-40","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"To confirm from the command line:","locale":"en"},"12041":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-41","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"If you do not want them, switch off **Enabled** on the channel's page, or:","locale":"en"},"12042":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-42","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-two-default-anonymous-channels","content":"(Command-line changes apply after the server restarts.) The two anonymous lanes are covered in Anonymous channels.","locale":"en"},"12043":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-43","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Page","locale":"en"},"12044":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-44","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"What you see the first time","locale":"en"},"12045":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-45","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Guide","locale":"en"},"12046":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-46","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Overview**","locale":"en"},"12047":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-47","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Today** (tokens, calls, cache hit, running now, and a 24-hour trend); **Endpoints** (the base URL and each endpoint, with copy buttons); **Channels** (the channels that are set up, with their status); **Server** (version, latest version, default model)","locale":"en"},"12048":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-48","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Overview","locale":"en"},"12049":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-49","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Models**","locale":"en"},"12050":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-50","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"The catalogue of the two anonymous channels. It loads channel by channel (**Loading providers: n/m**); search it, filter by **Provider** and **Availability**, and use **Probe** to check which models answer right now; each row can **Copy the model id** or **Open in the Playground**","locale":"en"},"12051":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-51","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Models","locale":"en"},"12052":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-52","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Channels**","locale":"en"},"12053":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-53","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Every station and service you can connect. The filter above switches between **All**, **In use**, **Needs attention**, **Not set up** and **Off**; choose a channel and its accounts, today's usage, allowance and network settings open beside the list, with a **Sign in** or **Add account** button","locale":"en"},"12054":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-54","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Channels","locale":"en"},"12055":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-55","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Usage**","locale":"en"},"12056":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-56","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Until a request has gone through the gateway it says **Nothing has been served yet**. After that, tokens, cache, latency and every call by 24 hours, 7 days, 30 days, 90 days or a single day","locale":"en"},"12057":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-57","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"Usage","locale":"en"},"12058":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-58","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"**Playground**","locale":"en"},"12059":{"id":"/en/docs/first-run-59","page_id":"/en/docs/first-run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/first-run#the-pages","content":"An empty chat (**What can I help wi