ge_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Tool cards","locale":"en"},"12108":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"Steer a reply while it works","locale":"en"},"12109":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-above-the-composer","content":"Background commands above the composer","locale":"en"},"12110":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#workspace","content":"Workspace","locale":"en"},"12111":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#stopping","content":"Stopping","locale":"en"},"12112":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"Safety","locale":"en"},"12113":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"Settings reference","locale":"en"},"12114":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent","content":"With tools on, a Playground reply becomes an agent loop. The model is offered built-in tools; each round it streams its words, the tools it called run one after another (once the ones that need it are approved, by the review model or by you), their results go back to it, and it goes on until a round calls nothing. The reply shows every call as a card you can open.","locale":"en"},"12115":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent","content":"Commands and file edits run on the machine that runs Hoshimi, with the permissions of the user running it. There is no sandbox. All tools are on by default, and new chats start in **Automatic review**: a model judges each command, file change and anything outside the workspace before it runs, and denies what's risky. **Ask first** leaves every one to you. The Safety section below says what each mode lets through.","locale":"en"},"12116":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-tools","content":"Open **Settings › Tools**. Under **Tools**, all six are on by default; switch off the ones you don't want (see Settings). These are the tools of every chat: a chat has no switches of its own, and a change applies to every chat from its next reply.","locale":"en"},"12117":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-tools","content":"If your config file never set `playground.tools` or `playground.approval`, it now gets all tools and **Automatic review**. A config that sets `\"tools\": []` keeps none.","locale":"en"},"12118":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#pick-a-model-that-calls-tools","content":"Tools are offered only to models that make tool calls. A model whose catalogue entry says it has no tool calls answers without them, and the reply notes \"*model* can’t call tools, so it answered without them.\" The same happens when a station refuses the tools before the reply starts: the reply is tried once more without them.","locale":"en"},"12119":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Switch (in Settings)","locale":"en"},"12120":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Tool names the model sees","locale":"en"},"12121":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12122":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Asks first (never in Full access)","locale":"en"},"12123":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Read files**","locale":"en"},"12124":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`read`","locale":"en"},"12125":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Read a text file, or list a folder","locale":"en"},"12126":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Only for paths outside the workspace","locale":"en"},"12127":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Edit files**","locale":"en"},"12128":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`apply_patch`","locale":"en"},"12129":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Create, change, move and delete files with a patch","locale":"en"},"12130":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Always in **Automatic review** and **Ask first**; in **Ask outside the workspace**, only for files outside it","locale":"en"},"12131":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Run commands**","locale":"en"},"12132":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`shell`","locale":"en"},"12133":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Run a command and wait for it","locale":"en"},"12134":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Only in **Automatic review** and **Ask first**","locale":"en"},"12135":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Background commands**","locale":"en"},"12136":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`exec_command`, `write_stdin`, `kill_session`","locale":"en"},"12137":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Start a command that keeps running, read its output, type into it, stop it","locale":"en"},"12138":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Starting one, or typing into one, only in **Automatic review** and **Ask first**","locale":"en"},"12139":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Search the web**","locale":"en"},"12140":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`web_search`","locale":"en"},"12141":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Search DuckDuckGo, or your own SearXNG","locale":"en"},"12142":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Never","locale":"en"},"12143":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"**Read web pages**","locale":"en"},"12144":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"`web_fetch`","locale":"en"},"12145":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Read a public web page as Markdown","locale":"en"},"12146":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"Never","locale":"en"},"12147":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-six-tools","content":"In **Automatic review**, a call that asks first goes to the review model, and comes to you only when it can't decide (see Automatic review below). Relative paths are taken from the workspace (see Workspace below). Whatever a tool returns, a model is sent at most 32,000 characters of it; the middle of a longer output is cut, keeping the start and the end.","locale":"en"},"12148":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-files-read","content":"Returns text with numbered lines (`L12: …`). Reads 2000 lines from the start unless the model asks for an `offset` (from 1) and a `limit` (up to 10,000).","locale":"en"},"12149":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-files-read","content":"A line longer than 500 characters is cut; one read returns at most 60,000 characters and says where to go on.","locale":"en"},"12150":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-files-read","content":"A path that is a folder returns its listing: folders first, up to 500 entries.","locale":"en"},"12151":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-files-read","content":"Binary files (with a NUL byte near the start) are refused.","locale":"en"},"12152":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#edit-files-apply_patch","content":"Takes a patch in the Codex `apply_patch` format, so a model that knows the tool from Codex knows it here:","locale":"en"},"12153":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#edit-files-apply_patch","content":"The whole patch is worked out against the files before anything is written: if one hunk does not apply, no file is changed.","locale":"en"},"12154":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#edit-files-apply_patch","content":"Files must be UTF-8 text. Line endings are kept (a CRLF file stays CRLF), and a file always ends with a line ending.","locale":"en"},"12155":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#edit-files-apply_patch","content":"The result lists the files added (`A`), modified (`M`) and deleted (`D`).","locale":"en"},"12156":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#edit-files-apply_patch","content":"A patch that names a file outside the workspace (or moves one there) needs **Edit files** approval for outside files: **Change files outside the workspace?**","locale":"en"},"12157":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#run-commands-shell","content":"Runs the command in the shell the model names, or else in the default shell (see Choose the shell below), in the workspace unless the model gives a `workdir`.","locale":"en"},"12158":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#run-commands-shell","content":"Waits for it to finish: 10 minutes by default; the model can ask for more or less (`timeout_ms`), with no upper limit. A command that runs longer is stopped, with everything it started, and reported as timed out (exit code 124).","locale":"en"},"12159":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#run-commands-shell","content":"Returns the exit code, the time taken and the output, standard error included. The command gets no input (standard input is closed), and pagers and colours are turned off (`PAGER=cat`, `NO_COLOR=1`, `TERM=dumb`, `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`).","locale":"en"},"12160":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#run-commands-shell","content":"For something that keeps running or asks for input, the model is told to use a background command instead.","locale":"en"},"12161":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"`exec_command` starts a command and waits a little (10 seconds by default, from 0.25 to 30; at least 10 on Windows). If it finishes, it returns its exit code and output; if not, it keeps running as a *session* and returns what it printed so far and a session ID.","locale":"en"},"12162":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"`write_stdin` types into a session (with `\\n` for Enter) and returns its new output, waiting 0.25 seconds by default after writing (at most 30); with nothing to type it just waits for new output (from 5 seconds, the default, to 5 minutes). A session itself has no time limit: it runs until it exits or is stopped. It says whether the command still runs, or its exit code.","locale":"en"},"12163":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"`kill_session` stops a session and everything it started, and returns its last output.","locale":"en"},"12164":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"A session keeps up to 1,000,000 characters of unread output (the middle of more is dropped); colour codes are stripped.","locale":"en"},"12165":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"At most 16 background commands run at once on the server. Sessions belong to the chat that started them, and stop when that chat is deleted and when the server stops.","locale":"en"},"12166":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-exec_command-write_stdin-kill_session","content":"`exec_command` asks first like `shell`. `write_stdin` asks too when it types something (**Run this command?**), since typing into a shell runs commands; only reading output never asks. `kill_session` never asks.","locale":"en"},"12167":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"`shell` and `exec_command` take an optional `shell`: `bash`, `zsh`, `sh`, `powershell` (PowerShell 7, `pwsh`, is preferred over Windows PowerShell; `pwsh` is accepted as a name) or `cmd`, by name or by path (such as `/usr/bin/zsh`). A shell that is unknown or not installed is an error the model reads, listing the shells installed.","locale":"en"},"12168":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"Shell","locale":"en"},"12169":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"How a command runs","locale":"en"},"12170":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"bash, zsh, sh","locale":"en"},"12171":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"`<shell> -c <command>`, never as a login shell","locale":"en"},"12172":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"PowerShell","locale":"en"},"12173":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"`-NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command <command>`","locale":"en"},"12174":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"cmd","locale":"en"},"12175":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"`/d /s /c <command>`","locale":"en"},"12176":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#choose-the-shell","content":"A call that names no shell runs in **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Shell** (`playground.shell`). **Automatic**, the default, is bash, or `sh` where there is no bash; on Windows it is PowerShell, or cmd without it. The option shows what it is now (\"Now bash\"). The menu lists only the shells installed on the machine; a chosen shell that is not installed falls back to automatic. The tool descriptions tell the model the default shell and the ones installed, and a command's result says which shell it ran in.","locale":"en"},"12177":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#output-that-is-not-utf-8","content":"Hoshimi reads command output as UTF-8. Output in any other encoding never stops a command or the reply: each byte that is not UTF-8 becomes `�` (U+FFFD). Hoshimi does not, however, make commands print UTF-8; they print in the encoding of the terminal Hoshimi was started from. Where that is not UTF-8 (most often Windows set to Chinese, Japanese or Korean, whose console uses a code page such as GBK, 936), non-English file names, `dir` listings and error messages reach the model as `����`, and what `write_stdin` types (always UTF-8) is misread the same way.","locale":"en"},"12178":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#output-that-is-not-utf-8","content":"To fix it, switch the terminal to UTF-8, then start Hoshimi from that same terminal; its commands inherit the setting:","locale":"en"},"12179":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#output-that-is-not-utf-8","content":"This lasts only for that terminal window. To keep it, and for a Hoshimi started without a terminal (a shortcut, a scheduled task, a service), set it for the system: on Windows, **Settings › Time & language › Language & region › Administrative language settings › Change system locale…**, tick **Beta: Use Unicode UTF-8 for worldwide language support** and restart; on Linux and macOS, put the `export` lines in your shell's profile, or `Environment=LANG=C.UTF-8` in a systemd unit. A program that picks its own encoding whatever the terminal says still prints in it.","locale":"en"},"12180":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#search-the-web-web_search","content":"Asks DuckDuckGo's light page (no key needed), or a SearXNG instance set in **SearXNG address** (`playground.search_url`), whose JSON format must be turned on.","locale":"en"},"12181":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#search-the-web-web_search","content":"Returns up to 8 results by default (at most 20), each with its title, address and a snippet.","locale":"en"},"12182":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#search-the-web-web_search","content":"DuckDuckGo limits how often it is asked; if it stops answering, wait a little or set up SearXNG.","locale":"en"},"12183":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-web-pages-web_fetch","content":"Reads a public `http://` or `https://` address (`https://` is added when none is given) and returns it with its final address and title. HTML is converted to Markdown, keeping headings, paragraphs, links, lists, code and tables; scripts, styles, navigation and forms are dropped, and a page's main content is preferred.","locale":"en"},"12184":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-web-pages-web_fetch","content":"Only text is read (HTML, plain text, JSON, XML, RSS and the like); at most 5 MB is downloaded and 60,000 characters returned.","locale":"en"},"12185":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-web-pages-web_fetch","content":"Local and private addresses are refused: `localhost`, names ending in `.localhost`, `.local` or `.internal`, and any name that resolves to a loopback, private, link-local, reserved or multicast address. The check is repeated at every redirect (at most 5). Addresses with a user name or password are refused too. This keeps a model from reading the gateway itself, which holds your account credentials, or anything else on your network.","locale":"en"},"12186":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#read-web-pages-web_fetch","content":"Both web tools go out through the gateway's network settings, including its proxy (see Network).","locale":"en"},"12187":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"The approval mode decides which calls need approval, and who gives it: the review model or you. New chats start with **Settings › Tools › How tools run › When tools ask first**; each chat can choose its own.","locale":"en"},"12188":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Mode (`playground.approval`)","locale":"en"},"12189":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Short name","locale":"en"},"12190":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Asks before","locale":"en"},"12191":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Automatic review** (`review`, default)","locale":"en"},"12192":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Auto review**","locale":"en"},"12193":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"The calls **Ask first** asks about go to the review model, which allows or denies them; you're asked only when it can't decide","locale":"en"},"12194":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Ask first** (`ask`)","locale":"en"},"12195":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Ask**","locale":"en"},"12196":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Every command (`shell`, `exec_command`, and `write_stdin` when it types), every file change, and reading anything outside the workspace","locale":"en"},"12197":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Ask outside the workspace** (`workspace`)","locale":"en"},"12198":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Workspace**","locale":"en"},"12199":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Only reading or changing files outside the workspace. Commands and changes inside it run without asking","locale":"en"},"12200":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Full access** (`full`)","locale":"en"},"12201":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"**Full access**","locale":"en"},"12202":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Nothing. Tools do whatever the model calls for","locale":"en"},"12203":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#when-tools-ask-first","content":"Searching and reading web pages never ask, and neither do reads inside the workspace. `auto`, the old name of `workspace`, is still accepted in the config file and the API; chats saved with it are moved to `workspace`.","locale":"en"},"12204":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#the-shield-menu-in-the-composer","content":"The composer always shows a shield, whether tools are on or not. It shows the chat's mode (**Auto review**, a shield with a check; **Ask**, a shield with a person; **Workspace**, a half shield; or **Full access**, a shield crossed out in red) and opens **When tools ask first** to change it for this chat alone. It works even while a reply is running: the new mode applies from the next tool call. A new chat starts as Settings say again. On a phone the shield shows only its icon.","locale":"en"},"12205":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"In **Automatic review**, the calls that would ask in **Ask first** go to a model instead of to you: every `shell` and `exec_command`, `write_stdin` when it types something, every `apply_patch`, and `read` outside the workspace. The reviewer is **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Review model** (`playground.review_model`); empty, the default, is **The chat’s own model**. A fast, careful model is a good choice.","locale":"en"},"12206":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"The reviewer is sent:","locale":"en"},"12207":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"A fixed policy, adapted from the automatic review (\"guardian\") in OpenAI Codex. It tells the reviewer there is no sandbox.","locale":"en"},"12208":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"The conversation so far, as a transcript. Only your messages count as trusted; the assistant's text, its tool calls and their output are untrusted, so instructions planted in a file or a web page cannot authorise anything.","locale":"en"},"12209":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"The planned call as JSON: the tool, its arguments, what it needs approval for, whether it reaches outside the workspace, the workspace, and for commands the shell.","locale":"en"},"12210":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"It cannot run anything itself. It answers with a risk level (low, medium, high or critical), how clearly you authorised the call (unknown, low, medium or high), an outcome and a one-sentence rationale:","locale":"en"},"12211":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Risk","locale":"en"},"12212":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Outcome","locale":"en"},"12213":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Low, medium","locale":"en"},"12214":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Allowed","locale":"en"},"12215":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"High","locale":"en"},"12216":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Allowed only when you clearly asked for it (authorisation at least medium) and it is narrowly scoped","locale":"en"},"12217":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Critical","locale":"en"},"12218":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"Denied","locale":"en"},"12219":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"High and critical are things like deleting data that can't be recovered, force-pushing shared branches, sending secrets or private data somewhere untrusted, reading credentials from unusual places, or weakening security for good.","locale":"en"},"12220":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"**Allowed**: the call runs. Opening its card shows \"Allowed by *model*\", with the risk and the rationale when given.","locale":"en"},"12221":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"**Denied**: the card shows **Denied by review** and opens to show \"Denied by *model* · high risk — *rationale*\". The model is told the rationale and not to work around it: no workaround, indirect execution or other tool to the same end. It goes on only with a materially safer alternative, or if you explicitly approve after being told the risk; otherwise it stops and asks you.","locale":"en"},"12222":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"**No decision**: a review takes at most 90 seconds. If the reviewer fails (a station error, too slow, or an answer that isn't a decision), the call is not denied: it waits for you with **Needs approval**, as in **Ask first**, and the card says \"The automatic review couldn’t decide, so you’re asked — *reason*\".","locale":"en"},"12223":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"While a call is reviewed, its card shows **Reviewing…** and the reply's foot line **Reviewing *tool*…**. Review time counts as the reply's own working time; time waiting for you is left out of \"Worked for\".","locale":"en"},"12224":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"If the reviewer denies 3 calls in a row, or 10 in one reply, the reply is stopped: the calls left in that round are marked **Stopped**, and the reply ends with \"The automatic review denied *n* of this reply’s calls, so it was stopped. Say how to go on, or choose another approval mode.\"","locale":"en"},"12225":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#automatic-review","content":"**Always allow**, given by you earlier in the chat, still holds: the calls it covers run without asking anyone, the reviewer included.","locale":"en"},"12226":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"A call that must ask you stops with **Needs approval**, opens, and shows what it would do (the command, or each file the patch changes, as a diff) and a question:","locale":"en"},"12227":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"Question","locale":"en"},"12228":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"Asked for","locale":"en"},"12229":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Run this command?**","locale":"en"},"12230":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"`shell`, `exec_command`, or `write_stdin` typing into a session","locale":"en"},"12231":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Apply these changes?**","locale":"en"},"12232":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"A patch inside the workspace","locale":"en"},"12233":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Change files outside the workspace?**","locale":"en"},"12234":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"A patch that touches a file outside it","locale":"en"},"12235":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Read this file outside the workspace?**","locale":"en"},"12236":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"`read` outside the workspace","locale":"en"},"12237":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"Answer with:","locale":"en"},"12238":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Allow**: run this call.","locale":"en"},"12239":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Always allow**: run this call, and calls like it in this chat, without asking again. \"Like it\" means the same tool switch, and inside versus outside the workspace counts separately: always allowing edits in the workspace does not allow edits outside it. The permission lasts until the server restarts, and is forgotten when the chat is deleted.","locale":"en"},"12240":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"**Deny**: skip it. The model is told you declined and not to try again unless you ask, and the card shows **Declined**.","locale":"en"},"12241":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#answer-an-approval","content":"A call waits 10 minutes for an answer; no answer counts as a denial. Stopping the reply stops a waiting call.","locale":"en"},"12242":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Each call is a line in the reply: an icon, a verb and what it acted on (**Read** `path`, **Edit** `files`, **Run** `command`, **Start** `command`, **Check** or **Type into** *session n*, **Stop** *session n*, **Search** \"query\", **Open** *address*), then its state:","locale":"en"},"12243":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"State","locale":"en"},"12244":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12245":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Preparing…**","locale":"en"},"12246":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The model is still writing the call","locale":"en"},"12247":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Reviewing…**","locale":"en"},"12248":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The review model is judging it","locale":"en"},"12249":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Needs approval**","locale":"en"},"12250":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Waiting for your answer","locale":"en"},"12251":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"A spinner with the time","locale":"en"},"12252":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Running","locale":"en"},"12253":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"A check with the time","locale":"en"},"12254":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Done","locale":"en"},"12255":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Exit** *code* or **Failed**","locale":"en"},"12256":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The command exited with an error, or the tool failed; the model reads why","locale":"en"},"12257":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Declined**","locale":"en"},"12258":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"You denied it","locale":"en"},"12259":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Denied by review**","locale":"en"},"12260":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The review model denied it; the model reads why","locale":"en"},"12261":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"**Stopped**","locale":"en"},"12262":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The reply was stopped before it finished","locale":"en"},"12263":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Click a card to open it. What was asked and what came back are laid out for each tool:","locale":"en"},"12264":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Tool","locale":"en"},"12265":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Opened, it shows","locale":"en"},"12266":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"`apply_patch`","locale":"en"},"12267":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"How many files changed and the lines added and removed, then each file with what happened to it (**Added**, **Modified**, **Renamed from** *path*, **Deleted**) and its diff, highlighted in the file's language. Once applied, each line has its numbers in the file before and after. A long diff starts folded. A patch shows while the model is still writing it","locale":"en"},"12268":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"`read`","locale":"en"},"12269":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"A file's lines beside their numbers, highlighted, with which lines they are (**Lines 1–2000 of 5000**); a directory's folders and files, and how many more were left out","locale":"en"},"12270":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"`shell` and background commands","locale":"en"},"12271":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The command, highlighted, with its shell and where it ran; the keys typed into a session (**^C** for Ctrl+C, **⏎** for Enter); then the output under its exit code (**Running** for a session still going), **Timed out**, and how long it took","locale":"en"},"12272":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"`web_search`","locale":"en"},"12273":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Each result's title as a link, its site, and what it says","locale":"en"},"12274":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"`web_fetch`","locale":"en"},"12275":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"The page's title and site, a link to it, **Cut short** when the tool cut it, and its text as Markdown, which opens to its full length when asked","locale":"en"},"12276":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Any other tool","locale":"en"},"12277":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Its arguments one to a row, and its output (highlighted when it is JSON)","locale":"en"},"12278":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#tool-cards","content":"Each part has a **Copy code** button, and anything the Playground does not recognise (an error, for one) shows as the tool returned it. Between rounds the reply shows **Working…**.","locale":"en"},"12279":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"While a reply with tools is running, you can add to it without stopping it. The box reads \"Add to what it’s doing…\"; type and press Enter (or the button, now **Send to the reply under way**).","locale":"en"},"12280":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"Your message shows faded under the reply with **Read after the current step**. The model reads it at the start of its next round, after the calls in progress, and it then appears in the reply where it was read.","locale":"en"},"12281":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"A message sent just as the model finishes keeps the reply going for one more round, to answer it.","locale":"en"},"12282":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"If the reply had already ended, the message goes back in the box (\"The reply had already ended; your message is back in the box.\") for you to send as a new message. If the reply is stopped or fails before reading it, the text comes back to the box too.","locale":"en"},"12283":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#steer-a-reply-while-it-works","content":"With an empty box, the button is still **Stop**, and Esc always stops.","locale":"en"},"12284":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#background-commands-above-the-composer","content":"Commands a chat's tools started with `exec_command` and that are still running are listed above the composer (**Background commands**): the command, **running**, and a stop button (**Stop** *command*) that stops it and everything it started. They keep running between replies until the model stops them, you stop them, the chat is deleted or the server stops.","locale":"en"},"12285":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#workspace","content":"The workspace is where the tools start: relative paths resolve there, and `shell` and background commands run there unless the model names another folder. It is **Settings › Tools › How tools run › Workspace** (`playground.workspace`; `~` is expanded); empty uses `workspace` in the data folder (see Data folder and paths). It is created when a reply with tools first runs.","locale":"en"},"12286":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#workspace","content":"The workspace is the line the approval modes draw: reading or changing files outside it asks in **Ask first** and **Ask outside the workspace**, and goes to the review model in **Automatic review**. It is not a boundary for commands: a command can `cd` anywhere and touch anything the user running Hoshimi can.","locale":"en"},"12287":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#stopping","content":"A reply calls tools for as many rounds as it takes: there is no limit, and it ends when the model answers without calling one. **Stop** (or Esc) ends the reply at once. A running `shell` command is stopped with everything it started; a call waiting for approval or being reviewed is dropped; calls not yet run are marked **Stopped**. What the reply said and did so far is kept. Background commands keep running: stop them above the composer.","locale":"en"},"12288":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"There is no sandbox. Tools run as the user running Hoshimi, on that machine, with its files, credentials and network.","locale":"en"},"12289":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"**Ask first** is the only mode where you see every command and every file change before it happens. Read each one before you allow it.","locale":"en"},"12290":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"**Automatic review** is a model's judgement. It can be wrong both ways, allowing what it should not and denying what is fine, and it can be fooled. It is a safeguard, not a sandbox.","locale":"en"},"12291":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"**Ask outside the workspace** runs any command without asking. A command is not confined to the workspace, so in this mode a model can change or delete files anywhere the user can, and reach your network. Use it only with a model and a task you trust.","locale":"en"},"12292":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"**Full access** runs every call without asking, including edits outside the workspace.","locale":"en"},"12293":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"**Always allow** removes the question for the rest of the chat (until the server restarts), and in **Automatic review** skips the reviewer too. Prefer **Allow** for anything you want to check each time.","locale":"en"},"12294":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"`web_fetch` refuses local and private addresses, but `shell` and background commands do not: a command can reach anything the machine can, including the gateway's own API.","locale":"en"},"12295":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"What a model reads (web pages, files, command output) can contain instructions meant to steer it. Use **Ask first** when tools read untrusted content.","locale":"en"},"12296":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#safety","content":"If the server is reachable from other machines, anyone who can sign in to the Web UI can use these tools. Set an access key and limit who can connect (see Access and security).","locale":"en"},"12297":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"Setting (**Settings › Tools**)","locale":"en"},"12298":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"12299":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"12300":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**Tools**","locale":"en"},"12301":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.tools`: any of `read`, `apply_patch`, `shell`, `terminal`, `web_search`, `web_fetch`","locale":"en"},"12302":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"All six (`[]` keeps none)","locale":"en"},"12303":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**When tools ask first**","locale":"en"},"12304":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.approval`: `review`, `ask`, `workspace` (`auto` is its old name) or `full`","locale":"en"},"12305":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`review`","locale":"en"},"12306":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**Review model**","locale":"en"},"12307":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.review_model`","locale":"en"},"12308":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"empty: the chat's own model","locale":"en"},"12309":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**Shell**","locale":"en"},"12310":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.shell`: `auto`, `bash`, `zsh`, `sh`, `powershell` or `cmd`","locale":"en"},"12311":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`auto`","locale":"en"},"12312":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**Workspace**","locale":"en"},"12313":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.workspace`","locale":"en"},"12314":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"empty: `workspace` in the data folder","locale":"en"},"12315":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"**SearXNG address**","locale":"en"},"12316":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`playground.search_url` (an `http(s)` address)","locale":"en"},"12317":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"empty: DuckDuckGo","locale":"en"},"12318":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"`terminal` is the switch for the three background-command tools.","locale":"en"},"12319":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Playground\" href=\"/docs/guide-playground\" description=\"Chats, attachments, versions, branches and Copy as API request.\" />","locale":"en"},"12320":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-agent-230","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-agent#settings-reference","content":"<Card title=\"Playground API\" href=\"/docs/api-playground\" description=\"Tool events, steps, approvals, steering and background commands over HTTP.\" />","locale":"en"},"12321":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"page","content":"Channels","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels","locale":"en"},"12322":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels","content":"The Channels page: each provider's state, signing into stations or adding API keys, account renewal, expiry, balances and check-in, the allowance, and a network route per channel.","locale":"en"},"12323":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"The channel list","locale":"en"},"12324":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"Channel details","locale":"en"},"12325":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#switching-a-channel-on-and-off","content":"Switching a channel on and off","locale":"en"},"12326":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#sign-into-a-station","content":"Sign into a station","locale":"en"},"12327":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#request-a-link","content":"Request a link","locale":"en"},"12328":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#finish-in-the-browser","content":"Finish in the browser","locale":"en"},"12329":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"Signed in","locale":"en"},"12330":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"Add an account","locale":"en"},"12331":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"Accounts","locale":"en"},"12332":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"Credential renewal","locale":"en"},"12333":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"Check-in and balances","locale":"en"},"12334":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#today","content":"Today","locale":"en"},"12335":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Allowance","locale":"en"},"12336":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Network","locale":"en"},"12337":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels","content":"The **Channels** page manages where models come from. A channel is one provider: a free station (such as Cline, TRAE, Qoder), a cloud service (such as Azure, Bedrock, Vertex), a local server (such as Ollama, LM Studio), or `agg` aggregator accounts. A channel can hold several accounts, and the gateway rotates between them. How providers differ and how to choose is in Providers.","locale":"en"},"12338":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels","content":"The list of channels is on the left and the chosen channel's details on the right; on a narrow window only one of them shows, and the back button at the top left of the details returns to the list. The chosen channel is part of the address (such as `#/channels/cline`), so a reload opens it again.","locale":"en"},"12339":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"The list holds the channels that are set up, plus the stations you can sign into or give a key that are not set up yet. Each row shows:","locale":"en"},"12340":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"A state dot and the name, with a state badge on the right when it is not **Ready**.","locale":"en"},"12341":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"The number of accounts (**N accounts**); **No account needed** for an anonymous channel, **Not set up** for one with nothing yet.","locale":"en"},"12342":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Today's tokens, when it was used today (**N tokens today**).","locale":"en"},"12343":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"An allowance bar underneath when the station reports one: red at 10% or less left, amber at 25% or less.","locale":"en"},"12344":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"State","locale":"en"},"12345":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12346":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"**Ready**","locale":"en"},"12347":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Serving normally","locale":"en"},"12348":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"**Needs attention**","locale":"en"},"12349":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Still serving, but something wants a human: an account needs a new login, a token has expired, an account is held out of rotation, or the channel was rate limited or has 10% or less of its allowance left","locale":"en"},"12350":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"**Off**","locale":"en"},"12351":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"You switched the channel off","locale":"en"},"12352":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"**Not set up**","locale":"en"},"12353":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"No usable account, and not an anonymous channel","locale":"en"},"12354":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Above the list:","locale":"en"},"12355":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"**Search providers**: by channel id or name.","locale":"en"},"12356":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Filters: **All**, **In use** (ready and needing attention), **Needs attention**, **Not set up**, **Off**, each with its count.","locale":"en"},"12357":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"On the right, the daily check-in status (**Done · time** or **Not yet today**; hover for the last result), **Check in all**, and the **Renew every account** icon button; see Check-in and balances and Credential renewal below.","locale":"en"},"12358":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#the-channel-list","content":"Saving a channel (switching it on, adding its first account) can move it in the order the server lists channels, but rows keep their places so nothing jumps from under the pointer; a reload takes the new order.","locale":"en"},"12359":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"Click a row to open its details. At the top are the name, the channel id and the **Enabled** switch; below them a row of actions:","locale":"en"},"12360":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"Action","locale":"en"},"12361":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12362":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"**Sign in**","locale":"en"},"12363":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"The main action of a station with a browser login; see Sign into a station","locale":"en"},"12364":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"**Add account**","locale":"en"},"12365":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"The main action of a channel that takes an API key or other credential; see Add an account","locale":"en"},"12366":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"**Renew now**","locale":"en"},"12367":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"With accounts: runs a renewal round for this channel","locale":"en"},"12368":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"⋮ menu","locale":"en"},"12369":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"**Renew now** and **Claim now** (with accounts); **Add account** when the channel takes both and it is not the main action; **View usage** opens the Usage page","locale":"en"},"12370":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#channel-details","content":"When the channel needs attention, a banner under the actions lists why, such as **2 need a new login**, **1 expired**, **1 held out of rotation**, **Rate limited ×3**, **Quota header unreadable ×1**, **Only 8% of the allowance is left**.","locale":"en"},"12371":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#switching-a-channel-on-and-off","content":"The **Enabled** switch writes `providers.<id>.enabled` in `config.json` and applies at once. Switched off, the channel no longer serves and its models leave the catalogue; its accounts stay in the configuration and come back when you switch it on. Adding an account to a channel that is off switches it back on.","locale":"en"},"12372":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#sign-into-a-station","content":"Free stations hand out credentials through the browser, so there is no key to paste. Click **Sign in**; the dialog shows three steps: **Request a link**, **Finish in the browser**, **Signed in**.","locale":"en"},"12373":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#request-a-link","content":"The gateway asks the station for a login link, showing **Asking the station for a login link…**.","locale":"en"},"12374":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#finish-in-the-browser","content":"As soon as the link arrives the browser opens the station's login page in a new tab (**A browser tab opened with the station's login page. Finish there.**). The dialog also shows the link with a copy button, for when the tab did not open.","locale":"en"},"12375":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#finish-in-the-browser","content":"A station with a device code shows the **Verification code** with a copy button: enter it on the authorization page.","locale":"en"},"12376":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#finish-in-the-browser","content":"A station that finishes through a callback to this machine (such as Codex, Gemini, TRAE, CodeArts, LobsterAI) shows an **Authorization code or callback URL** field. When the browser is on another machine than Hoshimi, the callback cannot reach the server: after logging in, copy the whole final callback URL from the browser's address bar, paste it here and click **Submit code**. Anthropic also accepts `code#state`.","locale":"en"},"12377":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#finish-in-the-browser","content":"The dialog ends with **This sign-in expires at …**.","locale":"en"},"12378":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"When the station answers, the account is written to `config.json` and joins the account pool at once, with **Signed in as** *account id*. Click **Done** to close.","locale":"en"},"12379":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"Closing the dialog, however it is closed, cancels a login still pending, so a late callback no longer saves an account. On failure the dialog shows the reason, and **Retry** starts over. Signing in again with the same station identity replaces the account rather than adding a second one.","locale":"en"},"12380":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"Cline has two login methods, chosen under **Cline login method** in the **Network** section of the Cline channel: **Device code (SDK)** (the default) or **Browser (extension)**. A change applies to later logins; existing accounts keep the identity they logged in with.","locale":"en"},"12381":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"The same logins work from the command line, which suits a server without a desktop:","locale":"en"},"12382":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#signed-in","content":"Each station's login, models and caveats are in Free stations; the EAC login is in EAC.","locale":"en"},"12383":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"For a channel that takes an API key or other credential, click **Add account**. The form depends on the provider: the server builds it from the fields that provider actually accepts.","locale":"en"},"12384":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"When a provider has several ways to authenticate, choose one under **Authentication method** first, such as Bedrock's **API key**, **AWS access keys**, **AWS profile**, **AWS default credentials**; Vertex's **API key**, **Google default credentials**, **Google service account file**; EAC's **Bundled EAC relay (GitHub sign-in)**, **Custom EAC worker relay**, **Direct EAC Bearer relay**.","locale":"en"},"12385":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"Common fields are **API key**, **API base URL (optional)** (blank for the default endpoint), **Model IDs** (separated by spaces or commas, or a JSON array), **Protocol**, and fields of particular cloud services such as **Azure resource name**, **Deployment mapping (JSON)**, **Cloudflare account ID**, **AWS region (default: us-east-1)**.","locale":"en"},"12386":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"Local servers (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp) use **Local server (optional key)**; the gateway contacts a local server only after an account is added.","locale":"en"},"12387":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"**Account ID (optional)**: left blank, the gateway names the account. A name the channel already has is refused.","locale":"en"},"12388":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"Click **Save account**. The gateway first lets the provider check the credential, then **appends** it to the channel's accounts in `config.json` (existing accounts are never replaced) and adds it to the running pool at once, with **Account** *id* **was added.** The key is kept in `config.json` and is never sent back to the browser.","locale":"en"},"12389":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"The `agg` aggregator's form is different: under **Station**, pick a station from the searchable list, or choose **Custom address…** and enter the station's OpenAI-compatible root in **Base URL**; then the **API key**. `hoshimi stations` lists the stations; see Aggregator accounts.","locale":"en"},"12390":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#add-an-account","content":"Which fields each cloud service needs is in Cloud services and Local and compatible endpoints.","locale":"en"},"12391":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"The **Accounts** section lists each account of the channel:","locale":"en"},"12392":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"The account id.","locale":"en"},"12393":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"A status line: when the token expires (\"expires in 3 hours\", \"expired 2 days ago\"; hover for the exact time), the balance (amount and unit, or the station's message), and why the account is held out of rotation and when it returns (\"Rate limited, back in 10 minutes\"). A failing account gets a second line with its last error.","locale":"en"},"12394":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"On the right, today's tokens and when it was last used.","locale":"en"},"12395":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"A state badge and a ⋮ menu.","locale":"en"},"12396":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"State","locale":"en"},"12397":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12398":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Ready**","locale":"en"},"12399":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"Usable","locale":"en"},"12400":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Needs login**","locale":"en"},"12401":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"The station refused the refresh token; sign in again","locale":"en"},"12402":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Expired**","locale":"en"},"12403":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"The token has expired","locale":"en"},"12404":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Resting**","locale":"en"},"12405":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"Held out of rotation for a while, **Rate limited** or **Blocked by policy**; it returns by itself","locale":"en"},"12406":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Failing**","locale":"en"},"12407":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"The last renewal failed; the next round tries again","locale":"en"},"12408":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"How long an account rests follows the reset time the station gives, or an hour when it gives none. Holds are kept in memory and cleared by a restart. The full rotation and retry rules are in Models and reasoning effort.","locale":"en"},"12409":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"An account's ⋮ menu:","locale":"en"},"12410":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Renew now**: for an account with a refresh token; runs a renewal round for this channel.","locale":"en"},"12411":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"**Forget**: after **Forget this account?**, the credential is removed from `config.json` and from the running pool. Sign in again to bring it back.","locale":"en"},"12412":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#accounts","content":"Account keys and tokens are stored in plain text in `config.json` in the data folder (made readable by the owner only, where the system allows). Do not share a filled-in config file. `hoshimi config path` prints where it is; see Data folder and paths.","locale":"en"},"12413":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"With **Settings › Automation › Credential renewal** on (the default), the gateway starts 30 seconds after launch and goes over every account with a refresh token every 30 minutes, renewing those whose token expires within the hour or that record no expiry at all. The renewed token is written back to that account in `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"12414":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"When the station refuses the refresh token (401/403, or a body that says the token is invalid), the account is marked **Needs login** and is not retried: sign in again.","locale":"en"},"12415":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"Any other failure (network trouble, a station error) is marked **Failing** and retried on the next round.","locale":"en"},"12416":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"**Renew now** and **Renew every account** run a round at once with the same rule as the timer: only accounts close to expiry are renewed.","locale":"en"},"12417":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#credential-renewal","content":"While timed renewal is on, the Channels page refreshes every 30 seconds, so renewal results show up by themselves.","locale":"en"},"12418":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"Some stations hand out free credits each day, claimed by a \"check-in\". With **Settings › Automation › Daily check-in** on (the default), the gateway checks in 30 seconds after launch and looks again every 24 hours, skipping a day (Beijing time, UTC+8, which the stations agree on) that is already covered. It goes one account after another, never several stations at once, to stay clear of the stations' risk controls. Stations without a check-in are skipped.","locale":"en"},"12419":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"**Check in all** above the list claims for every account of every channel at once; **Claim now** in a channel's ⋮ menu claims for that channel only. Stations usually answer \"already claimed\" to a second try, so clicking again does no harm.","locale":"en"},"12420":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"The status above the list reflects the daily timer only: **Done · time** when today's timed check-in got through, **Not yet today** otherwise.","locale":"en"},"12421":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"**Recent check-ins** in the channel details lists its last 5 results: **Claimed** or **Failed**, the account, the station's message, the credits received (**+N**) and the time. Every check-in result is kept for 365 days and can be read from `GET /api/v1/credits/checkins`.","locale":"en"},"12422":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#check-in-and-balances","content":"Balances are asked of each station once when the Channels page opens (`GET /api/v1/credits`) and appear in each account's status line. Stations without a balance endpoint show none.","locale":"en"},"12423":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#today","content":"The **Today** section shows the channel's **Tokens**, **Calls**, **Cache hit** and **Failed** for today (the server's local day).","locale":"en"},"12424":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Many stations report the remaining allowance in rate-limit headers on every response. The gateway reads it off ordinary responses, with no extra requests; when there is a reading, the details show an **Allowance** section:","locale":"en"},"12425":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"12426":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12427":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Allowance bar","locale":"en"},"12428":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"The percentage left; red at 10% or less, amber at 25% or less","locale":"en"},"12429":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Remaining**","locale":"en"},"12430":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"What is left / the limit","locale":"en"},"12431":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Reported in**","locale":"en"},"12432":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"The header the reading came from","locale":"en"},"12433":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Updated**","locale":"en"},"12434":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"When the last reading was taken; past five minutes the subtitle says **The last reading is more than five minutes old.**","locale":"en"},"12435":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Responses seen**","locale":"en"},"12436":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Responses read","locale":"en"},"12437":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Rate limited**","locale":"en"},"12438":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"How many 429s","locale":"en"},"12439":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Credential refusals**","locale":"en"},"12440":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"How many 401/403s","locale":"en"},"12441":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"**Server errors**","locale":"en"},"12442":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"How many 5xx","locale":"en"},"12443":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"The gateway takes the first remaining/limit header pair it can parse, in this order:","locale":"en"},"12444":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Remaining","locale":"en"},"12445":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"Limit","locale":"en"},"12446":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-remaining-requests`","locale":"en"},"12447":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-limit-requests`","locale":"en"},"12448":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-remaining`","locale":"en"},"12449":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-limit`","locale":"en"},"12450":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`ratelimit-remaining-requests`","locale":"en"},"12451":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`ratelimit-limit-requests`","locale":"en"},"12452":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`ratelimit-remaining`","locale":"en"},"12453":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`ratelimit-limit`","locale":"en"},"12454":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-remaining-requests-day`","locale":"en"},"12455":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-limit-requests-day`","locale":"en"},"12456":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-remaining-day`","locale":"en"},"12457":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"`x-ratelimit-limit-day`","locale":"en"},"12458":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#allowance","content":"A malformed pair counts as \"quota header unreadable\". Readings are kept in memory only, and the interface shows the header names, never their raw values.","locale":"en"},"12459":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Each channel can have its own network route, overriding the global one in **Settings › Network**. Choose under **Route**:","locale":"en"},"12460":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"12461":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"12462":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"**Inherit global settings**","locale":"en"},"12463":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"The default: use **Settings › Network**","locale":"en"},"12464":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"**Automatic (environment proxy)**","locale":"en"},"12465":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Reads the `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables; **Use Windows system proxy when no environment proxy exists** can then be turned on","locale":"en"},"12466":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"**Direct**","locale":"en"},"12467":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"No proxy at all","locale":"en"},"12468":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"**Proxy**","locale":"en"},"12469":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Enter an HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 address in **Proxy URL** and click **Save**; **Clear** goes back to inheriting","locale":"en"},"12470":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"The route covers every request the gateway makes for this channel: model catalogue, inference, login, token refresh, balance and check-in. Once saved, a proxy address is never shown again, only **Proxy configured; save to replace it.** A proxy that cannot be reached never falls back to a direct connection.","locale":"en"},"12471":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"Under it, the section lists the channel's recent failed network operations: the operation (such as **Model catalogue**, **Inference**, **Token refresh**, **Check-in**), the kind of failure (such as **Connection timed out**, **Proxy connection failed**, **Region restriction**, **Browser authorization required**), the HTTP status and the time; hover for the host and the route used. Successful operations are not listed.","locale":"en"},"12472":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-channels-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-channels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-channels#network","content":"The network settings in full are in Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"12473":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"page","content":"Models","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models","locale":"en"},"12474":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"The Models page: browse every model you can call, read its abilities, context length and free mark, run availability probes, copy a model id or try it in the Playground.","locale":"en"},"12475":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"The model list","locale":"en"},"12476":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#search-and-filters","content":"Search and filters","locale":"en"},"12477":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"How the catalogue loads","locale":"en"},"12478":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Availability probes","locale":"en"},"12479":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#failures-the-gateway-remembers","content":"Failures the gateway remembers","locale":"en"},"12480":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#copy-an-id-try-a-model","content":"Copy an id, try a model","locale":"en"},"12481":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-models#when-the-list-is-empty","content":"When the list is empty","locale":"en"},"12482":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models","content":"The **Models** page lists every model id the gateway can answer for right now: the values a client may put in a request's `model` field. They come from every enabled channel: the model lists the stations publish, plus the models declared in channel and account configuration. To make a model appear here, sign in or add an account for its provider on the Channels page first.","locale":"en"},"12483":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Under the title is the number of models; after a probe, also how many are **Available** (**N models · N available**).","locale":"en"},"12484":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Column","locale":"en"},"12485":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"12486":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Model id**","locale":"en"},"12487":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"The id used in requests. The line below is the station's display name (when it differs from the id) and **Free** when the station says the model is free. Long ids are cut; hover for the full id","locale":"en"},"12488":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Provider**","locale":"en"},"12489":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"The channel the model comes from","locale":"en"},"12490":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Context**","locale":"en"},"12491":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"The context window in K (1024 tokens); — when unknown","locale":"en"},"12492":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Abilities**","locale":"en"},"12493":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Three small icons: **Reasoning** (hover for the number of reasoning effort levels, such as **Reasoning · 3 effort levels**), **Vision** (reads images) and **Tools**. **No tool support** when the station says the model cannot call tools","locale":"en"},"12494":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Availability**","locale":"en"},"12495":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"The verdict of the last probe, below; **Not probed** for a model no round has reached","locale":"en"},"12496":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Click the **Model id**, **Provider**, **Context** or **Availability** heading to sort. On a narrower window **Context**, **Provider** and other columns are hidden in turn; on a phone the verdict moves under the model id and each row's two buttons fold into a ⋮ menu.","locale":"en"},"12497":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"About the marks:","locale":"en"},"12498":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"**Free** appears only when the station itself says so. No mark does not mean paid, only that the station did not say; a mark does not promise unlimited quota. Local models are not marked free automatically.","locale":"en"},"12499":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#the-model-list","content":"Abilities come from the provider's capability table and explicit account declarations; metadata the station publishes fills in where available, and models.dev only adds vision and reasoning for otherwise undeclared ids. Reasoning effort levels differ by provider; see Models and reasoning effort.","locale":"en"},"12500":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#search-and-filters","content":"**Search models**: matches the model id, the provider or the display name.","locale":"en"},"12501":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#search-and-filters","content":"**Provider**: one provider only (**All providers** to undo).","locale":"en"},"12502":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#search-and-filters","content":"**Availability**: appears after a probe and offers only the verdicts that occur, plus **Not probed**; **Any verdict** to undo.","locale":"en"},"12503":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#search-and-filters","content":"When nothing matches, the page says **No models match**.","locale":"en"},"12504":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"The model catalogue is shared with the Playground and the model pickers in Settings, and arrives as a stream:","locale":"en"},"12505":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"Cached models show first (a successful catalogue is saved in the data folder's `catalog-cache` and reused for up to seven days), so the page is usable at once.","locale":"en"},"12506":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"Each provider then asks for its own model list, and whichever answers first updates first. While it loads, a line above the list reads **Loading providers: done/total**.","locale":"en"},"12507":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"A provider that has not answered after 20 seconds is marked as timed out. Failed or timed-out providers are named in **Catalogue unavailable or timed out: …. Existing models are retained.** with the reason (such as **Connection timed out**, **Proxy connection failed**, **Credentials rejected**, **Region restriction**); a connection that broke off shows **Catalogue connection interrupted. Received models are retained.**","locale":"en"},"12508":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#how-the-catalogue-loads","content":"A failure never empties the list: the last successful catalogue stays. A failure is not retried by itself; click **Retry** (or the refresh button at the right of the toolbar) to load the catalogue again. When a station's list suddenly shrinks to less than half, the gateway keeps the old list until the next listing confirms the shrink. More in Models and reasoning effort.","locale":"en"},"12509":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Some channels' model lists are only a list of ids, which cannot say which models your network egress may actually use. Click **Probe** in the toolbar and the gateway sends each of those models the smallest possible request in the background (a `ping` with at most 64 output tokens) and records a verdict from the answer.","locale":"en"},"12510":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"A default round probes the channels whose lists cannot say: OpenCode Zen, `agg` aggregator accounts and NVIDIA NIM (the ones enabled). Kilo's free list is already filtered upstream and is not part of the default round.","locale":"en"},"12511":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"At most 2 models are probed at a time, each given up to 45 seconds, so the round does not trip the stations' rate limits.","locale":"en"},"12512":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"While a round runs the button reads **Probing…**, and clicking again does not start a second one. When it ends you see **Probe round finished** and the list updates.","locale":"en"},"12513":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Verdicts are kept in `hoshimi.db` in the data folder and survive a restart.","locale":"en"},"12514":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Verdict","locale":"en"},"12515":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12516":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"**Available**","locale":"en"},"12517":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"The model answered with content or tokens","locale":"en"},"12518":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"**Region blocked**","locale":"en"},"12519":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"The station refuses to serve this network egress","locale":"en"},"12520":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"**Unavailable**","locale":"en"},"12521":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"The station refused this model specifically","locale":"en"},"12522":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"**Throttled**","locale":"en"},"12523":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Quota ran out before the model could be asked","locale":"en"},"12524":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"**Unknown**","locale":"en"},"12525":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"A credential, network or station error that says nothing about the model","locale":"en"},"12526":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"Only **Unavailable** is a verdict about the model itself; region blocks, throttling and unknown results do not mean the model is gone.","locale":"en"},"12527":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"To probe particular models, call the management API (with the tool access key, when one is set):","locale":"en"},"12528":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#availability-probes","content":"`GET /api/v1/probe` reads the last round's results.","locale":"en"},"12529":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#failures-the-gateway-remembers","content":"Besides probes, the gateway remembers model failures while serving: a station answering 404/410 for a model (or 400/422 with a body that says the model was removed) counts once, and three within 10 minutes ban the model for the rest of this run. A banned model shows as **Unavailable** (over any probe verdict), and requests for it get `503 model_unavailable` at once, without upstream traffic. A restart, or `POST /api/v1/models/unavailable/reset`, lifts every ban:","locale":"en"},"12530":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#copy-an-id-try-a-model","content":"Each row ends with two buttons:","locale":"en"},"12531":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#copy-an-id-try-a-model","content":"**Copy the model id**: copies the id to the clipboard, for the `model` of a client.","locale":"en"},"12532":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#copy-an-id-try-a-model","content":"**Open in the Playground**: opens a Playground chat with this model, reasoning effort **Auto**. A chat that already has messages is not overwritten; a new one starts. See Playground.","locale":"en"},"12533":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#when-the-list-is-empty","content":"**No models yet**: no channel can serve yet. Sign into a free station or add an API key on the Channels page, then refresh. A fresh install can use OpenCode Zen and Kilo without an account; see Anonymous channels.","locale":"en"},"12534":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-models-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-models#when-the-list-is-empty","content":"A provider's models are missing: read the failure reason above the list, then open that channel and check its accounts and the diagnostics in its **Network** section. Common problems are in Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"12535":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-overview","locale":"en"},"12536":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview","content":"The Overview page: today's usage, endpoint addresses to copy, the channels in use, and the version, updates and default model.","locale":"en"},"12537":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Today","locale":"en"},"12538":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"Endpoints","locale":"en"},"12539":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"Channels","locale":"en"},"12540":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"Server","locale":"en"},"12541":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview","content":"**Overview** is the first page the interface opens on: the state of the gateway at a glance. From top to bottom it has **Today**, **Endpoints**, **Channels** and **Server**; each part has a button to the page with the details.","locale":"en"},"12542":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Figure","locale":"en"},"12543":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12544":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"**Tokens**","locale":"en"},"12545":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Input + output tokens of every call today","locale":"en"},"12546":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"**Calls**","locale":"en"},"12547":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Requests that went through the gateway today","locale":"en"},"12548":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"**Cache hit**","locale":"en"},"12549":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"The share of input tokens read from the upstream cache","locale":"en"},"12550":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"**Running now**","locale":"en"},"12551":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"Calls in flight at this moment","locale":"en"},"12552":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#today","content":"\"Today\" is the server's local day. The small line on the right is tokens per hour over the last 24 hours. The dot beside the title is the live connection's state (**Live**, **Reconnecting…**, **Offline**): while it is **Live**, the figures move as soon as a call finishes. **Usage** opens the Usage page with charts and every call.","locale":"en"},"12553":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"This part lists the addresses clients need. Its subtitle is the **Base URL**, the address you opened the interface on (by default `http://127.0.0.1:10600`). The button at the end of each row copies the full URL:","locale":"en"},"12554":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"Path","locale":"en"},"12555":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"What it is","locale":"en"},"12556":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"`/v1/chat/completions`","locale":"en"},"12557":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"**Chat Completions** (OpenAI)","locale":"en"},"12558":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"`/v1/responses`","locale":"en"},"12559":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"**Responses** (OpenAI)","locale":"en"},"12560":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"`/v1/messages`","locale":"en"},"12561":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"**Anthropic Messages**","locale":"en"},"12562":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"`/v1/messages/count_tokens`","locale":"en"},"12563":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"**Token count (estimate)** (Anthropic)","locale":"en"},"12564":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"`/v1/models`","locale":"en"},"12565":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"**Models**","locale":"en"},"12566":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"Most SDKs take `http://127.0.0.1:10600/v1` as their base URL. For example:","locale":"en"},"12567":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"If **Settings › Access** has a **Model API key**, requests also send `Authorization: Bearer <model API key>` (or `x-api-key`). Copy model ids from the Models page. How to connect each kind of client is in Connecting clients.","locale":"en"},"12568":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#endpoints","content":"The line under the list says whether a tool access key is set: **A tool access key is required to manage this server.** or **No tool access key is set.**. With no tool access key, the title also has **API reference**, which opens the server's own API documentation (`/docs`) in a new tab. With a key the button is left out, because that page cannot send the key the browser keeps; reach `/docs` and `/openapi.json` with the header instead, as described in the API reference.","locale":"en"},"12569":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"The channels that are set up or switched on are listed here (stations that are only offered, not set up, stay on the Channels page). Each card shows:","locale":"en"},"12570":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"The channel's name and state: **Ready**, **Needs attention**, **Off**.","locale":"en"},"12571":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"How many accounts it has, or **No account needed** (an anonymous channel, such as OpenCode Zen and Kilo).","locale":"en"},"12572":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"How many models in the catalogue come from it (once the catalogue has loaded).","locale":"en"},"12573":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"Today's tokens, when it was used today.","locale":"en"},"12574":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"Click a card to open that channel's details, or **Manage channels** for the list. While the model catalogue loads, or when a provider failed to load, a line above the cards shows the progress, the failed providers with their reasons, and **Retry**.","locale":"en"},"12575":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#channels","content":"With no channel at all the section says **No providers are enabled**. Sign into a free station or add an API key on the **Channels** page; there is no file to edit and no restart.","locale":"en"},"12576":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"12577":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12578":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"**Version**","locale":"en"},"12579":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"The Hoshimi version running","locale":"en"},"12580":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"**Latest version**","locale":"en"},"12581":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"The newest final release on PyPI, marked **Update available** or **Up to date**; **Checking…** until the first answer, **Could not check** when no check has succeeded yet","locale":"en"},"12582":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"**Default model**","locale":"en"},"12583":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"The model used when a request does not name one; **Not set** when there is none. Change it in **Settings › General**","locale":"en"},"12584":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"The server asks PyPI once in the background after it starts, then once a day. It only reads the version number; nothing is downloaded or installed. The check goes out through the global network settings. To keep Hoshimi from making this request, set `server.check_updates` to `false`; the **Latest version** row is then left out:","locale":"en"},"12585":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-overview-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-overview#server","content":"A change made from the command line needs a server restart. To upgrade, see Installation:","locale":"en"},"12586":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"page","content":"Playground","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground","locale":"en"},"12587":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground","content":"Chat with any model in the catalogue from the Web UI: keep, search and archive chats, attach images and files, edit questions, retry and branch replies, run slash commands, keep long chats going with context compaction, and copy a reply as an API request.","locale":"en"},"12588":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#start-a-chat","content":"Start a chat","locale":"en"},"12589":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#open-the-playground","content":"Open the Playground","locale":"en"},"12590":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#pick-a-model","content":"Pick a model","locale":"en"},"12591":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Ask","locale":"en"},"12592":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Commands","locale":"en"},"12593":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"Temporary chats","locale":"en"},"12594":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"The chat list","locale":"en"},"12595":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#titles","content":"Titles","locale":"en"},"12596":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#model-and-effort","content":"Model and effort","locale":"en"},"12597":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Attachments","locale":"en"},"12598":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"Images and models that cannot read them","locale":"en"},"12599":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"What a reply can show","locale":"en"},"12600":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"The image viewer","locale":"en"},"12601":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#reasoning","content":"Reasoning","locale":"en"},"12602":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"Edit, retry and versions","locale":"en"},"12603":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#branch-a-chat","content":"Branch a chat","locale":"en"},"12604":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#copy-as-api-request","content":"Copy as API request","locale":"en"},"12605":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Context and compaction","locale":"en"},"12606":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-long-a-reply-works","content":"How long a reply works","locale":"en"},"12607":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"How a reply ended","locale":"en"},"12608":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Playground settings","locale":"en"},"12609":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"A system prompt for the Playground","locale":"en"},"12610":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"Where chats are kept","locale":"en"},"12611":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground","content":"The **Playground** is a chat app built into the Web UI. It talks to models through the same gateway your clients use, so it is the quickest way to try a model, check an account, or see exactly what a request looks like. Chats are kept on the server, in the data folder, so they outlive the page and the process and come back from any browser.","locale":"en"},"12612":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground","content":"This page covers chatting. Letting a model read files, run commands and search the web is covered in Playground tools; the HTTP routes behind the page are in Playground API.","locale":"en"},"12613":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#open-the-playground","content":"Choose **Playground** in the navigation. The page opens the chat you had open last (on any browser), or an empty one.","locale":"en"},"12614":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#pick-a-model","content":"The **Model** menu in the composer lists every model the server advertises; type to search when the list is long. The first model is picked when nothing is chosen yet. From the Models page you can also open the Playground on one model, which starts a new chat with it.","locale":"en"},"12615":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Type in the box and press Enter. The chat is created on the server with its first message, and the reply streams in.","locale":"en"},"12616":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"The chat list sits beside the chat on a wide window and slides in as a drawer on a narrow one; the button at the start of the header opens and closes it. The button at the end of the header starts what comes next: **New chat**, or, on a new chat no one has written in yet, **Temporary chat**.","locale":"en"},"12617":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"12618":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Action","locale":"en"},"12619":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Enter","locale":"en"},"12620":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Send","locale":"en"},"12621":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Shift+Enter","locale":"en"},"12622":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"New line","locale":"en"},"12623":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Esc","locale":"en"},"12624":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Stop the reply coming in","locale":"en"},"12625":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"↑ in an empty box","locale":"en"},"12626":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Edit your last question","locale":"en"},"12627":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"/ at the start of the box","locale":"en"},"12628":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Open the commands","locale":"en"},"12629":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Ctrl+Shift+O (Cmd on macOS)","locale":"en"},"12630":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"New chat","locale":"en"},"12631":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"On a phone or a tablet, whose keyboard has no Shift+Enter, Enter starts a new line, and a message goes only when you tap **Send** (in the box, and when you edit a question). The hint under the box says so. While the command menu is open, Enter still runs the command that is highlighted.","locale":"en"},"12632":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"The whole conversation scrolls as one. A tool's output, a compaction summary and a question being edited scroll on their own when they are long; once one reaches its top or its end, scrolling on in the same direction (the wheel, a trackpad or a swipe) moves the conversation instead of stopping there.","locale":"en"},"12633":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"Pressing **Stop** (or Esc) ends the reply; what came so far is kept and the reply is marked **Stopped**.","locale":"en"},"12634":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#ask","content":"A reply runs on the server, not in the page. Opening another chat, starting a new one, leaving the Playground or reloading the page does not stop it: it goes on in the background, and several chats can work at the same time. Open the chat again to watch it from where it is, with what it wrote so far; it can be stopped from there too. A reply that ends while no page shows it is kept, and its chat is named as usual.","locale":"en"},"12635":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Type / at the start of the box to open the commands over the composer. Keep typing to narrow them (`/co` leaves **/compact** and **/status**, the matched letters in bold). ↑ and ↓ move, Tab completes the name, Enter runs the command and Esc closes the menu until you change what you typed. A command that chooses from a list opens the list once a space follows its name, and the words after it narrow the list: `/model gpt` then Enter picks the first match.","locale":"en"},"12636":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"12637":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12638":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/model`","locale":"en"},"12639":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Choose the model for this chat","locale":"en"},"12640":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/effort`","locale":"en"},"12641":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Choose the reasoning effort, for a model that has levels","locale":"en"},"12642":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/compact` *what to keep*","locale":"en"},"12643":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Compact the conversation now (see Context and compaction); words after the name tell the summary what to pay attention to","locale":"en"},"12644":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/status`","locale":"en"},"12645":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"How much of the context window is used and left, the last request's and the whole conversation's tokens (cached ones among them), compactions, how long replies worked, and the tools","locale":"en"},"12646":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/new` (or `/clear`)","locale":"en"},"12647":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Start a new chat","locale":"en"},"12648":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/fork` *title*","locale":"en"},"12649":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Continue this conversation in a new chat, up to the message on screen; words after the name are its title","locale":"en"},"12650":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"`/permissions` (or `/approval`)","locale":"en"},"12651":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"Choose when tools ask before they run","locale":"en"},"12652":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#commands","content":"While a reply is running only `/status`, `/permissions` and `/new` run; the others say why they can't. A slash followed by something that is not a command, such as `/etc/hosts`, is sent as a message.","locale":"en"},"12653":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"On a new, empty chat, the header button reads **Temporary chat**. A temporary chat works like any other but:","locale":"en"},"12654":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"it never appears in the chat list and is never named;","locale":"en"},"12655":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"it is deleted as soon as you leave it (open another chat or start a new one), and any left behind are deleted on the next start of the server;","locale":"en"},"12656":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"it has no chat menu and no **Branch in new chat**.","locale":"en"},"12657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#temporary-chats","content":"The box reads \"Ask anything — this chat won’t be saved\" while you are in one.","locale":"en"},"12658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"Chats are grouped by when they were last used: **Today**, **Yesterday**, **Previous 7 days**, **Previous 30 days** and **Older**. A chat branched from another carries a branch icon.","locale":"en"},"12659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"**Search chats** filters the list by title as you type.","locale":"en"},"12660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"Each chat has a menu (**Chat options**, the `…` button) with **Rename**, **Archive** and **Delete**. The same menu is in the header for the open chat.","locale":"en"},"12661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"**Rename** sets your own title, which is never replaced by a generated one.","locale":"en"},"12662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"**Archive** puts a chat away without deleting it. **Archived chats**, at the foot of the list, shows the archive; **Restore** brings a chat back, and so does sending a new message in it. **Back to chats** returns to the list. Archiving the open chat starts a new one.","locale":"en"},"12663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"**Delete** asks first, then removes the chat, its messages and the attachments only it carried, for good. A reply working in it is stopped first, and any background commands its tools started are stopped.","locale":"en"},"12664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-chat-list","content":"A chat whose reply is working now shows a spinner after its title (**Working…**), whether the page follows it or it works in the background; one whose tool call waits for your approval shows a shield (**Needs approval**) instead. Open it to answer.","locale":"en"},"12665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#titles","content":"Until a model names it, a chat is titled by its first question (up to 80 characters). Once the first reply is complete, a model names the chat in at most six words, in the language you wrote in. Which model does that is the **Title model** setting (see Playground settings below); by default it is the chat's own model. If the model cannot be reached, the first question stays the title. A title you set with **Rename** is kept.","locale":"en"},"12666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#model-and-effort","content":"The model and the effort are chosen in the composer and kept with the chat, so reopening it picks them up again. Both menus are locked while a reply is coming in.","locale":"en"},"12667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#model-and-effort","content":"**Model**: any model the server advertises. Picking another model resets the effort to automatic.","locale":"en"},"12668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#model-and-effort","content":"**Effort**: shown only for a model with reasoning levels. **Auto (server default)** sends no level and leaves it to the model and the provider; any other entry is sent as the request's `reasoning_effort`. See Model behaviour for how levels map to each provider.","locale":"en"},"12669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Use **Add photos and files** (the `+` button), drop files anywhere on the chat, or paste them into the box. Each file uploads right away and shows in a tray above the text; remove one with its close button before sending. A message can go with attachments and no text.","locale":"en"},"12670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Kind","locale":"en"},"12671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Accepted","locale":"en"},"12672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"How it is sent","locale":"en"},"12673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Images","locale":"en"},"12674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF","locale":"en"},"12675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"As an image. One larger than 2048 pixels on its longest side is scaled down in the browser (and re-encoded as WebP or JPEG); a smaller one under 1 MB, and any GIF that fits, goes as it is","locale":"en"},"12676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Text files","locale":"en"},"12677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Any `text/*` type, JSON, XML, YAML, TOML, SQL, shell scripts, and source files by extension (`.py`, `.ts`, `.vue`, `.rs`, `.go`, `.md`, `.csv`, `.log`, `.diff` and many more)","locale":"en"},"12678":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"As text inside your message, under the file's name. Up to 2,000,000 characters can be attached; a model is sent the first 200,000 and told the rest was cut","locale":"en"},"12679":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"PDF","locale":"en"},"12680":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Any PDF with a text layer","locale":"en"},"12681":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Its text is extracted in your browser page by page, then sent as a text file. A scanned PDF with no text is refused","locale":"en"},"12682":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#attachments","content":"Anything else is refused with \"send an image, a text file or a PDF\". An attachment uploaded but never sent is deleted after a day. Attachments are stored once and shared by branches, so branching a chat does not copy them.","locale":"en"},"12683":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"A model that reads images gets them as images. For one that does not (its catalogue entry says no vision), the Playground asks another model to describe each image, and sends the description in its place:","locale":"en"},"12684":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"The composer warns \"This model can’t read images; another model will describe them.\" when you attach an image to such a model.","locale":"en"},"12685":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"While a description is being written the reply shows \"Reading the image with *model*…\".","locale":"en"},"12686":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"The reply carries a note saying which model described which image. The description is kept with the image, so it is asked for once, not on every turn.","locale":"en"},"12687":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"Which model describes images is the **Image model** setting. **Automatic** takes the first model in the catalogue that reads images, skipping any the last availability probe found unavailable or region-blocked. **Off** never asks: the image is left out and the reply says so. You can also pick one model.","locale":"en"},"12688":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#images-and-models-that-cannot-read-them","content":"If a model listed as reading images is refused by its station because of the image, the reply is tried once more with descriptions, and a note says so.","locale":"en"},"12689":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"Replies are Markdown, and the Playground renders more than text:","locale":"en"},"12690":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"In the reply","locale":"en"},"12691":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"Shows as","locale":"en"},"12692":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"`$…$` or `\\(…\\)` in a line; `$$…$$` or `\\[…\\]` on lines of their own","locale":"en"},"12693":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"Typeset math (KaTeX). A wide formula scrolls sideways. A lone `$` stays a dollar sign, so \"$5 and $10\" is not math. TeX that cannot be read shows as code in the error colour","locale":"en"},"12694":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"A ` ```mermaid ` block","locale":"en"},"12695":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"The diagram, drawn in the interface's colours once the block is complete, with its kind (flowchart, sequence…) in the block's head. **Code** shows its source, **Diagram** the drawing again. It opens at its own size, or smaller to fit the column, but never below 60%, where its words would be too small to read; a frame shows at most 480 pixels of its height. A diagram larger than its frame fades out at the edges where there is more: drag it about, or scroll it sideways. Zoom it with Ctrl or ⌘ and the wheel, a pinch, or the head's **Zoom out** / **Zoom in** buttons; the percentage between them shows its size, and a click on it shows it at its actual size. **Fit to window** shows the whole diagram, and the arrows open it in the image viewer. A plain wheel still scrolls the chat. A diagram that cannot be drawn shows why, above its code","locale":"en"},"12696":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"A ` ```svg ` block","locale":"en"},"12697":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"The image. **Code** shows the source","locale":"en"},"12698":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"A ` ```html ` block","locale":"en"},"12699":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"Its code, with a **Preview** button that shows the page in a frame. The frame runs the page's scripts but cannot reach the network, this interface or its access key","locale":"en"},"12700":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"`![description](address)`","locale":"en"},"12701":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"The image. An address ending in `.mp4`, `.webm` or `.mov` shows a video player; `.mp3`, `.wav`, `.ogg` and similar an audio player","locale":"en"},"12702":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"Every code block, diagram and SVG has a toolbar for a head: an icon for what it holds (code, a command, a diff, a diagram, an image, a page), its language (**Python**, **Bash**…, or **Text** when the block names none), and its buttons, with **Copy code** last. HTML written directly in a reply (outside a code block) is shown as text.","locale":"en"},"12703":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#what-a-reply-can-show","content":"**Media from other sites.** Loading an image tells the site that serves it you are reading, and the address can carry text from the conversation, so an image, video or audio file a reply points to on another site waits behind a button that names the site (\"Load image from example.com\"). Media written into the reply itself (a `data:` address) shows at once. To always load media, set **Images and video from other sites** to **Always load** in **Settings › Appearance**.","locale":"en"},"12704":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"Click any image in the chat (an attachment, an image in a reply, a diagram or an SVG) to open it in the viewer:","locale":"en"},"12705":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"**Zoom** with the mouse wheel, a pinch, a double click, or + and -; 0 or **Fit to window** goes back. Drag to look around while zoomed. Diagrams and SVG images stay sharp at every zoom.","locale":"en"},"12706":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"**Move** between all the images in the chat with the side buttons, ← and →, or a swipe.","locale":"en"},"12707":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"**Download** saves the image; **Open in a new tab** opens it on its own (not offered for images written into the reply, which browsers do not open as pages).","locale":"en"},"12708":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#the-image-viewer","content":"Esc or **Close** closes it.","locale":"en"},"12709":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#reasoning","content":"For a model that shows its reasoning, the reply starts with a folded line: **Thinking…** with the time so far while it reasons, then **Thought for** *time* once it answers. Click the line to read the reasoning; it stays as you left it. Models that do not return reasoning have no such line.","locale":"en"},"12710":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"A chat is a tree: editing a question or retrying a reply adds a new version beside the old one, and both stay readable.","locale":"en"},"12711":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"**Edit message** (on a question, or ↑ in an empty box for the last one) opens the question in place. Change the text, remove attachments, and press **Send** (or Enter; Esc cancels). The edit becomes a new version of that question, answered afresh; what followed the old version stays with it.","locale":"en"},"12712":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"**Try again** (on a reply) asks for another reply to the same question, with the model and effort now in the composer. Switch the model first to compare models on the same question. A failed reply also shows **Try again** next to its error.","locale":"en"},"12713":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"A turn with versions shows **Previous version**, *n* / *total* and **Next version**. Moving to another version also brings back the newest replies under it; they slide in from the side the arrow points to, while the messages above stay put. The version on screen is remembered with the chat.","locale":"en"},"12714":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#edit-retry-and-versions","content":"Editing, retrying and switching versions are unavailable while a reply is coming in.","locale":"en"},"12715":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#branch-a-chat","content":"**Branch in new chat** (on a reply) copies the chat up to that reply into a new chat and opens it (\"Opened in a new chat\"). The new chat keeps the title, the model and effort, and the chat's approval mode; the original is untouched. Use it to take a conversation in two directions without switching versions back and forth.","locale":"en"},"12716":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#copy-as-api-request","content":"Under **More actions** on a reply, **Copy as API request** copies a `curl` command that sends the same Chat Completions request through the gateway's public API:","locale":"en"},"12717":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#copy-as-api-request","content":"The body is built on the server exactly as the reply was sent: the system prompt first, files inline, images as `data:` URLs (or as their descriptions, for a model that cannot read them), `reasoning_effort` when one was chosen, and the tool definitions with `tool_choice` when the chat has tools on. For a reply that used tools, it is the first round's request. Set `HOSHIMI_API_KEY` to your model API key, or drop the header when the server has none (see Access and security).","locale":"en"},"12718":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#copy-as-api-request","content":"Use **Copy** on a message to copy its text, and **Copy code** on a code block to copy just the code.","locale":"en"},"12719":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"Every model has a **context window**: how much of a conversation it can read at once. The ring beside the send button shows how much of it is left; press it, or type `/status`, for the details. The window is the one the model's station lists. When a station refuses a request as too long and names its real limit, that limit is used from then on.","locale":"en"},"12720":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"When a conversation nears the window, it is **compacted**: a model writes a summary of the conversation so far (the goal, the decisions and why, what is done and still to do, the files involved, the next step), and from then on the model reads that summary, with your latest messages kept word for word, in place of everything before it. The conversation itself stays on screen. A line marks where it was compacted; press it to read the summary.","locale":"en"},"12721":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"A conversation is compacted:","locale":"en"},"12722":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"**as a reply begins**, once the conversation has reached 85% of the window (`playground.compact_threshold`), or sooner when what is left could not hold a reply;","locale":"en"},"12723":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"**between a reply's rounds of tool calls**, so a long agent run keeps going;","locale":"en"},"12724":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"**when the model refuses a request as too long**: the conversation is compacted and the request sent again, and if that is still too long, once more with long tool outputs cut. This happens even with automatic compaction off;","locale":"en"},"12725":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"**when you type `/compact`**, optionally followed by what the summary should keep.","locale":"en"},"12726":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#context-and-compaction","content":"A compaction that fails leaves the conversation as it was. Editing a question from before a compaction, or branching from there, goes back to the whole conversation.","locale":"en"},"12727":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-long-a-reply-works","content":"While a reply runs, a line at its foot says what it is doing (writing, running or reviewing a tool, compacting the context) and for how long, second by second. The clock stops while a tool call waits for your approval; time the review model takes counts. When the reply ends, **Worked for 1m 23s** (or **Stopped after**, **Failed after**) stays beside its actions; point at it to see when it started and ended.","locale":"en"},"12728":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"What you see","locale":"en"},"12729":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"12730":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"**Stopped**","locale":"en"},"12731":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"You stopped it, or the server stopped; the text that came is kept","locale":"en"},"12732":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"**This reply failed.** and a reason","locale":"en"},"12733":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"The model or the station returned an error; **Try again** retries","locale":"en"},"12734":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"\"The image … was described by …\"","locale":"en"},"12735":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"A model that cannot read images got a description","locale":"en"},"12736":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"\"The image … was left out: no model could read it.\"","locale":"en"},"12737":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"No describing model was available, or **Image model** is **Off**","locale":"en"},"12738":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"\"… refused the image, so it was sent as a description.\"","locale":"en"},"12739":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"The station refused the image; the reply was retried with descriptions","locale":"en"},"12740":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"**Context compacted** above the reply","locale":"en"},"12741":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"The conversation was compacted before it (see Context and compaction)","locale":"en"},"12742":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"\"The conversation no longer fits in …'s context window, even compacted.\"","locale":"en"},"12743":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"Even the compacted conversation is too long: start a new chat, or branch from an earlier message","locale":"en"},"12744":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#how-a-reply-ended","content":"Notes about tools (a model that cannot call tools) are explained in Playground tools.","locale":"en"},"12745":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"The Playground's own settings are in **Settings › General › Playground** (see Settings), and in `config.json` under `playground` (see config.json):","locale":"en"},"12746":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12747":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"12748":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"12749":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12750":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**System prompt**","locale":"en"},"12751":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.system_prompt`","locale":"en"},"12752":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"empty","locale":"en"},"12753":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Sent first in every Playground chat, from its next message on. Empty sends none","locale":"en"},"12754":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**Title model**","locale":"en"},"12755":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.title_model`","locale":"en"},"12756":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"empty (**The chat’s own model**)","locale":"en"},"12757":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"The model that names new chats after their first reply","locale":"en"},"12758":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**Image model**","locale":"en"},"12759":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.vision_model`","locale":"en"},"12760":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`auto` (**Automatic**)","locale":"en"},"12761":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Describes images for models that cannot read them: `auto`, `off`, or a model id","locale":"en"},"12762":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**Compact long chats automatically**","locale":"en"},"12763":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.auto_compact`","locale":"en"},"12764":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`true`","locale":"en"},"12765":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"Compact a conversation as it nears the window. A request refused as too long is compacted either way","locale":"en"},"12766":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**Compact at**","locale":"en"},"12767":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.compact_threshold`","locale":"en"},"12768":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`0.85`","locale":"en"},"12769":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"The share of the window (0.5 to 0.95) at which a conversation is compacted","locale":"en"},"12770":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"**Summary model**","locale":"en"},"12771":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"`playground.compact_model`","locale":"en"},"12772":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"empty (**The chat’s own model**)","locale":"en"},"12773":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"The model that writes the summary","locale":"en"},"12774":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#playground-settings","content":"The tool settings (`playground.tools`, `workspace`, `approval`, `search_url`) are in Playground tools.","locale":"en"},"12775":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"The system prompt is empty by default, so a model gets only the conversation and the tool descriptions. The prompt below gives it the rest: when to act and when to ask, how to use the tools well, how to take approvals, steering and compaction, and how its reply is rendered here. Paste it into **Settings › General › Playground › System prompt**. It suits chats with and without tools, and any model; replies follow the language the user writes in.","locale":"en"},"12776":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"It is adapted from the base instructions OpenAI's Codex sends its models. What only Codex has is left out (its identity, its message channels, skills, apps, plugins and its JavaScript tool runner), and what the Playground does differently is fitted: local files are paths, not links; questions go in the reply; the tool descriptions already explain each tool, so the prompt says how to use them rather than what they are.","locale":"en"},"12777":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#a-system-prompt-for-the-playground","content":"Change it as you need: a line that names your project and its conventions, or one that sets the tone, goes at the end. The prompt only describes; what a tool may do is still decided by the tools you turn on and the approval mode (see Playground tools).","locale":"en"},"12778":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"Chats, their messages and attachments live in `hoshimi.db` in the data folder (see Data folder and paths), and are kept until you delete them. The chat open last is remembered there too, which is how the Playground comes back to it from any browser. A reply cut off by a server stop is kept as stopped.","locale":"en"},"12779":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"Every model call the Playground makes is recorded in Usage like any other call, under its own origin: `playground` for replies, `playground-title` for titles, `playground-vision` for image descriptions, `playground-compact` for compaction summaries and `playground-review` for automatic reviews of tool calls.","locale":"en"},"12780":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"<Card title=\"Playground tools\" href=\"/docs/guide-agent\" description=\"Let a model read and edit files, run commands and search the web, with approvals.\" />","locale":"en"},"12781":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-playground-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-playground#where-chats-are-kept","content":"<Card title=\"Playground API\" href=\"/docs/api-playground\" description=\"The conversation routes and streamed events behind this page.\" />","locale":"en"},"12782":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"page","content":"Settings","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","locale":"en"},"12783":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"The eight tabs of the Settings page: General, Tools, Access, Security, Network, Automation, Appearance and About, what each field does and the config key behind it.","locale":"en"},"12784":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"General","locale":"en"},"12785":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Tools","locale":"en"},"12786":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"12787":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Security","locale":"en"},"12788":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"Network","locale":"en"},"12789":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Automation","locale":"en"},"12790":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"Appearance","locale":"en"},"12791":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"About","locale":"en"},"12792":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#settings-that-are-not-in-the-interface","content":"Settings that are not in the interface","locale":"en"},"12793":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"**Settings** sits at the foot of the navigation and is split into eight tabs. The current tab is part of the address (such as `#/settings?tab=access`).","locale":"en"},"12794":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"Every field **saves on its own** as it changes; there is no overall save button. Switches and selections save at once, text and number fields when you leave them (or press Enter), and list fields each time a value is added or removed. A save shows **Saved**; a field that needs a restart shows **Saved · Takes effect after a restart.** An invalid value shows the reason and leaves the configuration unchanged.","locale":"en"},"12795":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"Apart from **Language** and **Appearance**, which are browser preferences, every setting is written to `config.json` in the data folder and applies to the running gateway at once. Each field below names its config key; the config file in full is described in Configuration file. Changes made from the command line or by editing the file need a server restart; changes made here do not (except the listening address and port).","locale":"en"},"12796":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings","content":"A channel's own switch and network route are not here but in that channel's details on the Channels page.","locale":"en"},"12797":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The **General** section:","locale":"en"},"12798":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12799":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12800":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12801":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Language**","locale":"en"},"12802":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"None (browser)","locale":"en"},"12803":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Auto detect (system language)**, English, 简体中文, 日本語","locale":"en"},"12804":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Default model**","locale":"en"},"12805":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"`server.default_model`","locale":"en"},"12806":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Used when a request does not name a model. Searchable; **None** means a request must name its model","locale":"en"},"12807":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"The **Requests** section, limits applied to every request the gateway accepts:","locale":"en"},"12808":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12809":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12810":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"12811":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12812":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"**Tries per request across accounts**","locale":"en"},"12813":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#general","content":"`server.max_account_retries`","locale":"en"},"12814":{"id":"