,"locale":"en"},"12890":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`playground.approval`","locale":"en"},"12891":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Automatic review** (`review`)","locale":"en"},"12892":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Automatic review**: a model judges commands, file changes and anything outside the workspace, and denies what's risky; you're asked when it can't decide; **Ask first** (`ask`): before commands, file changes and anything outside the workspace; **Ask outside the workspace** (`workspace`, formerly `auto`): commands and changes in the workspace run, reads and changes outside it ask; **Full access** (`full`): nothing asks. Calls that need leave are judged by the review model, or wait in the chat for your approval; the shield in a chat's composer changes the mode for that chat alone","locale":"en"},"12893":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Review model**","locale":"en"},"12894":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`playground.review_model`","locale":"en"},"12895":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**The chat’s own model**","locale":"en"},"12896":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Judges tool calls under **Automatic review**. A fast, careful model is a good choice","locale":"en"},"12897":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Shell**","locale":"en"},"12898":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`playground.shell`","locale":"en"},"12899":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Automatic** (`auto`)","locale":"en"},"12900":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Where commands run when the model names no shell. **Automatic** is bash (`sh` without it; PowerShell on Windows, `cmd` without it), and its help text shows the one in effect (\"Now bash\"). The menu lists only the shells installed here; a model can still ask for any other of them","locale":"en"},"12901":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**Workspace**","locale":"en"},"12902":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`playground.workspace`","locale":"en"},"12903":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`workspace` in the data folder","locale":"en"},"12904":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Where tools start, and the only folder whose files they can edit. The help text shows the path in effect","locale":"en"},"12905":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"**SearXNG address**","locale":"en"},"12906":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"`playground.search_url`","locale":"en"},"12907":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Empty","locale":"en"},"12908":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#tools","content":"Search with your own SearXNG (its JSON format turned on); must be an `http://` or `https://` address. Empty uses DuckDuckGo","locale":"en"},"12909":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"The **Listening address** section (subtitle **Takes effect after a restart.**):","locale":"en"},"12910":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12911":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12912":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"12913":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12914":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"**Host**","locale":"en"},"12915":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`server.host`","locale":"en"},"12916":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`127.0.0.1`","locale":"en"},"12917":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"The address the server binds; by default only this machine can connect","locale":"en"},"12918":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"**Port**","locale":"en"},"12919":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`server.port`","locale":"en"},"12920":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"10600","locale":"en"},"12921":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"The port the server tries first","locale":"en"},"12922":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"**Use only this port**","locale":"en"},"12923":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`server.strict_port`","locale":"en"},"12924":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Off","locale":"en"},"12925":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Off: when the port is taken, the server tries the next free one, up to 65535 and then from 1024. On: a taken port makes the start fail","locale":"en"},"12926":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Under them, **Listening on** *address* shows where the server listens right now. When the port was taken and another was used, it adds **Port 10600 was taken, so the server is on 10601.**; that describes this run and needs no restart. After you save a new host or port, a banner at the top says **The server listens on a different address than the saved** *host*:*port*. **Restart it to apply.**; restart `hoshimi serve`.","locale":"en"},"12927":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"The **Keys** section. The two keys are independent; leaving one empty turns off key checks for its APIs:","locale":"en"},"12928":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12929":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12930":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Protects","locale":"en"},"12931":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"**Tool access key**","locale":"en"},"12932":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`server.access_token`","locale":"en"},"12933":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Signing in to this interface, and the management API `/api/v1/*`, `/docs` and `/openapi.json`","locale":"en"},"12934":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"**Model API key**","locale":"en"},"12935":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"`server.model_api_key`","locale":"en"},"12936":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"The model API `/v1/*`, for agents and other clients; they send it as `Authorization: Bearer` or `x-api-key`","locale":"en"},"12937":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Type a key and click **Save** (or press Enter); **Clear** removes it. Keys are stored in the config file and never shown again: the interface only says **A tool access key is set.** or **A model API key is set.** After you save or clear the tool access key, this browser switches to the new key by itself; other browsers have to sign in again.","locale":"en"},"12938":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#access","content":"Setting **Host** to an address other than this machine's (such as `0.0.0.0`) requires both a **Tool access key** and **Security › Allowed CIDRs**, or the save is refused: the gateway forwards requests with your upstream accounts' credentials. Setting a **Model API key** as well is recommended. The full steps are in Access and security.","locale":"en"},"12939":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Who may connect. Press Enter after each value, or paste several at once (separated by spaces or commas); the × on a value removes it.","locale":"en"},"12940":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12941":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12942":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12943":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"**Allowed CIDRs**","locale":"en"},"12944":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"`security.allow_cidrs`","locale":"en"},"12945":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Networks that may connect, such as `10.0.0.0/8`. Loopback is always allowed","locale":"en"},"12946":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"**Allowed hosts**","locale":"en"},"12947":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"`security.allow_hosts`","locale":"en"},"12948":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"`Host` names that may connect, such as `gateway.example.com`. Empty allows any host","locale":"en"},"12949":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"**Allowed origins**","locale":"en"},"12950":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"`security.allow_origins`","locale":"en"},"12951":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Browser pages on other origins that may call this API (CORS), such as `https://app.example.com`. Needs a tool access key first","locale":"en"},"12952":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#security","content":"Host and origin checks apply to requests with a key too; a key does not get around them. The detailed rules are in Access and security.","locale":"en"},"12953":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"The default network route for every channel (config key `network`). Choose under **Route**:","locale":"en"},"12954":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"12955":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"12956":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"**Automatic (environment proxy)**","locale":"en"},"12957":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"The default. Reads `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` (lowercase variables take precedence). **Use Windows system proxy when no environment proxy exists** can then be turned on","locale":"en"},"12958":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"**Direct**","locale":"en"},"12959":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"No proxy at all","locale":"en"},"12960":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"**Proxy**","locale":"en"},"12961":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"Enter an HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 address in **Proxy URL** and click **Save**; **Clear** goes back to automatic","locale":"en"},"12962":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"The route is used for every request the gateway makes: model catalogue, inference, login, token refresh, balance, check-in, and the PyPI version check. A proxy address may hold a user name and password, so once saved the interface only says **Proxy configured; save to replace it.** A proxy that cannot be reached never falls back to a direct connection. Changes apply to new requests; streams already running finish on their original connections.","locale":"en"},"12963":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#network","content":"When one channel needs a different route, **Per-channel routes** takes you to the Channels page, where the channel's **Network** section overrides it. See Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"12964":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Two timers that keep the channels' accounts working:","locale":"en"},"12965":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Switch","locale":"en"},"12966":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Config key","locale":"en"},"12967":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"12968":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"12969":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"**Daily check-in**","locale":"en"},"12970":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"`server.auto_checkin`","locale":"en"},"12971":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"On","locale":"en"},"12972":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Claims each station's free credits once a day. **Today's check-in** under it says whether today is done, and the last round's result","locale":"en"},"12973":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"**Credential renewal**","locale":"en"},"12974":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"`server.auto_refresh`","locale":"en"},"12975":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"On","locale":"en"},"12976":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"Renews tokens before they expire: every 30 minutes, accounts expiring within the hour are renewed","locale":"en"},"12977":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#automation","content":"A pure gateway that should make no background requests can turn them off. Manual check-in and renewal are on the Channels page, with the rules in Channels. For one run, `hoshimi serve --no-checkin --no-refresh` turns them off at start; see Command reference.","locale":"en"},"12978":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"These options are kept in the current browser and affect only it:","locale":"en"},"12979":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"12980":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"Options","locale":"en"},"12981":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Theme**","locale":"en"},"12982":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Light**, **Dark**, **System** (the default). The theme button in the top bar switches it too","locale":"en"},"12983":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Colour**","locale":"en"},"12984":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"Pick a colour; the interface's palette is generated from it","locale":"en"},"12985":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Contrast**","locale":"en"},"12986":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Standard** (the default), **Medium**, **High**","locale":"en"},"12987":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Motion**","locale":"en"},"12988":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Follow system** (the default) or **Reduced**: short fades instead of slides and growth","locale":"en"},"12989":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Images and video from other sites**","locale":"en"},"12990":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#appearance","content":"**Ask first** (the default): media a Playground reply points to on another site waits behind a button naming the site; **Always load**","locale":"en"},"12991":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"12992":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"12993":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"**Version**","locale":"en"},"12994":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"The Hoshimi version running","locale":"en"},"12995":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"**Data directory**","locale":"en"},"12996":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"The folder holding the configuration, the database and the workspace","locale":"en"},"12997":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"**Config file**","locale":"en"},"12998":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"The full path of `config.json`","locale":"en"},"12999":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"**Database**","locale":"en"},"13000":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"The full path of `hoshimi.db`: usage, check-in history, probe verdicts and Playground chats are all in it","locale":"en"},"13001":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#about","content":"**Copy config path** copies the config file's path to the clipboard. With no tool access key there is also **API reference**, which opens the server's own API documentation (`/docs`). Where the data folder is and what is in it: Data folder and paths; on the command line, `hoshimi config path` prints the config file's path.","locale":"en"},"13002":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#settings-that-are-not-in-the-interface","content":"A few settings are only in `config.json`, such as `server.check_updates` (whether to ask PyPI for new versions) and the options in `providers.<id>.options` other than the network route and the Cline login method. Change them with `hoshimi config set` and restart the server:","locale":"en"},"13003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-settings-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-settings#settings-that-are-not-in-the-interface","content":"Every config key is in Configuration file.","locale":"en"},"13004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"page","content":"Usage","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Web UI guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage","locale":"en"},"13005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage","content":"The Usage page: choose a range or a single day, read the headline tiles and the token and speed charts, break usage down by model, provider, account and API, and look at each call.","locale":"en"},"13006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Ranges","locale":"en"},"13007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"Headline tiles","locale":"en"},"13008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#tokens-over-time","content":"Tokens over time","locale":"en"},"13009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#speed","content":"Speed","locale":"en"},"13010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#breakdown","content":"Breakdown","locale":"en"},"13011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#calls","content":"Calls","locale":"en"},"13012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#requests-and-responses","content":"Requests and responses","locale":"en"},"13013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#what-counts-as-a-call-and-as-a-failure","content":"What counts as a call, and as a failure","locale":"en"},"13014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#how-long-data-is-kept","content":"How long data is kept","locale":"en"},"13015":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#reset-statistics","content":"Reset statistics","locale":"en"},"13016":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage","content":"The **Usage** page records every call that goes through the gateway: how many tokens, how much was read from cache, time to first token and generation speed, which account of which channel answered, and whether it failed. The data is kept in `hoshimi.db` in the data folder and survives a restart. How usage is recorded and counted is in Usage statistics.","locale":"en"},"13017":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage","content":"Before any call, the page says **Nothing has been served yet**: send one request through the gateway (or say something in the Playground) and the data appears.","locale":"en"},"13018":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Choose a range at the left of the toolbar: **Day**, **24 hours**, **7 days** (the default), **30 days**, **90 days**. The range is part of the address (such as `#/usage?range=30d`), so a reload or a shared link opens the same one.","locale":"en"},"13019":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"With **Day**, a day navigator appears: the arrows step to the **Previous day** and **Next day**, and the button between them (**Today**, **Yesterday** or a date) opens a calendar. Days with usage are shaded by how many tokens they had; days after today, or before the first recorded day, cannot be chosen.","locale":"en"},"13020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Range","locale":"en"},"13021":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Chart buckets","locale":"en"},"13022":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Compared with","locale":"en"},"13023":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**Day** (today)","locale":"en"},"13024":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Hours","locale":"en"},"13025":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**Compared with yesterday up to this time**","locale":"en"},"13026":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**Day** (a past day)","locale":"en"},"13027":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Hours","locale":"en"},"13028":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**Compared with the day before**","locale":"en"},"13029":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**24 hours**","locale":"en"},"13030":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Hours","locale":"en"},"13031":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"The 24 hours before","locale":"en"},"13032":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"**7 days**, **30 days**, **90 days**","locale":"en"},"13033":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Days","locale":"en"},"13034":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"The span of the same length just before","locale":"en"},"13035":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#ranges","content":"Days follow the server's local time. At the right of the toolbar are the live connection's dot, a refresh button and a ⋮ menu (Reset statistics). When you change the range the page keeps the old numbers until the new ones arrive and then moves to them in one step, with a thin progress bar under the toolbar meanwhile.","locale":"en"},"13036":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"Six tiles sum up the range. Each shows its value, the change from the previous span (hover to see what it is compared with) and a small trend line:","locale":"en"},"13037":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"Tile","locale":"en"},"13038":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"13039":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"The line under it","locale":"en"},"13040":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"**Total tokens**","locale":"en"},"13041":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"Input + output tokens","locale":"en"},"13042":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"The number of calls","locale":"en"},"13043":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-usage","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-usage#headline-tiles","content":"**Input tokens**","locale":"en"},"13044":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-usage-39","page_id":"/en/docs/gui