"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-presets","content":"`OLLAMA_API_KEY`","locale":"en"},"13434":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-131","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-presets","content":"\"Upstream key variable\" is the environment variable the station's own tools read their key from, for reference only. Hoshimi reads credentials from `config.json` only and never reads these variables.","locale":"en"},"13435":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-132","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-presets","content":"\"Catalogue without a key\" only means the model list can be browsed; chat requests to these stations still need a key.","locale":"en"},"13436":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-133","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-presets","content":"A preset supplies the address only, never a model list; models are always read live.","locale":"en"},"13437":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-134","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"The same ID at two stations can be two different models at two different prices, so the gateway records which station each ID came from:","locale":"en"},"13438":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-135","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"A request for an ID tries the accounts that declare it in `models` first, then accounts with no `models` declaration, then the rest.","locale":"en"},"13439":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-136","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"With a single station you need no declarations. With several, use `models` to pin IDs to the right account, so a request does not land first on a station that does not know the ID.","locale":"en"},"13440":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-137","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#several-stations-in-one-channel","content":"Station rules (chat-model filters, free marks, capability tables) are matched by the `base_url` address, not the `preset` name: an account that says `preset: sambanova` but points `base_url` elsewhere does not get SambaNova's rules. A custom address gets no station rules at all.","locale":"en"},"13441":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-138","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"A station's `/models` usually carries IDs and nothing more. Without declarations, agg treats a model as text-only and non-thinking, and forwards the caller's request unchanged. Declare more in `options` when you need it:","locale":"en"},"13442":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-139","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"13443":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-140","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"13444":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-141","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`vision`","locale":"en"},"13445":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-142","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether the model accepts image input.","locale":"en"},"13446":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-143","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`reasoning`","locale":"en"},"13447":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-144","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether it is a thinking model.","locale":"en"},"13448":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-145","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`context_window`","locale":"en"},"13449":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-146","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Context length in tokens.","locale":"en"},"13450":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-147","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`max_output`","locale":"en"},"13451":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-148","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Maximum output length in tokens.","locale":"en"},"13452":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-149","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`efforts`","locale":"en"},"13453":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-150","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"The thinking-level menu, in display order. Including `disabled` makes thinking switchable off.","locale":"en"},"13454":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-151","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_default`","locale":"en"},"13455":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-152","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"The default level.","locale":"en"},"13456":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-153","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_patch`","locale":"en"},"13457":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-154","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"JSON merged into the request body when a level is chosen; `\"$effort\"` inside it is replaced by the level's name.","locale":"en"},"13458":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-155","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`effort_off_patch`","locale":"en"},"13459":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-156","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"JSON merged into the request body when the off level is chosen.","locale":"en"},"13460":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-157","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`region_sensitive`","locale":"en"},"13461":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-158","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Whether availability depends on the network exit's region.","locale":"en"},"13462":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-159","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"`model_specs`","locale":"en"},"13463":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-160","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Per-model-ID overrides of the keys above.","locale":"en"},"13464":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-161","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#capability-declarations","content":"Precedence: account declarations outrank what the station's own listing says, which outranks the defaults; keys placed flat in `options` act as defaults, and the ID's `model_specs` entry is applied last. Flat keys apply to every ID in the channel, so when the channel holds several stations, put declarations in `model_specs`. For an undeclared ID, only two facts are filled in from models.dev, whether it thinks and whether it accepts images; context limits are never borrowed from another station. The same keys can also go in `providers.agg.options` as defaults for the whole channel. The full rules for capabilities and thinking levels are in Model behaviour.","locale":"en"},"13465":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-162","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Each model's `free` field in `GET /v1/models` has three values: `true`, `false` and `null` (the station did not say). agg takes only what the station itself publishes:","locale":"en"},"13466":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-163","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Read from the listing rows: `anyapi`, `gmi`, `opengateway`, `orcarouter`, `tokenrouter`, `xkiro`, `bai` (IDs with `:free`), `merge` (a route whose input and output prices are both 0).","locale":"en"},"13467":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-164","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"Fixed IDs recorded from the station's pricing page: `agnes`, `bai`, `commandcode`.","locale":"en"},"13468":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-165","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"`venice` and `llm7` are deliberately left unmarked: Venice's zero-priced models still require a positive account balance, and LLM7's prices are list prices, not a statement about an account's balance.","locale":"en"},"13469":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-166","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#free-marks","content":"A free mark describes the station's price list; it does not promise that an account has allowance or that a call will succeed.","locale":"en"},"13470":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-167","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**Chat-model filters**: listings from known stations drop image, video, embedding, transcription and other non-chat rows, with a filter written per station; a row missing the relevant fields is kept, so a station's schema change does not empty its catalogue. LLM7 is filtered on its own `model_type` field.","locale":"en"},"13471":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-168","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**CommandCode**: models whose name starts with `claude-` go to Anthropic Messages (`<base_url>/messages`); the station's vision and reasoning tables act as defaults, and account declarations win.","locale":"en"},"13472":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-169","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"**Request shape**: requests to known stations turn `max_completion_tokens` into `max_tokens` and `developer` messages into `system`; requests to custom addresses are not rewritten. A station that answers a streaming request with one complete JSON document is still read correctly.","locale":"en"},"13473":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-agg-170","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-agg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-agg#station-specific-handling","content":"Most of these rules are ported from pi-free; the differences are in Migrating from pi-free.","locale":"en"},"13474":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"page","content":"Anonymous lanes","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","locale":"en"},"13475":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"The two free lanes that are on by default and need no account, OpenCode Zen and Kilo: what they offer, how to turn them off, how a key widens the catalogue, and how their protocols are handled.","locale":"en"},"13476":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance","locale":"en"},"13477":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Turning the anonymous lanes off","locale":"en"},"13478":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#opencode-zen-opencode","content":"OpenCode Zen (`opencode`)","locale":"en"},"13479":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"Anonymous use","locale":"en"},"13480":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"Widening the catalogue with an API key","locale":"en"},"13481":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Protocol handling","locale":"en"},"13482":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Thinking levels","locale":"en"},"13483":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#region-and-probes","content":"Region and probes","locale":"en"},"13484":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#kilo-kilo","content":"Kilo (`kilo`)","locale":"en"},"13485":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"Anonymous use","locale":"en"},"13486":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"Signing in with a key or a device code","locale":"en"},"13487":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Request handling and thinking levels","locale":"en"},"13488":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#verification-scope","content":"Verification scope","locale":"en"},"13489":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"On the first start, before there is any configuration, the `opencode` (OpenCode Zen) and `kilo` (Kilo AI) channels already work: each runs on a placeholder account with no credential in it and sends requests to the upstream's free models. On the **Channels** page both show **No account needed**.","locale":"en"},"13490":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","content":"Whether a model answers depends on the upstream's current models, quota and service state, and can differ by the region your network exits from. This page describes how the adapters work, not a promise about upstream availability.","locale":"en"},"13491":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"13492":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Upstream","locale":"en"},"13493":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Anonymous catalogue","locale":"en"},"13494":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"With an account","locale":"en"},"13495":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`opencode`","locale":"en"},"13496":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`https://opencode.ai/inference`","locale":"en"},"13497":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"The free slice of the live listing (IDs containing `free`, plus `big-pickle`, `space-bunny-free` and `union-alpha`)","locale":"en"},"13498":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"An API-key account uses its authenticated catalogue","locale":"en"},"13499":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`kilo`","locale":"en"},"13500":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"`https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway`","locale":"en"},"13501":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"Chat models the live listing marks `isFree: true`","locale":"en"},"13502":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"API key or device-code sign-in; the catalogue widens to every chat model the account can see","locale":"en"},"13503":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"To see the IDs available now:","locale":"en"},"13504":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#at-a-glance","content":"You can call them with the channel prefix, for example `opencode/big-pickle` or `kilo/kilo-auto/free`.","locale":"en"},"13505":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"An anonymous lane is switched off only with `enabled: false` (with no accounts it is otherwise enabled automatically):","locale":"en"},"13506":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Or in `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13507":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#turning-the-anonymous-lanes-off","content":"Switching the channel off on the **Channels** page does the same. To turn it back on, set `enabled` to `true` or delete the entry.","locale":"en"},"13508":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"Unless switched off, `opencode` runs on a placeholder account (`opencode-public`). The gateway reads the upstream `/v1/models` and keeps only the free slice: models whose ID has `free` as a separate segment (such as `mimo-v2.6-flash-free`), plus `big-pickle`, `space-bunny-free` and `union-alpha`, which are always treated as free. New free IDs keep the upstream's own spelling.","locale":"en"},"13509":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use","content":"The live listing is authoritative. A failed refresh keeps the last good catalogue; only a cold start with an unreachable listing uses the built-in historical fallback list.","locale":"en"},"13510":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"On **Channels** › **OpenCode Zen**, click **Add account** and choose **API key**, or write it into `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13511":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"Once the channel has accounts, it uses only the ones you configured; the anonymous placeholder is no longer added. An account without `api_key` sends its requests anonymously.","locale":"en"},"13512":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"When the first account has a key, the catalogue is no longer cut down to the free slice; the key's own permissions still apply.","locale":"en"},"13513":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"`project_id` is sent as the `x-opencode-project` header; the default is `global`.","locale":"en"},"13514":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#widening-the-catalogue-with-an-api-key","content":"The OpenCode Go plan is a separate channel, `opencode-go`; see Local and compatible endpoints.","locale":"en"},"13515":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The anonymous lane aligns with captured OpenCode v2.2.1 requests. In a 2026-10-29 live check of `deepseek-v4.1-flash-free`, default Python/httpx returned `FreeUsageLimitError`; Python returned 200 after aligning both TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 cipher lists and ordering with Bun. This does not reproduce Bun's entire TLS fingerprint. Other network exits and future quota remain subject to upstream responses.","locale":"en"},"13516":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Anonymous inference uses pyOpenSSL inside the Python process, with no Bun or OpenCode installation or subprocess required. Dependencies ship with Hoshimi; network diagnostics record `transport: pyopenssl`. A 429 or network failure never triggers a replay through another transport. Catalog queries, API-key accounts and other providers keep their existing transport.","locale":"en"},"13517":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The transport shares admission control, proxy routing and httpcore pooling. It supports HTTP/HTTPS and SOCKS5/SOCKS5H proxies, incremental streaming, connection and read/write timeouts, and releases connections when streams close early. TLS verifies certificate chains and hostnames, using HTTPX's default CA roots or `SSL_CERT_FILE` / `SSL_CERT_DIR`. Process-wide SSL settings remain unchanged.","locale":"en"},"13518":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Requests use `/inference/openai/v1` or `/inference/anthropic/v1`. Anonymous requests retain an OpenCode caller's `User-Agent`; other callers use `opencode/latest/2.2.1/cli`. They send `x-opencode-client: cli` without the legacy `x-opencode-request`.","locale":"en"},"13519":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-44","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"OpenCode session IDs and `x-opencode-project` are preserved; credentials still come from channel configuration. All four session/affinity headers share the session ID. Chat Completions uses `max_completion_tokens`, requests streaming usage and no longer injects `prompt_cache_key`. Responses still defaults its cache key to the session ID.","locale":"en"},"13520":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-45","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Playground conversations and other callers' `session_id`, `conversation_id`, `user`, or first user message map to descending IDs with real creation timestamps. Up to 8192 account-isolated mappings remain stable within the process, including across compaction and later replies; restart or cache eviction creates a new ID. Supply distinct IDs for conversations with identical opening messages.","locale":"en"},"13521":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-46","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Anonymous requests preserve existing system environment context. When absent, an `<env>` envelope says the working directory was not supplied by the caller and the platform is unknown. It never includes the gateway's local paths, files or skills.","locale":"en"},"13522":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-47","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Protocol selection prefers `options.model_protocols`, then catalogue declarations, then known model mappings. `deepseek-v4.1-flash-free` uses `/inference/openai/v1/chat/completions`, `muse-spark-*` uses `/inference/openai/v1/responses`, and `union-alpha` uses `/inference/anthropic/v1/messages`. The catalogue remains at `/inference/v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"13523":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-48","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"HTTP or streaming `FreeUsageLimitError` and `GoUsageLimitError` responses hold the affected account/model pair, retain the upstream error type, and do not invalidate login credentials. `FreeTierError` identifies a client restriction; protocol alignment cannot guarantee access beyond upstream quotas or access policies.","locale":"en"},"13524":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-49","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Anonymous requests declare the reference implementation's `read` and `shell` tool definitions (the upstream compares tool descriptions). A caller tool with the same name but a different definition is sent under an alias (such as `read_client`), consistently in declarations, history and forced choices, and restored in the response.","locale":"en"},"13525":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-50","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The anonymous lane maps `exec_command`, `write_stdin` and `kill_session` to `terminal_execute`, `terminal_send` and `terminal_stop`, avoiding the upstream's `FreeUsageLimitError` rejection of that tool combination. Descriptions, parameters and execution behavior are preserved. History and forced choices use the same mapping, and responses restore the caller's original names. Numeric suffixes resolve collisions with existing caller tools. API-key accounts do not use this mapping.","locale":"en"},"13526":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-51","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"The caller cannot actually run those two injected tools. When the model calls only tools the caller did not offer, the gateway answers it with `unsupported call: <name>` and asks again in the same session, for at most two rounds; if the model keeps calling them, the request fails with a 502 error. The caller sees only the text and calls to its own tools.","locale":"en"},"13527":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-52","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"When the caller sets `tool_choice: \"none\"`, the field is left out of the upstream request and the gateway makes sure no tool call reaches the caller.","locale":"en"},"13528":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-53","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#protocol-handling","content":"Accounts with an API key skip all of this tool handling; the caller's tools are sent as declared.","locale":"en"},"13529":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-54","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"These IDs use the thinking menus declared by the reference implementation; other IDs follow the shared capability table (see Model behaviour).","locale":"en"},"13530":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-55","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Model","locale":"en"},"13531":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-56","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Levels","locale":"en"},"13532":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-57","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"13533":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-58","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Thinking can be switched off","locale":"en"},"13534":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-59","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`deepseek-v4.1-flash-free`","locale":"en"},"13535":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-60","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`disabled`, `low`, `high`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13536":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-61","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13537":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-62","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"13538":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-63","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`glm-5.3-flash-free`","locale":"en"},"13539":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-64","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`low`, `high`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13540":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-65","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13541":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-66","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"No","locale":"en"},"13542":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-67","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free`","locale":"en"},"13543":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-68","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`disabled`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`","locale":"en"},"13544":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-69","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13545":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-70","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"13546":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-71","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`space-bunny-free`","locale":"en"},"13547":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-72","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"13548":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-73","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"13549":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-74","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"No","locale":"en"},"13550":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-75","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#thinking-levels","content":"The level is sent in the `reasoning_effort` field.","locale":"en"},"13551":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-76","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#region-and-probes","content":"The listing names IDs only; it cannot say whether your network exit may use a given model, and the `muse-spark` family is marked as region-sensitive. `opencode` takes part in the default availability probe, so you can confirm with one real request from the **Models** page or `POST /api/v1/probe`; see Model behaviour.","locale":"en"},"13552":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-77","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"Unless switched off, `kilo` runs on a placeholder account (`kilo-public`) and calls the Kilo gateway with no credential. The catalogue keeps only the chat models the upstream marks `isFree: true` (embedding, image, audio and similar rows are excluded); paid IDs only answer 401 without a key. A cold start with an unreachable listing uses the built-in historical fallback list (such as `kilo-auto/free` and `openrouter/free`).","locale":"en"},"13553":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-78","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#anonymous-use-1","content":"The anonymous free pool is protected by no credential at all, and the upstreams behind the free models may log prompts. Do not send sensitive content through it.","locale":"en"},"13554":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-79","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"There are two ways to add a Kilo account:","locale":"en"},"13555":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-80","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"The terminal prints a verification link and a code (in the Web UI, click **Sign in**; the dialog shows the **Verification code**). Confirm in the browser and the account is written to `config.json`. Kilo returns a long-lived key, not a renewable OAuth token, so it is never renewed on a timer.","locale":"en"},"13556":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-81","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"You can also paste an API key in **Add account**, or write it into `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"13557":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-82","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"The account accepts any one of `api_key`, `access_token` or `token`.","locale":"en"},"13558":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-83","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"With a credentialed account, the catalogue includes every chat model the account can see; `options.free_only: true` keeps it to free models.","locale":"en"},"13559":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-84","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#signing-in-with-a-key-or-a-device-code","content":"As with `opencode`, once the channel has accounts the anonymous placeholder is no longer added; an account with no credential calls anonymously.","locale":"en"},"13560":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-85","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Requests use OpenAI Chat Completions: `max_completion_tokens` becomes `max_tokens`, `developer` messages become `system`, `strict` is removed from tool definitions, and `store` and `reasoning_effort` are dropped.","locale":"en"},"13561":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-86","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Thinking levels come from the capabilities each listing row declares and are sent as `reasoning: {\"effort\": ...}`; switching thinking off sends `reasoning: {\"enabled\": false}`.","locale":"en"},"13562":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-87","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Models under `stepfun/`, `liquid/` and `thinkingmachines/` require thinking, and `kilo-auto/free` and `openrouter/free` accept the parameter but keep thinking, so their menus have no off level.","locale":"en"},"13563":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-88","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#request-handling-and-thinking-levels","content":"Kilo is not part of the default availability probe: the anonymous listing is already the free pool's verdict.","locale":"en"},"13564":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous-89","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-anonymous#verification-scope","content":"`tests/core/test_opencode_lane.py`, `tests/core/test_pi_free_parity.py` and the protocol tests cover local regressions; they do not replace a successful request from a particular network exit. Model availability, regional limits and quota are settled by the upstream's current answers or an explicit probe.","locale":"en"},"13565":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"page","content":"Cloud platforms","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","locale":"en"},"13566":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"Connect Azure OpenAI, Cloudflare Workers AI and AI Gateway, the Gemini Developer API, Vertex AI and Amazon Bedrock, plus the two special protocols Radius and TypeSafe: credentials, account fields, protocol selection and limits.","locale":"en"},"13567":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Optional dependencies","locale":"en"},"13568":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Azure OpenAI (`azure`)","locale":"en"},"13569":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Cloudflare (`cloudflare-workers-ai`, `cloudflare-ai-gateway`)","locale":"en"},"13570":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"Gemini Developer API (`google`)","locale":"en"},"13571":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Google Vertex AI (`google-vertex`)","locale":"en"},"13572":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Amazon Bedrock (`amazon-bedrock`)","locale":"en"},"13573":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"Radius (`radius`)","locale":"en"},"13574":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"TypeSafe (`typesafe`)","locale":"en"},"13575":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Protocol selection","locale":"en"},"13576":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"Every channel on this page needs your own cloud account. Pick the channel ID that matches the upstream endpoint, protocol, credentials and plan; a similar model name does not make credentials interchangeable. For example, `gemini` is Code Assist (see Free stations), `google` is the Gemini Developer API and `google-vertex` is Vertex AI; `amazon-bedrock` and `bedrock-mantle` are two services configured separately.","locale":"en"},"13577":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","content":"The JSON below are fragments of `providers` in the data folder's `config.json`, not files to place next to the program. Replace the placeholders and enable only the channels you use; restart after editing the file. **Add account** under **Channels** takes effect immediately, and its form lists the fields for each **Authentication method**.","locale":"en"},"13578":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Vertex default credentials and service accounts need Google's auth library; Bedrock needs the AWS SDK:","locale":"en"},"13579":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#optional-dependencies","content":"Vertex API-key mode and ordinary HTTP channels need neither. A missing dependency or credential produces a clear error; it never falls back to anonymous access.","locale":"en"},"13580":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Give the Azure resource name, the key, the public model IDs and the deployment mapping:","locale":"en"},"13581":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"13582":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"13583":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`resource`","locale":"en"},"13584":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"The resource name; the default root is `https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1`.","locale":"en"},"13585":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`base_url`","locale":"en"},"13586":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Optional; replaces the address built from `resource`.","locale":"en"},"13587":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`api_key`","locale":"en"},"13588":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Sent in the `api-key` header.","locale":"en"},"13589":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"13590":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"The public model IDs (required in the Web UI form).","locale":"en"},"13591":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`deployments`","locale":"en"},"13592":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Maps model IDs to deployment names. The upstream request's `model` becomes the deployment name, while capabilities and protocol are still looked up by the public ID.","locale":"en"},"13593":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"13594":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#azure-openai-azure","content":"Responses by default; `\"chat\"` selects Chat Completions.","locale":"en"},"13595":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Workers AI needs an account ID; AI Gateway also needs a gateway ID:","locale":"en"},"13596":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"**Workers AI**: the address is `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account_id>/ai/v1`. The catalogue comes from Cloudflare's native model search, keeping text-generation tasks only; `models` declared on the account replaces it.","locale":"en"},"13597":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"**AI Gateway**: Chat requests go to `https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<account_id>/<gateway_id>/compat` with the key in the `cf-aig-authorization` header. The Messages protocol uses the gateway's `/anthropic/v1/messages` instead, and Responses uses `/openai/responses`.","locale":"en"},"13598":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#cloudflare-cloudflare-workers-ai-cloudflare-ai-gateway","content":"Both accept `base_url` in place of the built address. Set `protocol` or `model_protocols` (see the end of this page) only for a protocol the upstream really supports.","locale":"en"},"13599":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The default is native Gemini streaming (`generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta`) with the key in `x-goog-api-key`. `protocol: \"chat\"` switches to Google's OpenAI-compatible Chat endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13600":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The catalogue is the native model list (paginated), keeping models that support `generateContent`; `models` can declare it instead.","locale":"en"},"13601":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"The native translation keeps function calls and their opaque thought signatures, so multi-turn tool use replays correctly.","locale":"en"},"13602":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"Thinking is set with `reasoning_effort`, or with Google's own `thinking_config` (not both at once).","locale":"en"},"13603":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#gemini-developer-api-google","content":"This channel does not use the Code Assist sign-in of the `gemini` channel.","locale":"en"},"13604":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Use one of three authentication methods: an API key, application default credentials (ADC), or a service-account file.","locale":"en"},"13605":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Authentication method","locale":"en"},"13606":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"Account fields","locale":"en"},"13607":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**API key**","locale":"en"},"13608":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`api_key`; optional `project`, `location`","locale":"en"},"13609":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**Google default credentials**","locale":"en"},"13610":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-44","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`auth: \"adc\"`, `project` (required), optional `location`","locale":"en"},"13611":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-45","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"**Google service account file**","locale":"en"},"13612":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-46","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`service_account_file` (a path on the server), `project` (required), optional `location`","locale":"en"},"13613":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-47","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"ADC and service accounts need `hoshimi[google]`, and the credentials must be visible to the process running Hoshimi. Missing or expired credentials are reported as an error; there is no silent switch to another method.","locale":"en"},"13614":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-48","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"`location` defaults to `global`; a region name (such as `us-central1`) selects the regional endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13615":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-49","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"The default is the native Gemini protocol; `protocol: \"chat\"` connects to Vertex's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which requires `project`.","locale":"en"},"13616":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-50","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#google-vertex-ai-google-vertex","content":"The catalogue comes from Google's publisher model list; the models your account is authorised for can be declared with `models` instead.","locale":"en"},"13617":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-51","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Uses Bedrock ConverseStream. Every authentication method needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`.","locale":"en"},"13618":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-52","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Authentication method","locale":"en"},"13619":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-53","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"Account fields","locale":"en"},"13620":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-54","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"**AWS default credentials**","locale":"en"},"13621":