],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"SDK modes can list the text foundation models that support streaming; a bearer key is not authorised for the control-plane model listing, so declare `models`. Account-specific inference profile IDs or ARNs should also be declared explicitly.","locale":"en"},"13630":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-64","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"The adapter translates messages, supported images, tool calls and results, usage and thinking signatures; a `thinking` object in the request body is passed upstream as an additional model field. Not every Bedrock model supports every feature, and model access is still decided by your AWS account.","locale":"en"},"13631":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-65","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#amazon-bedrock-amazon-bedrock","content":"`bedrock-mantle` is another service: Bedrock's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, configured separately with a bearer key and its own address (default `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/v1`):","locale":"en"},"13632":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-66","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"Radius uses a dedicated pi-messages protocol rather than a generic Chat endpoint.","locale":"en"},"13633":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-67","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"**Adding an account**: `hoshimi login radius` (device-code sign-in, renewable token), or an API key in **Add account**.","locale":"en"},"13634":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-68","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#radius-radius","content":"**Models**: the inference address and model list are read from the gateway's `/v1/config`. The account's `gateway` field replaces the default gateway `https://radius.pi.dev`.","locale":"en"},"13635":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-69","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"TypeSafe is a classification service, not a chat model: its models do not appear in `/v1/models` and cannot be used for chat.","locale":"en"},"13636":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-70","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`classifiers` is optional and defaults to `[\"jev-latest\"]`. `GET /v1/classifiers` lists the available classifiers, and classification requests go to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"13637":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-71","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`model` comes from `/v1/classifiers`, in the form `typesafe/<classifier>`.","locale":"en"},"13638":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-72","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"`state` is an object and `questions` a non-empty object; their contents are passed to TypeSafe as they are.","locale":"en"},"13639":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-73","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"Each question's `type` is `bool`, `score` or `choice`. `bool` returns a probability; `score` and `choice` return a score or a choice with its confidence.","locale":"en"},"13640":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-74","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#typesafe-typesafe","content":"Image input is not supported. The full field definitions are in the running server's `/docs`.","locale":"en"},"13641":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-75","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Channels such as `azure` and `cloudflare-ai-gateway` speak several protocols. The protocol for a model is decided in this order:","locale":"en"},"13642":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-76","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The protocol named for the model in the channel option `options.model_protocols`, for example `{\"claude-sonnet\": \"messages\"}`.","locale":"en"},"13643":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-77","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The account's `protocol` field.","locale":"en"},"13644":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-78","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Protocol information carried by the model's catalogue row.","locale":"en"},"13645":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-79","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The channel's default protocol.","locale":"en"},"13646":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-80","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"The values are `chat`, `responses` and `messages`, with the aliases `openai-completions`, `openai-responses` and `anthropic-messages` also accepted. `google` and `google-vertex` use `gemini` or `chat`. Set these only for protocols the upstream really supports. More protocol-related options are in Local and compatible endpoints.","locale":"en"},"13647":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud-81","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-cloud","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-cloud#protocol-selection","content":"Availability has to be confirmed with a real request from a configured account; this page describes the configuration behaviour that is implemented. The full service mapping is in the provider inventory.","locale":"en"},"13648":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","type":"page","content":"Provider inventory","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","locale":"en"},"13649":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Where each provider definition comes from, its endpoint and protocol, how it authenticates, and how far Hoshimi covers it. Generated.","locale":"en"},"13650":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source snapshots: pi `482c1381a`, pi-free `2da9909`, free-claude-code `f919f46d` (2026-10-19).","locale":"en"},"13651":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"This page is generated by `scripts/generate_provider_inventory.py` from `hoshimi/core/provider_sources.py`; do not edit it by hand. Reference repositories are not runtime dependencies.","locale":"en"},"13652":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Deduplication uses endpoint + protocol + credential types + plan. Existing native lanes and all 22 agg presets are retained.","locale":"en"},"13653":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"`native` and `agg` record an existing entry point, not live endpoint verification or complete upstream parity. `partial` has protocol gaps; `planned` is not registered yet.","locale":"en"},"13654":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"MiniMax API uses `minimax-api` to preserve the Agent service. Gemini Developer API uses `google`, separate from Code Assist `gemini`. The legacy `openai-codex` source maps to the existing `codex` account namespace. TypeSafe is classification, not chat.","locale":"en"},"13655":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source snapshots and coverage labels do not establish current live availability. See Providers for registration, plans and authentication.","locale":"en"},"13656":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"13657":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Source ID","locale":"en"},"13658":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Hoshimi ID","locale":"en"},"13659":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Endpoint","locale":"en"},"13660":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Protocol","locale":"en"},"13661":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","content":"Authentication","locale":"en"},"13662":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-inventory","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/d