ends","content":"`http://localhost:1234/v1`","locale":"en"},"14847":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`/v1/models`; loaded models' context lengths from `/api/v0/models`","locale":"en"},"14848":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`ollama`","locale":"en"},"14849":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"Ollama","locale":"en"},"14850":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`http://localhost:11434/v1`","locale":"en"},"14851":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`/api/tags`; capabilities and context lengths from `/api/show`","locale":"en"},"14852":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`llamacpp`","locale":"en"},"14853":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"LLaMA.cpp","locale":"en"},"14854":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`http://localhost:8080/v1`","locale":"en"},"14855":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"`/v1/models`","locale":"en"},"14856":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#local-backends","content":"Hoshimi does not scan local ports: it contacts these addresses only after you add an account and the channel is enabled.","locale":"en"},"14857":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Open **Channels**, find **LM Studio**, **LLaMA.cpp** or **Ollama** under the **Not set up** filter, and click **Add account**.","locale":"en"},"14858":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"The authentication method is **Local server (optional key)**. **API base URL (optional)** is pre-filled with the default address; change it if your server is on another port.","locale":"en"},"14859":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Enter an **API key** if the local server requires one, otherwise leave it blank; restrict the models in **Model IDs** if you want. Click **Save account**.","locale":"en"},"14860":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Without `base_url` the default address is used; an account can be just an `id`.","locale":"en"},"14861":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"`base_url` must be an HTTP(S) address without a user name and password, query or fragment; `/v1` is appended when it is missing.","locale":"en"},"14862":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-35","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"When `api_key` (or `access_token`, `token`) has a value it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer`; otherwise no auth header is sent.","locale":"en"},"14863":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-36","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-a-local-server","content":"Local models are never marked free (`free` is `null`).","locale":"en"},"14864":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-37","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**LM Studio**: reads the actual context length of loaded models (cached for 30 seconds). Before a request it makes a rough check: when a quarter of the messages' JSON byte size plus `max_tokens` exceeds the loaded context, it answers 400 at once (`LM Studio request exceeds this model's loaded context window`). For requests close to the limit, the server's own tokenizer still decides. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`; `xhigh` and `max` become `high`).","locale":"en"},"14865":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-38","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**Ollama**: reads each model's capabilities, keeps only models that can do completion or tool calls, and marks vision, thinking and tool support from them; the context length is the largest one in the model info. A model whose details fail to load is still listed. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`, `xhigh` becomes `max`).","locale":"en"},"14866":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-39","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"**llama.cpp**: the thinking switch maps to chat-template parameters: `enable_thinking` and `thinking` in `chat_template_kwargs`. A request that already sets `enable_thinking` cannot also name a thinking level.","locale":"en"},"14867":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-40","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#how-each-backend-is-handled","content":"A thinking menu (including the off level `none`) appears only when the catalogue says the model thinks.","locale":"en"},"14868":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-41","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#conventional-api-services","content":"These services' addresses, protocols and catalogue endpoints are built in, so an account needs only a key.","locale":"en"},"14869":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-42","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"Pick the service in **Channels** and click **Add account**. The authentication method is **API key**: fill in the **API key**, and optionally **API base URL (optional)** and **Model IDs**; OpenAI, xAI and Vercel AI Gateway also offer a **Protocol** choice. Some services also support browser or device-code sign-in:","locale":"en"},"14870":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-43","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"14871":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-44","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"Sign-in","locale":"en"},"14872":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-45","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"Resulting credential","locale":"en"},"14873":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-46","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#adding-an-account","content":"`anthropic`","locale":"en"},"14874":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-47","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text",