,"locale":"en"},"15228":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"page","content":"NVIDIA NIM","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","locale":"en"},"15229":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","content":"Connect NVIDIA-hosted NIM models with an API key: adding the account, choosing models, catalogue filtering, and the request translations the adapter makes for NIM.","locale":"en"},"15230":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Adding an account","locale":"en"},"15231":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#choosing-a-model","content":"Choosing a model","locale":"en"},"15232":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"Catalogue","locale":"en"},"15233":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Request translations","locale":"en"},"15234":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","content":"The `nvidia` channel connects to NVIDIA's hosted NIM inference service (`https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1`) over OpenAI Chat Completions. An account needs only an NVIDIA API key.","locale":"en"},"15235":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Open **Channels** › **NVIDIA NIM**, click **Add account**, enter the **API key** and click **Save account**. The account takes effect immediately.","locale":"en"},"15236":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Find the configuration file with `hoshimi config path` and add:","locale":"en"},"15237":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Restart after editing the file.","locale":"en"},"15238":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"The account also accepts `access_token` in place of `api_key`, and `models` on the account declares a model list in place of the live catalogue; the channel option `options.base_url` replaces the default address. This upstream key is a different thing from the gateway's own model API key and management key; see Security.","locale":"en"},"15239":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#choosing-a-model","content":"Use `nvidia/<model-id>` to select this channel explicitly. When the model ID itself contains a slash, the `nvidia/` prefix makes sure the request lands here rather than on an earlier channel in the routing order:","locale":"en"},"15240":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"The adapter reads the model list live and excludes recognised non-chat tasks: embeddings (`embed`), rerankers (`rerank`), `nvclip`, reward scorers (`-reward`), detectors (`-detector`), document parsers (`nemotron-parse`) and `gliner`. This is a task filter, not an outage list.","locale":"en"},"15241":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"A model being listed does not prove there is quota for it or that inference will succeed. `nvidia` takes part in the default availability probe, so you can confirm with one real request from the **Models** page or `POST /api/v1/probe`; see Model behaviour. Capability metadata and account options follow the same model rules.","locale":"en"},"15242":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"NIM does not accept some OpenAI fields, so the adapter changes requests before sending them:","locale":"en"},"15243":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Translation","locale":"en"},"15244":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Details","locale":"en"},"15245":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Removed fields","locale":"en"},"15246":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`store`, `reasoning_effort`, `reasoning`, `prompt_cache_retention`","locale":"en"},"15247":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`max_completion_tokens`","locale":"en"},"15248":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Becomes `max_tokens` when no `max_tokens` was given","locale":"en"},"15249