pters implement. Each station decides its own free allowance, models and rules, and can change them at any time; the built-in model lists are only a fallback for when the station's listing cannot be reached. What actually works is whatever the station answers now.","locale":"en"},"15282":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Open **Channels** and pick the station from the list (stations without accounts are under the **Not set up** filter).","locale":"en"},"15283":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Click **Sign in**. The dialog goes through **Request a link**, **Finish in the browser** and **Signed in**, and opens the station's login page in a new tab.","locale":"en"},"15284":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"For device-code stations, the dialog shows a **Verification code**; enter it on the authorization page.","locale":"en"},"15285":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"When the browser is not on the machine running Hoshimi, paste the address the browser finally lands on into **Authorization code or callback URL** and click **Submit code**.","locale":"en"},"15286":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"On success it prints `Signed into <channel> as <account id>.` and the account is written to `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"15287":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"A sign-in waits at most 10 minutes. In the Web UI you can cancel it; a callback that arrives after cancelling does not save an account.","locale":"en"},"15288":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Signing in again as the same station identity updates the existing account rather than adding another.","locale":"en"},"15289":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Stations that need a local callback listen only on `127.0.0.1` (or `localhost`) for the duration of the sign-in, never on a public interface. When the browser is on another machine, paste the callback with `--manual` or the Web UI's **Authorization code or callback URL**. The one flow without manual input (Loomy) has to be finished in a browser on the same machine.","locale":"en"},"15290":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-30","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Channel","locale":"en"},"15291":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-31","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Station","locale":"en"},"15292":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-32","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Sign-in","locale":"en"},"15293":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-33","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Renewal","locale":"en"},"15294":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-34","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"Check-in","locale":"en"},"