\""],[12552,"\"Today\" is the server's local day. The small line on the right is tokens per hour over the last 24 hours. The dot beside the title is the live connection's state (**Live**, **Reconnecting…**, **Offline**): while it is **Live**, the figures move as soon as a call finishes. **Usage** opens the Usage page with charts and every call."],[13434,"\"Upstream key variable\" is the environment variable the station's own tools read their key from, for reference only. Hoshimi reads credentials from `config.json` only and never reads these variables."],[5615,"“上游密钥变量”是该站点官方工具读取密钥的环境变量名，仅供参考。Hoshimi 只从 `config.json` 读取凭据，不会读取这些变量。"],[4731,"“今天”按服务器的本地时间计算。右侧的小折线是最近 24 小时每小时的 Token 量。标题旁的圆点是实时连接的状态（**实时**、**正在重连…**、**离线**）：处于 **实时** 时，调用一结束这些数字就会更新。点 **用量** 打开用量页查看图表和每次调用。"],[4915,"“图片……已略去：没有可读取它的模型”"],[5616,"“无密钥可读目录”只表示能浏览模型列表，这些站点的聊天请求仍然需要密钥。"],[7567,"“续期”指适配器能用续期令牌换新令牌；不支持续期的站点，令牌过期后需要重新登录。“签到”和“余额”见本页末尾。"],[11349,"(Abridged; see `hoshimi/core/login/kilo.py`.) Kilo returns a long-lived key, so the flow invents no `refresh_token` or `expires_at`, which would schedule renewals that do not exist."],[12042,"(Command-line changes apply after the server restarts.) The two anonymous lanes are covered in Anonymous channels."],[4221,"（命令行修改在服务器重启后生效。）两个匿名入口的细节见匿名渠道。"],[3528,"（节选，见 `hoshimi/core/login/kilo.py`。）Kilo 返回的是长期有效的密钥，所以流程不编造 `refresh_token` 或 `expires_at`，免得为它安排根本不存在的续期。"],[9959,"**`HOSHIMI_CONFIG`.** Older releases used it to name the configuration file; it has been removed, and the configuration file is always `<data folder>/config.json`. Leaving it set has no effect."],[2138,"**`HOSHIMI_CONFIG`。** 旧版本用它指定配置文件，已经移除；配置文件总是 `<数据目录>/config.json`。仍然设置着它不会有任何效果。"],[10260,"**`provider/model`**, such as `opencode/big-pickle`, which names the provider. Everything after the first slash is sent as the upstream model name, further slashes included, e.g. `kilo/kilo-auto/free`. Use this form to choose between providers that list the same name."],[9992,"**`serve` options apply to that start only.** For example, `hoshimi serve --port 11000 --access-token …` writes nothing to the configuration file. Precedence: `serve` options, then `config.json`, then the defaults."],[2171,"**`serve` 的选项只作用于这一次启动。** 例如 `hoshimi serve --port 11000 --access-token …` 不会写入配置文件。优先级为：`serve` 的选项 ＞ `config.json` ＞ 默认值。"],[13029,"**24 hours**"],[13060,"**24 hours** and **Day** are by the hour; hours of today still to come are drawn faint, not as a fall to zero."],[5210,"**24 小时**"],[5241,"**24 小时** 和 **单日** 按小时显示；今天还没到的小时以浅色显示，不算作下降。"],[627,"**24 小时** 和单日视图"],[13061,"**7 days**, **30 days** and **90 days** are by the day. Click a day's bar to open that day hour by hour (**Choose a day to see its hours**)."],[13032,"**7 days**, **30 days**, **90 days**"],[5213,"**7 天**、**30 天**、**90 天**"],[5242,"**7 天**、**30 天**、**90 天** 按天显示。点某一天的柱子，直接打开那一天的逐小时视图（**选择某一天可查看逐小时用量**）。"],[630,"**7 天**、**30 天**、**90 天** 视图"],[8419,"**A client disconnecting is not a failure**: when the caller hangs up mid-answer, the gateway did serve the call, and the record counts as a success."],[13284,"**A fixed port**: when a client needs a fixed address, use `--strict-port` (or `server.strict_port: true` in the configuration). Only the requested port is tried, and if it is taken the command ends with exit code 3."],[8118,"**A request that has already sent content to the caller is never replayed automatically**, so the same answer never arrives twice."],[9991,"**A running server needs a restart to see changes.** `hoshimi config set` and `hoshimi login` only write `config.json`; a running server does not reread the file. Restart the server after such changes, or make them in the Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages instead, where they apply at once (except the listening address and port)."],[12492,"**Abilities**"],[15391,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `client_profile`, `account_id`."],[15411,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `device_id`, `machine_id`, `uid`."],[15473,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `device_id`, `office_identity` (the organisation code, sent as `X-Org-Code`)."],[15477,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `uuid`."],[15458,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`; the sign-in also saves `user_id`, `enterprise_id` and others, which the balance query uses."],[15406,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`."],[15441,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `security_oauth_token`, `refresh_token`, `machine_id`."],[15469,"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `userid`, `expires_at`."],[15453,"**Account fields**: `personal_token`, `access_token`, `security_oauth_token`, `refresh_token`, `uid` / `user_id`, `nickname`, `email`, `machine_id`, `expires_at`."],[15401,"**Account fields**: `zcode_jwt` (or `access_token`), `device_mid`."],[12387,"**Account ID (optional)**: left blank, the gateway names the account. A name the channel already has is refused."],[13072,"**Account**"],[12364,"**Add account**"],[13633,"**Adding an account**: `hoshimi login radius` (device-code sign-in, renewable token), or an API key in **Add account**."],[15484,"**Adding an account**: create an API key in the bigmodel.cn console, then **Add account** under **Channels** › **Zhipu GLM (BigModel)**, or write it into `config.json`."],[13597,"**AI Gateway**: Chat requests go to `https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<account_id>/<gateway_id>/compat` with the key in the `cf-aig-authorization` header. The Messages protocol uses the gateway's `/anthropic/v1/messages` instead, and Responses uses `/openai/responses`."],[5778,"**AI Gateway**：Chat 请求发往 `https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<account_id>/<gateway_id>/compat`，密钥以 `cf-aig-authorization` 头发送。选择 Messages 协议时改走网关的 `/anthropic/v1/messages`，Responses 协议走 `/openai/responses`。"],[12238,"**Allow**: run this call."],[12943,"**Allowed CIDRs**"],[12946,"**Allowed hosts**"],[12949,"**Allowed origins**"],[12220,"**Allowed**: the call runs. Opening its card shows \"Allowed by *model*\", with the risk and the rationale when given."],[12293,"**Always allow** removes the question for the rest of the chat (until the server restarts), and in **Automatic review** skips the reviewer too. Prefer **Allow** for anything you want to check each time."],[12225,"**Always allow**, given by you earlier in the chat, still holds: the calls it covers run without asking anyone, the reviewer included."],[12239,"**Always allow**: run this call, and calls like it in this chat, without asking again. \"Like it\" means the same tool switch, and inside versus outside the workspace counts separately: always allowing edits in the workspace does not allow edits outside it. The permission lasts until the server restarts, and is forgotten when the chat is deleted."],[9932,"**Amazon Bedrock with AWS default credentials** (no access keys or profile in the account): the AWS SDK's default credential chain, such as `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_PROFILE` and the shared configuration files. Needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`."],[2111,"**Amazon Bedrock，AWS 默认凭据**（账户里没有写访问密钥或 profile 时）：AWS SDK 的默认凭据链，例如 `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`、`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`、`AWS_PROFILE` 和共享配置文件。需要 `hoshimi[bedrock]`。"],[11668,"**Analytics**: the site uses Umami, loaded in production builds only and counted on the two site domains alone; local previews are not counted."],[4740,"**Anthropic Messages**"],[5264,"**Anthropic Messages**"],[12561,"**Anthropic Messages**"],[13083,"**Anthropic Messages**"],[11743,"**Anthropic Messages**: `tests/api/test_native_messages.py` drives the gateway with the official Anthropic SDK's JSON and stream helpers (the SDK is in the `dev` extra), against a local mock transport, so no real credentials are needed. `tests/api/test_messages_heartbeat.py` separately checks the heartbeat timing, that heartbeats never split a whole SSE frame, and that the upstream is released when the client goes away. To try a configured gateway with real Claude Code, see Claude Code."],[3922,"**Anthropic Messages**：`tests/api/test_native_messages.py` 用官方 Anthropic SDK（`dev` 附加依赖中）的 JSON 与流式辅助函数访问网关，上游是本地的模拟传输，所以不需要真实凭据。`tests/api/test_messages_heartbeat.py` 单独检查心跳的时机、心跳不会切开完整的 SSE 帧，以及客户端断开时释放上游。用真实的 Claude Code 试用一个已配置的网关，见 Claude Code。"],[13285,"**Any free port**: `--port 0` lets the system pick one."],[13607,"**API key**"],[13626,"**API key**"],[5788,"**API 密钥**"],[5807,"**API 密钥**"],[13074,"**API**"],[11508,"**API**: `python -m hoshimi serve --no-open --no-ui --port 10600 --strict-port`, with the repository root first on `PYTHONPATH`, so the code in the working tree is what runs."],[3687,"**API**：`python -m hoshimi serve --no-open --no-ui --port 10600 --strict-port`，仓库根目录放在 `PYTHONPATH` 最前面，所以运行的是工作区里的代码。"],[12231,"**Apply these changes?**"],[12662,"**Archive** puts a chat away without deleting it. **Archived chats**, at the foot of the list, shows the archive; **Restore** brings a chat back, and so does sending a new message in it. **Back to chats** returns to the list. Archiving the open chat starts a new one."],[12722,"**as a reply begins**, once the conversation has reached 85% of the window (`playground.compact_threshold`), or sooner when what is left could not hold a reply;"],[12194,"**Ask first** (`ask`)"],[12990,"**Ask first** (the default): media a Playground reply points to on another site waits behind a button naming the site; **Always load**"],[12289,"**Ask first** is the only mode where you see every command and every file change before it happens. Read each one before you allow it."],[12197,"**Ask outside the workspace** (`workspace`)"],[12291,"**Ask outside the workspace** runs any command without asking. A command is not confined to the workspace, so in this mode a model can change or delete files anywhere the user can, and reach your network. Use it only with a model and a task you trust."],[12195,"**Ask**"],[11889,"**Authentication**: the `api` middleware adds `Authorization: Bearer <access key>` to every request. The key is kept in the browser's `localStorage` (`hoshimi:access-token`); when the server answers 401 with `auth_required`, the interface opens the access-key dialog."],[8691,"**Authentication**: with a tool access key (`server.access_token`) set, every endpoint except `GET /api/v1/app/health` needs `Authorization: Bearer <tool-access-key>`; a missing or wrong key answers `401` (`auth_required`). `x-api-key` and the model API key do not work here."],[12803,"**Auto detect (system language)**, English, 简体中文, 日本語"],[12192,"**Auto review**"],[12464,"**Automatic (environment proxy)**"],[12956,"**Automatic (environment proxy)**"],[12191,"**Automatic review** (`review`, default)"],[12891,"**Automatic review** (`review`)"],[12290,"**Automatic review** is a model's judgement. It can be wrong both ways, allowing what it should not and denying what is fine, and it can be fooled. It is a safeguard, not a sandbox."],[12892,"**Automatic review**: a model judges commands, file changes and anything outside the workspace, and denies what's risky; you're asked when it can't decide; **Ask first** (`ask`): before commands, file changes and anything outside the workspace; **Ask outside the workspace** (`workspace`, formerly `auto`): commands and changes in the workspace run, reads and changes outside it ask; **Full access** (`full`): nothing asks. Calls that need leave are judged by the review model, or wait in the chat for your approval; the shield in a chat's composer changes the mode for that chat alone"],[12899,"**Automatic** (`auto`)"],[12494,"**Availability**"],[12502,"**Availability**: appears after a probe and offers only the verdicts that occur, plus **Not probed**; **Any verdict** to undo."],[12516,"**Available**"],[13624,"**AWS access keys**"],[13620,"**AWS default credentials**"],[13622,"**AWS profile**"],[5805,"**AWS 访问密钥**"],[5803,"**AWS 配置档案**"],[5801,"**AWS 默认凭据**"],[12135,"**Background commands**"],[12875,"**Background commands**"],[12011,"**Background timers.** Credential renewal (every 30 minutes) and daily check-in start with the server, each with a line in the log. The server also asks PyPI in the background whether a newer release exists. All three can be turned off, see Configuration."],[15390,"**Balance**: needs the account's `account_id` (a `usr-…` value, saved automatically at sign-in)."],[15395,"**Balance**: shows the remaining share of the five-hour and weekly quota windows, not credits."],[15491,"**Balance**: supporting stations can report a balance or quota. Separately, the gateway reads the remaining allowance passively from the rate-limit headers of every station response and shows it in the channel's **Allowance** section, with no extra requests."],[15463,"**Benefit models**: requests for models in `options.benefit_models` (default `glm-5.3-flash` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash`) carry a `maas_type: benefit` header; if the station rejects the header, the request is retried without it."],[12723,"**between a reply's rounds of tool calls**, so a long agent run keeps going;"],[15447,"**Body encoding**: chat bodies use Qoder's custom Base64 (`Encode=1`) — substituted alphabet, `$` padding, and the three blocks rotated. `region/endpoints` answers in the same encoding."],[12715,"**Branch in new chat** (on a reply) copies the chat up to that reply into a new chat and opens it (\"Opened in a new chat\"). The new chat keeps the title, the model and effort, and the chat's approval mode; the original is untouched. Use it to take a conversation in two directions without switching versions back and forth."],[13065,"**Breakdown** groups usage four ways, chosen by tab:"],[15444,"**Browser login (international only)**: `hoshimi login qodercli` without `--manual` opens Qoder's device authorization page and polls for the approval, while the same session still accepts a pasted PAT — whichever answers first wins. The China edition has no device flow. A browser credential carries no PAT, so it renews against `{center}/algo/api/v3/user/refresh_token` instead of re-exchanging."],[15451,"**Busy models**: `10605` with `serviceAvailable` is the scheduler's answer. A ready request is re-sent after the hinted delay (bounded, with a fresh `request_id`); a genuinely queued one is returned as a rate limit carrying the wait, so the caller can schedule it."],[13049,"**Cache hit rate**"],[12548,"**Cache hit**"],[7979,"**Cached for 5 minutes**: a channel's listing is not fetched again within 5 minutes."],[13105,"**Cached**"],[12546,"**Calls**"],[13052,"**Calls**"],[12233,"**Change files outside the workspace?**"],[9958,"**Channel key variables.** The **Key env** column of `hoshimi stations` (such as `ZENMUX_API_KEY`) and other key variables upstream tools use are not read. Channel credentials come only from the accounts in `config.json`, so there is no second source."],[12052,"**Channels**"],[13160,"**Channels**"],[12067,"**Channels** → choose the station → **Sign in** or **Add account**"],[11899,"**Charts**: series take the eight colour-blind-checked slots `--app-chart-1` to `--app-chart-8` in a fixed order; charts carry a legend and a hover / focus tooltip."],[5260,"**Chat Completions**"],[13079,"**Chat Completions**"],[12557,"**Chat Completions** (OpenAI)"],[4736,"**Chat Completions**（OpenAI）"],[13470,"**Chat-model filters**: listings from known stations drop image, video, embedding, transcription and other non-chat rows, with a filter written per station; a row missing the relevant fields is kept, so a station's schema change does not empty its catalogue. LLM7 is filtered on its own `model_type` field."],[12419,"**Check in all** above the list claims for every account of every channel at once; **Claim now** in a channel's ⋮ menu claims for that channel only. Stations usually answer \"already claimed\" to a second try, so clicking again does no harm."],[15405,"**Check-in and balance**: daily credits are claimed by the UTC+8 calendar day; the balance is the sum of what remains in each credit pack."],[15410,"**Check-in and balance**: the device identity is derived from the account's `uid`; an account without `uid` cannot check in."],[15439,"**Check-in**: claiming the campaign reward needs the machine token cached by the Qoder desktop client. The adapter looks for `Qoder` (or `Qoder CN`) `/SharedClientCache/cache/machine_token.json` under `%APPDATA%`, `~/Library/Application Support` or `~/.config`; on a machine without Qoder desktop installed, check-in fails. The station refreshes its campaigns at 10:00 UTC+8."],[15464,"**Check-in**: claims the \"daily login\" campaign; token-billed and non-credit-billed accounts are outside the campaign."],[15457,"**Check-in**: only CodeBuddy has a daily check-in; the WorkBuddy international station has no check-in endpoint, though its balance still works."],[15490,"**Check-in**: starts 30 seconds after boot and claims once a day per account, by the UTC+8 calendar day, one account after another (stations rate-limit parallel requests). A station answering \"already claimed today\" counts as done. To check in by hand, use **Check in all** at the top of **Channels**, or **Claim now** in a channel's menu; **Recent check-ins** shows the channel's latest results."],[11901,"**Choices**: one choice out of a few (a list filter, a report range) is a `SegmentedControl`, which becomes a select where it does not fit; days are picked with `DatePicker`."],[13085,"**Classification**"],[13093,"**Click a row in the breakdown and the call list below shows only that row's calls**; a chip with its name appears above the list, and clicking it clears the filter."],[13124,"**Client HTTP request / response**: method, path, headers, status and JSON or SSE body."],[12983,"**Colour**"],[11896,"**Colour**: every colour role is generated from one seed colour (`theme/scheme.ts`, `#5267d8` by default, which users can change) with Material's Tonal Spot scheme, at standard, medium or high contrast. `theme/applyTheme.ts` writes them as `--md-sys-color-*` on `:root` and follows the system's light or dark setting."],[13471,"**CommandCode**: models whose name starts with `claude-` go to Anthropic Messages (`<base_url>/messages`); the station's vision and reasoning tables act as defaults, and account declarations win."],[5652,"**CommandCode**：`claude-` 开头的模型改走 Anthropic Messages（`<base_url>/messages`）；站点的视觉和思考能力表作为默认值，账号声明优先。"],[11669,"**Comments**: every documentation page ends with Giscus comments (`components/docs-comments.tsx`, `lib/giscus.ts`, as rvc-next's site), backed by this repository's GitHub Discussions in the \"Comment\" category. Each page has one discussion thread, mapped `specific` on the page path with the base path, the language prefix and the slashes around it dropped (`docs/<slug>`), so a page's Chinese and English versions, on the main site (at the root) and the backup (under `/Hoshimi/`) alike, share one thread. The comments follow the site's theme and language, which are posted to the loaded comments frame rather than reloading it."],[12851,"**Compact at (% of the window)**"],[12766,"**Compact at**"],[12762,"**Compact long chats automatically**"],[12847,"**Compact long chats automatically**"],[13028,"**Compared with the day before**"],[13025,"**Compared with yesterday up to this time**"],[12997,"**Config file**"],[12740,"**Context compacted** above the reply"],[12490,"**Context**"],[12985,"**Contrast**"],[13001,"**Copy config path** copies the config file's path to the clipboard. With no tool access key there is also **API reference**, which opens the server's own API documentation (`/docs`). Where the data folder is and what is in it: Data folder and paths; on the command line, `hoshimi config path` prints the config file's path."],[12531,"**Copy the model id**: copies the id to the clipboard, for the `model` of a client."],[12439,"**Credential refusals**"],[12973,"**Credential renewal**"],[15461,"**Credentials**: the result is a temporary AK/SK pair and security token with an expiry. The adapter does not renew them; sign in again when they expire."],[15467,"**Credentials**: the session lasts about 14 days and the adapter does not renew it; sign in again when it expires."],[15452,"**Credits**: request-level `usage.credits`, `original_credits` and `billable` are preserved, and `charged_credits` is zero for a non-billable call. **Balance** reads the account-wide period quota (personal, add-on and organization buckets); there is no daily check-in on this path."],[7633,"**Credits**：保留请求级 `usage.credits`、`original_credits`、`billable`，非计费请求的 `charged_credits` 为 0。**余额** 读取账号级周期额度（个人、加量、组织三个桶）；此路径没有每日签到。"],[12969,"**Daily check-in**"],[12995,"**Data directory**"],[12999,"**Database**"],[13026,"**Day** (a past day)"],[13023,"**Day** (today)"],[12257,"**Declined**"],[12582,"**Default model**"],[12804,"**Default model**"],[12663,"**Delete** asks first, then removes the chat, its messages and the attachments only it carried, for good. A reply working in it is stopped first, and any background commands its tools started are stopped."],[12259,"**Denied by review**"],[12221,"**Denied**: the card shows **Denied by review** and opens to show \"Denied by *model* · high risk — *rationale*\". The model is told the rationale and not to work around it: no workaround, indirect execution or other tool to the same end. It goes on only with a materially safer alternative, or if you explicitly approve after being told the risk; otherwise it stops and asks you."],[12240,"**Deny**: skip it. The model is told you declined and not to try again unless you ask, and the card shows **Declined**."],[12466,"**Direct**"],[12958,"**Direct**"],[11985,"**Documentation**"],[12707,"**Download** saves the image; **Open in a new tab** opens it on its own (not offered for images written into the reply, which browsers do not open as pages)."],[13109,"**Duration**"],[12127,"**Edit files**"],[12869,"**Edit files**"],[12711,"**Edit message** (on a question, or ↑ in an empty box for the last one) opens the question in place. Change the text, remove attachments, and press **Send** (or Enter; Esc cancels). The edit becomes a new version of that question, answered afresh; what followed the old version stays with it."],[12668,"**Effort**: shown only for a model with reasoning levels. **Auto (server default)** sends no level and leaves it to the model and the provider; any other entry is sent as the request's `reasoning_effort`. See Model behaviour for how levels map to each provider."],[8692,"**Errors**: `{\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"detail\": {}}`, usually with `400` (`invalid_input`), `404` (`not_found`) or `409` (`conflict`); a body that does not match the schema gets the framework's `422`. See API overview."],[9989,"**Every command uses the same configuration.** Each command reads `config.json` in the data folder (its path is printed by `hoshimi config path`), whatever the working directory. The Web UI reads and writes the same file. `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` moves the data folder elsewhere, see Environment variables."],[12255,"**Exit** *code* or **Failed**"],[12402,"**Expired**"],[13116,"**Failed only**: only calls that failed."],[12406,"**Failing**"],[8693,"**Fields**: the running server's `/openapi.json` has every endpoint's full schema; the Web UI's types are generated from it."],[13055,"**First token (median)**"],[12988,"**Follow system** (the default) or **Reduced**: short fades instead of slides and growth"],[12411,"**Forget**: after **Forget this account?**, the credential is removed from `config.json` and from the running pool. Sign in again to bring it back."],[12498,"**Free** appears only when the station itself says so. No mark does not mean paid, only that the station did not say; a mark does not promise unlimited quota. Local models are not marked free automatically."],[12201,"**Full access**"],[12200,"**Full access** (`full`)"],[12292,"**Full access** runs every call without asking, including edits outside the workspace."],[11468,"**GitHub Pages** (the backup, licyk.github.io/Hoshimi): `.github/workflows/site.yml` builds the site with `VITE_BASE_PATH=/Hoshimi/` and force-pushes it to the `gh-pages` branch, which Pages serves. Pages on the backup carry a canonical link to the Netlify site."],[3647,"**GitHub Pages**（备份，licyk.github.io/Hoshimi）：`.github/workflows/site.yml` 以 `VITE_BASE_PATH=/Hoshimi/` 构建站点，并强制推送到 `gh-pages` 分支，由 Pages 提供服务。备份站的页面带有指向 Netlify 站点的 canonical 链接。"],[13609,"**Google default credentials**"],[13611,"**Google service account file**"],[5792,"**Google 服务账号文件**"],[5790,"**Google 默认凭据**"],[7980,"**Guarded against sudden shrinking**: when a fresh listing has fewer than half the models of the previous one, the old list is kept for one more cycle and the log warns `the catalogue came back at N of M models (likely a partial answer)`. If the next cycle says the same, the new list is accepted."],[12914,"**Host**"],[8116,"**How long a quota hold lasts**: the `Retry-After` header first, then a reset time stated in the body (such as `将在 2026-09-11 18:08:17 UTC+8 重置` or `reset at … UTC+8`, converted with its stated offset), and one hour when neither exists. A running hold is never shortened."],[12884,"**How tools run**:"],[12758,"**Image model**"],[12839,"**Image model**"],[12989,"**Images and video from other sites**"],[12462,"**Inherit global settings**"],[13043,"**Input tokens**"],[15486,"**International station**: set `options.base_url` to `https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4` to move the whole channel to api.z.ai."],[13184,"**Just finished** lists the last 10 calls, each **Served** or **Failed**."],[12825,"**Keep calls for (days)**"],[7982,"**Kept across restarts**: every successful catalogue is saved in the data directory's `catalog-cache/` and restored at start (only snapshots up to 7 days old, for exactly the same accounts and options), then refreshed in the background at once."],[7981,"**Kept on failure**: when a fetch fails, the last good catalogue stays and the fetch is retried after 30 seconds. A channel that never succeeded uses its built-in fallback list; fallback lists are historical data, not a claim that those models are available now."],[9797,"**Key env** is only the environment variable name the upstream's own tools use, so you know which key to look for; Hoshimi does not read these variables, and the key goes into the account in `config.json`. `--json` prints `{\"stations\": [...]}`, each entry with `id`, `display_name`, `base_url`, `key_env` and `catalog_keyless` (whether the model list can be fetched without a key). Usage and every preset are in agg aggregators."],[1976,"**Key env** 只是上游工具惯用的环境变量名，方便你知道去哪里找密钥；Hoshimi 不读取这些变量，密钥要写在 `config.json` 的账户里。`--json` 输出 `{\"stations\": [...]}`，每项有 `id`、`display_name`、`base_url`、`key_env`，以及 `catalog_keyless`（不带密钥也能获取模型列表）。用法和全部预设见 agg 聚合。"],[12801,"**Language**"],[12580,"**Latest version**"],[11903,"**Layers**: everything that opens over the page (dialogs, sheets, menus, an open picker) stacks through `ui/layers.ts`: what opened later paints above; Esc and an outside click close the topmost layer alone; while a modal layer is open, the page and every layer under it are `inert`; a closing layer gives focus back to what opened it."],[12982,"**Light**, **Dark**, **System** (the default). The theme button in the top bar switches it too"],[13181,"**Live activity**: an activity icon while nothing runs; a spinner with a count (**N calls running**) while calls are in flight. Click it for the live activity sheet:"],[11891,"**Live data**: `stores/live.ts` keeps the one connection to `GET /api/v1/stats/live`, which drives the top bar's live-calls sheet, the **Usage** page and the **Overview** card. It is read with `fetch` (`api/sse.ts`), because `EventSource` cannot send the access key as a header. REST stays the source of truth: a finished call invalidates the usage and channel queries, which refetch; after a drop it reconnects at 1, 2, 4, 8, 15 and 30 second intervals and starts from a fresh snapshot."],[14866,"**llama.cpp**: the thinking switch maps to chat-template parameters: `enable_thinking` and `thinking` in `chat_template_kwargs`. A request that already sets `enable_thinking` cannot also name a thinking level."],[7047,"**llama.cpp**：思考开关映射到聊天模板参数：`chat_template_kwargs` 中的 `enable_thinking` 和 `thinking`。请求中已有 `enable_thinking` 时不能同时指定思考级别。"],[8171,"**LLM7 uses Hoshimi's own rule**: keep rows whose `model_type` is `chat`. Checking for text output is not enough: `whisper-large-v3` (speech-to-text) and `gpt-image-2` (text and an image) would both slip in."],[350,"**LLM7 用的是 Hoshimi 自己的规则**：按行中的 `model_type` 只保留 `chat`。只看输出是否为文本不够：`whisper-large-v3`（语音转写）和 `gpt-image-2`（同时输出文本和图片）都会被误收。"],[14864,"**LM Studio**: reads the actual context length of loaded models (cached for 30 seconds). Before a request it makes a rough check: when a quarter of the messages' JSON byte size plus `max_tokens` exceeds the loaded context, it answers 400 at once (`LM Studio request exceeds this model's loaded context window`). For requests close to the limit, the server's own tokenizer still decides. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`; `xhigh` and `max` become `high`)."],[7045,"**LM Studio**：读取已加载模型的实际上下文长度（缓存 30 秒）。请求前做粗略检查：消息 JSON 字节数的四分之一加上 `max_tokens` 超过已加载的上下文时，直接返回 400（`LM Studio request exceeds this model's loaded context window`）。接近上限的请求仍以服务端的分词结果为准。思考级别通过 `reasoning_effort` 发送（`minimal` 映射为 `low`，`xhigh`、`max` 映射为 `high`）。"],[15389,"**Login method**: the channel's **Network** section has a **Cline login method** selector with **Device code (SDK)** (default) and **Browser (extension)**, matching `sdk` and `extension` for `providers.cline.options.client_profile`. The extension flow takes a callback on one of the local ports 48801–48811 and accepts a pasted callback. New accounts record the method they signed in with; changing the selector affects later sign-ins only."],[12816,"**Maximum request size (bytes)**"],[12703,"**Media from other sites.** Loading an image tells the site that serves it you are reading, and the address can carry text from the conversation, so an image, video or audio file a reply points to on another site waits behind a button that names the site (\"Load image from example.com\"). Media written into the reply itself (a `data:` address) shows at once. To always load media, set **Images and video from other sites** to **Always load** in **Settings › Appearance**."],[12934,"**Model API key**"],[12486,"**Model id**"],[13125,"**Model input / output**: the input before provider conversion and the normalized output chunks. Background Playground model rounds also record these sections."],[13068,"**Model**"],[13099,"**Model**"],[12667,"**Model**: any model the server advertises. Picking another model resets the effort to automatic."],[9051,"**Models with their own thinking menu** (the **Models** page shows several levels, for example `disabled` / `low` / `high` / `max`): a level on the menu is used as is; anything else goes through these aliases:"],[12049,"**Models**"],[12565,"**Models**"],[13158,"**Models**"],[8286,"**Models** and **Channels › Network** show the failure reason, known HTTP status, target host and suggested action. HTTP 200 can still carry an invalid model list. For 404/405, check the API base URL; if the upstream has no model listing endpoint, enter model IDs on the account manually. Another account succeeding in the same channel does not clear the failed refresh; a complete successful refresh does. The UI and catalogue failure logs omit raw response bodies, full request URLs and keys."],[13191,"**Models**, the **Playground** and the model pickers in **Settings** share one model catalogue. It arrives as a stream: cached models first, then each provider's own results as they come in, with **Loading providers: done/total** while it loads. A provider that fails or times out (after 20 seconds) is named with the reason, the models already received stay, and **Retry** loads again. See Models."],[15404,"**Models**: `MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview`, `MiniMax-M3`, `MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed`, `MiniMax-M2.7`. The M3.1 family requires adaptive thinking, so the adapter turns it on even when no level is given; M2.7 declares no levels, so a caller's level is not forwarded."],[15472,"**Models**: a fixed list such as `sn-sensenova-6-8-flash`, `sn-glm-5-3`, `sn-kimi-k3` and `sn-deepseek-v4-1-flash`."],[15394,"**Models**: a single `gemini-3.8-flash`, with thinking levels `low`, `medium`, `high` and `tiered` (`medium` when none is given). The level sets the thinking budget and is appended to the upstream model name as a suffix."],[15456,"**Models**: CodeBuddy has 16 fallback IDs (hy4/hy3, deepseek-v4, glm-5.x, kimi, minimax-m3); WorkBuddy has 23 (including aliases such as `default-model`, gpt-5.x, gemini-3.5-flash, glm and kimi). WorkBuddy switches its User-Agent by model family."],[15462,"**Models**: discovered from the station's built-in model list (`-VL` models excluded), with `GLM-5.x`, `deepseek-v4*`, `openpangu-2.0-*` and others as the fallback."],[15449,"**Models**: discovered live from `algo/api/v2/model/list`. The public ID is the catalogue's `display_name` without whitespace (`Auto`, `Qwen3.8-Max`, `DeepSeek-V4-Pro`, …); the upstream key (`auto`, `qmodel_38max`, `dmodel`) travels only inside the request. Context is the largest advertised option (often 1M), output is 131072, and each model's own thinking menu comes from its `thinking_config`. Capability discovery refreshes the catalogue before reading the thinking menu, so the first `/v1/models` response and the management catalogue include the live `efforts` and `effort_default` fields when discovery succeeds. Later reads reuse the model cache. Static fallbacks differ per edition."],[15481,"**Models**: read from the account's model catalogue, or declared with `models` on the account."],[15409,"**Models**: the fallback list includes `DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Official`, `Doubao-Seed-2.1-Pro`, `glm-5.2`, `kimi-k3` and others. TRAE provides a context-length table but no thinking menu, so a caller's `reasoning_effort` is forwarded unchanged."],[13634,"**Models**: the inference address and model list are read from the gateway's `/v1/config`. The account's `gateway` field replaces the default gateway `https://radius.pi.dev`."],[15485,"**Models**: the live listing comes first (other models the account's balance covers appear too). When it cannot be reached, the 7 free IDs are the fallback: `glm-4.7-flash`, `glm-4.5-flash`, `glm-4-flash-250414`, `glm-z1-flash`, `glm-4.6v-flash`, `glm-4.1v-thinking-flash`, `glm-4v-flash`."],[15438,"**Models**: the two editions have different tables: 17 international IDs (`auto`, `ultimate`, `performance`, `efficient`, `smodel`, `cmodel`, `qmodel_38max`, …) and 14 China IDs (including the China-only `q37fmodel` and `gm51model`). Sending one edition's exclusive ID to the other always fails."],[12987,"**Motion**"],[11904,"**Motion**: navigation fades through with View Transitions; tabs and filters slide along a shared horizontal axis (`AxisPanes`); a list-detail pane moves vertically between items (`shared-axis-y`); one view replacing another fades through (`FadeSwap`), as one Playground chat replacing another does; moving to another version of a Playground turn slides that turn and what follows it along the horizontal axis (`components/chat/VersionPanes.vue`, over `AxisPanes`), keeping what is above in place; a control that comes and goes in a row (the composer's effort and approval chips, the context ring) opens and closes its width with the gap beside it (`chip-row`, `chipRowHooks`), so the others slide and a long model name narrows rather than jumping, and a chip whose words change eases to its new width (`useMorphWidth`); list items use the `list` motion. **Settings › Appearance › Motion** (or the system's reduced-motion setting) turns every transition into a short fade."],[12706,"**Move** between all the images in the chat with the side buttons, ← and →, or a swipe."],[10051,"**Native forwarding**: when the account's provider has a Messages endpoint of its own (for example `anthropic`), the request is forwarded unchanged except for the model name. System arrays, content order, signatures, cache markers, `context_management`, structured output and fields added in the future are left for the upstream to validate; `anthropic-*` headers and query parameters go along. Upstream errors come back as they are: status, body, `request-id`, `retry-after`, `anthropic-ratelimit-*` and so on."],[12249,"**Needs approval**"],[12348,"**Needs attention**"],[12400,"**Needs login**"],[11467,"**Netlify** (the main site, hoshimi-dev.netlify.app): builds `site/` on every push to `main`, configured by `netlify.toml` at the repository root; it skips the build when `site/` did not change."],[3646,"**Netlify**（主站，hoshimi-dev.netlify.app）：每次推送到 `main` 都构建 `site/`，配置在仓库根目录的 `netlify.toml`；`site/` 没有改动时跳过构建。"],[12009,"**No configuration file is needed.** Without `config.json`, Hoshimi uses every default: it listens on `127.0.0.1:10600`, sets no key, and enables only the two anonymous channels. `config.json` is created the first time you save a setting, add an account or run `hoshimi config set`."],[12222,"**No decision**: a review takes at most 90 seconds. If the reviewer fails (a station error, too slow, or an answer that isn't a decision), the call is not denied: it waits for you with **Needs approval**, as in **Ask first**, and the card says \"The automatic review couldn’t decide, so you’re asked — *reason*\"."],[12533,"**No models yet**: no channel can serve yet. Sign into a free station or add an API key on the Channels page, then refresh. A fresh install can use OpenCode Zen and Kilo without an account; see Anonymous channels."],[15448,"**Nodes**: chat is routed to the account's `dataNodeMap.remote_agent` node, which is what the CLI uses; the catalogue stays on the inference node. The resolved node is cached for an hour. A `403 code 110 \"Billing daily count exceeded\"` is counted per node, so the adapter rotates through the remaining candidates and remembers whichever node served the request."],[12352,"**Not set up**"],[15476,"**Note**: the `uuid` and `firstKeyfrom` generated at sign-in are sent with every renewal request; do not remove them from the account or renewal fails."],[15399,"**Note**: the adapter puts the official ZCode client's identity and environment sections before the caller's system prompt, and inserts a date reminder before the first user message. The caller's system prompt is kept, after those blocks."],[15440,"**Note**: the official client uses an encrypted WASM inference path; Hoshimi uses the public OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which may answer `503`. Matching headers, models and renewal do not mean inference behaves exactly as in the official client."],[12350,"**Off**"],[14865,"**Ollama**: reads each model's capabilities, keeps only models that can do completion or tool calls, and marks vision, thinking and tool support from them; the context length is the largest one in the model info. A model whose details fail to load is still listed. Thinking levels are sent as `reasoning_effort` (`minimal` becomes `low`, `xhigh` becomes `max`)."],[7046,"**Ollama**：逐个读取模型的能力，只保留能做补全或工具调用的模型，并据此标记视觉、思考和工具能力；上下文长度取模型信息中的最大值。读取单个模型的详情失败时仍保留该模型。思考级别通过 `reasoning_effort` 发送（`minimal` 映射为 `low`，`xhigh` 映射为 `max`）。"],[12532,"**Open in the Playground**: opens a Playground chat with this model, reasoning effort **Auto**. A chat that already has messages is not overwritten; a new one starts. See Playground."],[13185,"**Open usage** goes to the **Usage** page."],[15400,"**Options**: `options.app_version` (default `3.14.3`)."],[9063,"**Other reasoning models** use Hoshimi's three output budgets (one ceiling shared by thinking and the answer):"],[13046,"**Output tokens**"],[12069,"**Overview › Endpoints**"],[12046,"**Overview**"],[13156,"**Overview**"],[12541,"**Overview** is the first page the interface opens on: the state of the gateway at a glance. From top to bottom it has **Today**, **Endpoints**, **Channels** and **Server**; each part has a button to the page with the details."],[12016,"**Overview**, **Models**, **Channels**, **Usage**, **Playground**; **Settings** sits at the foot of the rail. In a narrow window the rail becomes a bar at the bottom. When channels need attention, **Channels** carries a count badge"],[13091,"**Playground image descriptions**"],[13089,"**Playground titles**"],[5272,"**Playground 图片描述**"],[5270,"**Playground 标题**"],[4237,"**Playground**"],[5345,"**Playground**"],[12058,"**Playground**"],[13087,"**Playground**"],[13164,"**Playground**"],[4790,"**Playground** 是网页界面内置的聊天应用。它和客户端走同一个网关调用模型，所以是试用模型、检查账号、查看请求实际内容的最快方式。对话保存在服务端的数据目录中，关掉页面、重启进程都不会丢，换一个浏览器打开也能接着用。"],[5010,"**Playground** 部分，设置 Playground 与模型对话的方式："],[8694,"**Playground**: `/api/v1/playground/*` is covered in Playground API."],[873,"**Playground**：`/api/v1/playground/*` 见 Playground API。"],[12918,"**Port**"],[11744,"**POSIX-only tests**: the Playground's shell and background-command tests skip on Windows (`pytest.mark.skipif(os.name == \"nt\", ...)`); usage tests that switch the local time zone skip where `time.tzset` is missing."],[12245,"**Preparing…**"],[10052,"**Protocol conversion**: for other providers, Messages is converted to the internal Chat format first. Text, images, system prompts, tools and thinking convert; features only a native upstream has (the MCP connector, containers, `context_management`, server tools, `task_budget`, non-text documents and the like) return `400` naming the field."],[13101,"**Provider / account**"],[11742,"**Provider adapters**: build the adapter's client on `httpx.MockTransport` and check the request's address, headers and body, and the chunk types `stream_raw` yields. There is an example in Provider adapters."],[12488,"**Provider**"],[13070,"**Provider**"],[12501,"**Provider**: one provider only (**All providers** to undo)."],[12468,"**Proxy**"],[12960,"**Proxy**"],[4154,"**Python**"],[11975,"**Python**"],[11890,"**Queries**: `src/api/queries/` wraps Vue Query per area, with the query keys collected in `queries/keys.ts`, hierarchically, so invalidating a prefix invalidates every key under it. A 4xx `ApiError` is not retried, other failures at most twice; a window regaining focus does not refetch."],[12437,"**Rate limited**"],[12123,"**Read files**"],[12866,"**Read files**"],[12235,"**Read this file outside the workspace?**"],[12143,"**Read web pages**"],[12881,"**Read web pages**"],[12346,"**Ready**"],[12398,"**Ready**"],[12421,"**Recent check-ins** in the channel details lists its last 5 results: **Claimed** or **Failed**, the account, the station's message, the credits received (**+N**) and the time. Every check-in result is kept for 365 days and can be read from `GET /api/v1/credits/checkins`."],[11950,"**Reference projects**: protocols and behaviour come from local clones of a few outside repositories. They are excluded by `.gitignore` and are not runtime dependencies; see Reference projects below."],[12518,"**Region blocked**"],[12429,"**Remaining**"],[12661,"**Rename** sets your own title, which is never replaced by a generated one."],[12366,"**Renew now**"],[12369,"**Renew now** and **Claim now** (with accounts); **Add account** when the channel takes both and it is not the main action; **View usage** opens the Usage page"],[12416,"**Renew now** and **Renew every account** run a round at once with the same rule as the timer: only accounts close to expiry are renewed."],[12410,"**Renew now**: for an account with a refresh token; runs a renewal round for this channel."],[15489,"**Renewal**: starts 30 seconds after the gateway boots and checks every 30 minutes, renewing accounts that expire within the hour or record no expiry (only accounts with a `refresh_token`). When a station refuses the refresh token, the account is marked **Needs login** and taken out of rotation until you sign in again. A renewed token is written back to its own account only. To renew by hand, use **Renew now** in the channel detail (the whole channel, or one account from its menu) or **Renew every account** at the top of **Channels**; the API is `GET /api/v1/refresh` (status) and `POST /api/v1/refresh` (renew now)."],[15398,"**Renewal**: the adapter does not renew; sign in again when the token stops working."],[11902,"**Replies**: `ui/Markdown.vue` renders a reply block by block (only the block being written changes as it streams, so a drawn diagram or an open preview above it stays). Model text is untrusted: raw HTML stays text; math goes through KaTeX without `trust`; Mermaid draws in `strict` mode, loaded on first use (`ui/mermaid.ts`) and kept by source and theme; an `html` block previews only on request, in an `iframe` with `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` and a CSP that keeps it off the network; media on another site waits for a press unless the browser preference says otherwise (`ui/markdownRich.ts`). Any element marked `data-view` opens in `ImageViewer` through `useImageViewer`."],[12431,"**Reported in**"],[13472,"**Request shape**: requests to known stations turn `max_completion_tokens` into `max_tokens` and `developer` messages into `system`; requests to custom addresses are not rewritten. A station that answers a streaming request with one complete JSON document is still read correctly."],[15446,"**Request signing**: every catalogue and chat request carries `Authorization: Bearer COSY.<payload>.<sig>`. The payload encrypts the identity (AES-128-CBC, key reused as IV) under an RSA-encrypted key, and the signature is an MD5 over payload, key, timestamp, the exact encoded body and the signed path. The header set declares a CLI client (`Cosy-Clienttype: 5`, machine id/type/OS, `Cosy-Data-Policy: disagree`, `Login-Version: v2`). The client version follows the latest Qoder CLI release (checked once a day, cached in the data directory), because the gateway serves a reduced catalogue to clients that lag behind."],[13123,"**Requests and responses** at the bottom of the sheet loads full payloads on demand. Expand a section to inspect or copy it:"],[15480,"**Requests**: system and developer messages are merged into `instructions`, and `max_output_tokens`, `temperature` and `top_p` are not sent; the account's `account_id` is sent as the `ChatGPT-Account-Id` header."],[15468,"**Requests**: the token is sent both as `Authorization: Bearer` and as a `token` header (the chat and control endpoints each accept one of them)."],[13141,"**Reset statistics** in the ⋮ menu clears every counter, chart and recorded call, after you confirm **Reset all usage statistics?**. **It cannot be undone.** Calls in flight at the time are still recorded when they end."],[10546,"**Reset statistics** on the Web UI's **Usage** page, or `DELETE /api/v1/stats`. Cannot be undone"],[8486,"**Reset statistics** on the Web UI's **Usage** page, or:"],[12435,"**Responses seen**"],[5262,"**Responses**"],[13081,"**Responses**"],[12559,"**Responses** (OpenAI)"],[4738,"**Responses**（OpenAI）"],[12404,"**Resting**"],[12306,"**Review model**"],[12893,"**Review model**"],[12247,"**Reviewing…**"],[8418,"**Routing failures count as failures**: a request that ends before reaching upstream (model not found, every account failed and so on) is still recorded, as a failure."],[12131,"**Run commands**"],[12872,"**Run commands**"],[12229,"**Run this command?**"],[13183,"**Running now (N)** shows a card per call: the model, provider / account (**Choosing an account…** until one is picked), the API, the reasoning effort, how many accounts were tried, a **Waiting**, **Thinking**, **Answering** track, and **TTFT**, **Tokens out** (estimated from the streamed text, marked ≈, until the station reports its own count) and **tok/s**."],[12550,"**Running now**"],[13115,"**Search calls**: searches the model, provider, account, error code, error message and finish reason (case-insensitive)."],[12659,"**Search chats** filters the list by title as you type."],[12500,"**Search models**: matches the model id, the provider or the display name."],[12355,"**Search providers**: by channel id or name."],[12139,"**Search the web**"],[12878,"**Search the web**"],[12315,"**SearXNG address**"],[12905,"**SearXNG address**"],[4494,"**SearXNG 地址**"],[5086,"**SearXNG 地址**"],[13114,"**Served** or **Failed**"],[12441,"**Server errors**"],[12085,"**Settings › About** (**Data directory**, **Config file**, **Database**, **Copy config path**), or `hoshimi config path`"],[12071,"**Settings › Access › Keys**"],[12073,"**Settings › Access › Listening address** (after a restart)"],[12083,"**Settings › Automation**"],[12079,"**Settings › General › Default model**"],[12077,"**Settings › Network**; for one channel, on that channel's page"],[12075,"**Settings › Security**, see Security"],[12081,"**Settings › Tools**, see Playground tools"],[9960,"**Settings.** No environment variable maps to a `config.json` key (there is no `HOSHIMI_PORT`, for example). To change the port, keys and so on for one start, use the `hoshimi serve` options; to change them for good, use `hoshimi config set` or the Web UI."],[12061,"**Settings**"],[13166,"**Settings**"],[10234,"**Settings** › **Access** › **Keys**"],[12793,"**Settings** sits at the foot of the navigation and is split into eight tabs. The current tab is part of the address (such as `#/settings?tab=access`)."],[11900,"**Shared components**: pages and composites take shared components from `@/ui` and do not restyle them (the convention stated in `ui/index.ts`). A page is a `Toolbar` row over one column of `PageSection`s, and adapts to the content area's width (`@container app-content`). A list that can grow without bound sits in a `ScrollArea` or a `DataTable` (sortable, rendering only what is in view past 200 rows). Channels is a `ListDetail` layout."],[4488,"**Shell**"],[5078,"**Shell**"],[12309,"**Shell**"],[12897,"**Shell**"],[12362,"**Sign in**"],[10855,"**Sign in** and **Add account** in the Web UI, and `hoshimi login`, write accounts here and enable the channel; signing in again as the same identity replaces the account instead of adding a second one."],[15455,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login buddy` or `hoshimi login workbuddy` opens an external login page, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed."],[15388,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login cline` uses WorkOS device authorization by default, then registers with Cline to obtain the station token. The token is stored with its `workos:` prefix and sent as is."],[15460,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login codearts` opens the Huawei Cloud portal's authorization page, which calls back to a random local port of 10000 or above (the portal refuses lower ports); the token exchange carries a DPoP proof. It waits at most 5 minutes for the callback and accepts a pasted one."],[15479,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login codex` opens OpenAI's consent page and calls back to the fixed local address `localhost:1455` (the redirect registered for the Codex client), so that port must be free; only one Codex sign-in can run at a time. A pasted callback is accepted."],[15393,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login gemini` opens Google's consent page, which calls back to a temporary port on `localhost`; a pasted callback is accepted. The sign-in stores the public desktop client's `client_id` and `client_secret` with the account, so renewal needs no extra setup. `options.client_id` / `options.client_secret` override them."],[15475,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login lobsterai` opens the `lobsterai.youdao.com` portal, which calls back to a temporary local port; a pasted callback is accepted."],[15466,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login loomy` starts a local page showing a WeChat QR code; scan and confirm. A WeChat account using Loomy for the first time must bind a phone number on the same page (request and enter the SMS code). The page is served only on `127.0.0.1`, so open it in a browser on the same machine."],[15403,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login minimax` uses a device code on `account.minimax.cn`, checked with PKCE."],[15437,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login qoder` or `hoshimi login qodercn` opens the device authorization page on `qoder.com` / `qoder.cn`, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed. The sign-in generates a `machine_id` that renewal requests carry, so keep it in the account."],[15443,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login qodercli --manual` (or `qodercli-cn`) opens the account's integrations page and asks for a Personal Access Token. Create one at https\\://qoder.com/account/integrations (international) or https\\://qoder.com.cn/account/integrations (China). In the web UI, **Sign in** shows the same paste field, and **Add account → Personal Access Token** files the token directly. A token exported as `QODER_API_KEY` / `QODER_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` / `QODER_PAT` (or the `QODERCN_*` equivalents) signs the lane in without a prompt."],[15471,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login raccoon` opens the station's WeChat QR page, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed."],[15408,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login trae` opens the login page on `www.trae.cn`; the station sends the tokens straight back to a local callback, on port 18080 when free or any free port otherwise. A pasted callback is accepted."],[15397,"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login zcode` is mediated by the station and authorised with a Zhipu account; there is no local callback, so it works on a remote server. The sign-in generates and stores a fixed `device_mid`."],[12986,"**Standard** (the default), **Medium**, **High**"],[11897,"**Static tokens**: type, shape, elevation, motion durations and easing, state layers and the rest are in `theme/tokens.css`, named `--md-sys-*` and `--app-*`."],[8169,"**Stations are recognised by address**, not by preset name: an account with `preset: sambanova` whose `base_url` points elsewhere is not reading SambaNova's catalogue and does not get its rules. Addresses outside the preset table (your own relays included) are not filtered."],[13113,"**Status**"],[12261,"**Stopped**"],[12730,"**Stopped**"],[12770,"**Summary model**"],[12855,"**Summary model**"],[12750,"**System prompt**"],[12833,"**System prompt**"],[11983,"**The API contract**"],[10259,"**The bare `id`**, such as `big-pickle`. Hoshimi picks the first provider, in provider order, that lists it. With only one provider enabled, a name missing from the catalogue is passed to that provider as is."],[12012,"**The browser.** About a second later the browser opens `http://127.0.0.1:10600`, and the address becomes `http://127.0.0.1:10600/#/overview`. Page addresses all live after the `#` and can be bookmarked, such as `#/playground` or `#/settings?tab=access`."],[12857,"**The chat's own model**"],[12895,"**The chat’s own model**"],[11948,"**The code and its tests**: when anything else disagrees with them, they win. Many rules are tests themselves (the layering rule, the Web UI's layout and colour rules, matching i18n keys), so a change that breaks one does not pass CI."],[12010,"**The data folder.** The server creates `hoshimi.db` (usage, check-in records, probe verdicts and Playground conversations) and `server.json` (the running server's address and PID) in the data folder. Where that folder is, is covered in Data folder; it is also shown under **Settings › About**."],[11898,"**The rule**: components use tokens only, never a literal colour, radius or duration. `src/tokens.test.ts` checks that no `.vue` or `.css` file outside `src/theme/` contains a hex colour."],[9990,"**The server does not need to be running.** `check`, `models`, `providers`, `login`, `config` and the rest build the channels from the configuration in their own process and exit when done; they do not talk to a running server."],[12981,"**Theme**"],[13186,"**Theme**: cycles between light, dark and following the system. More appearance options are in **Settings › Appearance**."],[15487,"**Thinking**: text models without a menu leave the caller's request untouched; thinking-by-construction models such as Z1 and V-Thinking use the budget ladder."],[15450,"**Thinking**: the level rides in the envelope's `parameters` (`enable_thinking`, and `reasoning_effort` for effort-based models). Off takes both signals; a model with no `disabled` branch is sent the switch alone, because it rejects `reasoning_effort: \"none\"`. Leaked `<thinking>` tags and DSML tool-call markup are stripped, and a turn that produced nothing but markup is reported as a retryable error instead of a finished task."],[12732,"**This reply failed.** and a reason"],[11949,"**This site**: it replaces the repository's old `docs/` folder and is Hoshimi's only documentation. A change users can see (a command, an option, a config key, an endpoint, the interface) updates the matching pages, in Chinese and in English; see Documentation site."],[12522,"**Throttled**"],[13097,"**Time**"],[13119,"**Time**, **Model**, **Provider**, **Account**, **API**, **Effort**, **Response** (**Streamed** or **Whole**), **Accounts tried** (how many accounts the rotation went through), **Finish reason**."],[13121,"**Timing**: **TTFT**, **Decode**, **Duration**, **tok/s**."],[12754,"**Title model**"],[12836,"**Title model**"],[12047,"**Today** (tokens, calls, cache hit, running now, and a 24-hour trend); **Endpoints** (the base URL and each endpoint, with copy buttons); **Channels** (the channels that are set up, with their status); **Server** (version, latest version, default model)"],[5292,"**tok/s**"],[13111,"**tok/s**"],[12563,"**Token count (estimate)** (Anthropic)"],[15445,"**Token exchange**: a `pt-…` token is not an API credential. The adapter exchanges it at `{openApi}/api/v1/jobToken/exchange` for a job token (`jt-…`, one day) plus a job refresh token, reads the account identity from `/api/v1/userinfo`, and re-exchanges on renewal. The PAT stays in the account so renewal can repeat the exchange; a PAT the station refuses takes the account out of rotation until a human signs in again."],[5221,"**Token 总量**"],[4742,"**Token 数量估算**（Anthropic）"],[4723,"**token**"],[5284,"**token**"],[12544,"**Tokens**"],[13103,"**Tokens**"],[12931,"**Tool access key**"],[12300,"**Tools**"],[12862,"**Tools** (`playground.tools`, all on by default, for every chat):"],[13040,"**Total tokens**"],[12812,"**Tries per request across accounts**"],[12712,"**Try again** (on a reply) asks for another reply to the same question, with the model and effort now in the composer. Switch the model first to compare models on the same question. A failed reply also shows **Try again** next to its error."],[13107,"**TTFT**"],[12520,"**Unavailable**"],[12524,"**Unknown**"],[12433,"**Updated**"],[13126,"**Upstream exchange**: the actual provider URL, headers and request body, response status, headers and body. Failures, retries and redirects are separate entries with account and attempt information. The Bedrock SDK path records SDK parameters, metadata and response events."],[12055,"**Usage**"],[13162,"**Usage**"],[13177,"**Usage** for one day"],[13175,"**Usage** over **30 days**"],[12922,"**Use only this port**"],[12578,"**Version**"],[12993,"**Version**"],[9931,"**Vertex with `auth: \"adc\"`**: Google's application default credentials (ADC), such as a service account file named by `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`. Needs `hoshimi[google]`."],[2110,"**Vertex，`auth: \"adc\"`**：Google 的应用默认凭据（ADC），例如 `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` 指向的服务账户文件。需要 `hoshimi[google]`。"],[11509,"**Vite**: `bun run dev --port 5173 --strictPort` in `hoshimi/webui`, with `HOSHIMI_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:10600`."],[3688,"**Vite**：在 `hoshimi/webui` 中运行 `bun run dev --port 5173 --strictPort`，并设置 `HOSHIMI_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:10600`。"],[4159,"**Web UI**"],[11980,"**Web UI**"],[12724,"**when the model refuses a request as too long**: the conversation is compacted and the request sent again, and if that is still too long, once more with long tool outputs cut. This happens even with automatic compaction off;"],[13283,"**When the port is taken**: the server binds the socket itself, so the port it tested is the port it serves. If the requested port is taken or reserved by the system, it tries the next port, up to 65535, then wraps around to the ports from 1024 up to the requested one; any other bind error (such as an address this machine does not have) fails at once. When it moves, the log says `Port 10600 is unavailable. Using port 10601.`"],[12303,"**When tools ask first**"],[12889,"**When tools ask first**"],[12725,"**when you type `/compact`**, optionally followed by what the summary should keep."],[13286,"**Where to find the actual address**: the `SERVER_READY url=…` line in the terminal; `server.json` in the data folder (host, actual port, URL and process PID, removed when the server exits); and **Listening on …** under **Settings › Access › Listening address**."],[13596,"**Workers AI**: the address is `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account_id>/ai/v1`. The catalogue comes from Cloudflare's native model search, keeping text-generation tasks only; `models` declared on the account replaces it."],[5777,"**Workers AI**：地址为 `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account_id>/ai/v1`。模型目录读取 Cloudflare 原生的模型搜索接口，只保留文本生成任务；账号中声明 `models` 时以声明为准。"],[12198,"**Workspace**"],[12312,"**Workspace**"],[12901,"**Workspace**"],[11745,"**Your own Services**: call `make_services(default_model=..., ...)` for particular settings; pass extra `FakeProvider`s or subclasses for several providers."],[12705,"**Zoom** with the mouse wheel, a pinch, a double click, or + and -; 0 or **Fit to window** goes back. Drag to look around while zoomed. Diagrams and SVG images stay sharp at every zoom."],[4669,"**上下文**"],[5023,"**上下文** 部分，Playground 对话接近模型上下文窗口时如何处理："],[5307,"**上游请求与返回**：实际发送给渠道的 URL、请求头和正文，以及返回状态、响应头和正文；失败、重试和跳转分别记录，并标明账号与尝试次数。Bedrock SDK 路径记录 SDK 参数、元数据与返回事件。"],[4886,"**下载** 保存图片；**在新标签页中打开** 单独打开它（直接写在回复中的图片不提供此项，浏览器不会把它们作为页面打开）。"],[4699,"**不可用**"],[2169,"**不需要服务器在运行。** `check`、`models`、`providers`、`login`、`config` 等命令在自己的进程里按配置构建渠道，执行完就退出，不会连接正在运行的服务器。"],[4188,"**不需要配置文件。** 没有 `config.json` 时，Hoshimi 使用全部默认值：监听 `127.0.0.1:10600`，不设任何密钥，只启用两个匿名渠道。`config.json` 在你第一次保存设置、添加账户或执行 `hoshimi config set` 时才会创建。"],[5209,"**与前一天相比**"],[5206,"**与昨天同一时刻相比**"],[5162,"**主题**"],[5367,"**主题**：在浅色、深色和跟随系统之间轮流切换。更多外观选项在 **设置 › 外观**。"],[5164,"**主题色**"],[5103,"**仅使用此端口**"],[4470,"**仅在工作区外询问** 会不经询问运行任何命令。命令并不局限于工作区，所以在这个模式下，模型可以修改或删除该用户能访问的任何文件，也可以访问你的网络。只在你信任模型和任务时使用。"],[4376,"**仅在工作区外询问**（`workspace`）"],[5297,"**仅失败**：只看失败的调用。"],[4602,"**今日** 部分显示这个渠道今天（服务器本地时间）的 **token**、**调用次数**、**缓存命中** 和 **失败** 次数。"],[4226,"**今日**（Token、调用次数、缓存命中、正在进行，以及最近 24 小时的趋势）；**接口**（Base URL 和各接口地址，可复制）；**渠道**（已设置的渠道及其状态）；**服务器**（版本、最新版本、默认模型）"],[4127,"**代码和测试**：其他任何内容与它们冲突时，以它们为准。很多规则本身就是测试（分层规则、Web UI 的布局与配色规则、i18n 键一致），破坏规则的改动过不了 CI。"],[7626,"**令牌交换**：`pt-…` 不是 API 凭据。适配器在 `{openApi}/api/v1/jobToken/exchange` 用它换取作业令牌（`jt-…`，一天有效）和作业刷新令牌，再从 `/api/v1/userinfo` 读取账号身份，续期时重新交换。PAT 会保留在账号里以便重复交换；站点拒绝 PAT 时账号退出轮换，直到重新登录。"],[5466,"**任意空闲端口**：`--port 0` 让系统挑选一个。"],[7644,"**优惠模型**：`options.benefit_models`（默认 `glm-5.3-flash`、`deepseek-v4.1-flash`）中的模型请求时附带 `maas_type: benefit` 头；站点拒绝该头时自动去掉重试。"],[7672,"**余额**：支持的站点可以查询余额或额度。另外，网关会从站点每次响应的限流头中被动读取剩余额度，显示在渠道详情的 **额度** 部分，不产生额外请求。"],[7576,"**余额**：显示五小时和每周两个额度窗口的剩余比例，不是积分。"],[7571,"**余额**：需要账号中的 `account_id`（形如 `usr-…`，登录时自动保存）。"],[4904,"**你输入 `/compact` 时**，后面可以写上总结应保留的内容。"],[2170,"**修改要重启才对运行中的服务器生效。** `hoshimi config set` 和 `hoshimi login` 只写入 `config.json`；正在运行的服务器不会重新读取文件。修改后重启服务器，或者直接在 Web UI 的 **设置** 和 **渠道** 页修改，那里的修改立即生效（监听地址和端口除外）。"],[4399,"**允许**：调用照常运行。展开卡片会显示“*模型* 已允许”，并附上风险和理由（如有）。"],[4417,"**允许**：运行这一次调用。"],[5124,"**允许的 CIDR**"],[5127,"**允许的主机名**"],[5130,"**允许的来源**"],[4372,"**先询问** 下会询问的调用交给审查模型允许或拒绝；只有它无法判断时才询问你"],[4373,"**先询问**（`ask`）"],[5171,"**先询问**（默认）：Playground 回复引用的其他网站上的媒体，先显示为注明网站的按钮；**始终加载**"],[4677,"**免费** 只在站点自己说明免费时出现。没有标记不代表收费，只是站点没有说；有标记也不保证额度无限。本地模型不会自动标为免费。"],[4079,"**共享组件**：页面和组合组件从 `@/ui` 取用共享组件，不重新设定它们的样式（`ui/index.ts` 的约定）。页面的骨架是一行 `Toolbar`，下面是一列 `PageSection`；页面按内容区的宽度调整布局（`@container app-content`）。可能无限增长的列表放在 `ScrollArea` 或 `DataTable` 里（`DataTable` 可排序，超过 200 行时只渲染可见部分）。渠道页面是 `ListDetail` 布局。"],[1242,"**其他推理模型**使用 Hoshimi 的三档输出预算（思考和回答共用这个上限）："],[4759,"**最新版本**"],[2439,"**写成 `渠道/模型`**，如 `opencode/big-pickle`，指定由哪个渠道处理。第一个斜杠后面的全部内容作为上游模型名发送，可以再含斜杠，例如 `kilo/kilo-auto/free`。几个渠道提供同名模型时，用这种写法选择其中一个。"],[4424,"**准备中…**"],[7648,"**凭据**：会话有效期约 14 天，适配器不续期，到期后重新登录。"],[7642,"**凭据**：得到的是带过期时间的临时 AK/SK 和安全令牌。适配器不续期，过期后重新登录。"],[5154,"**凭据续期**"],[4618,"**凭据被拒**"],[4585,"**出错**"],[5266,"**分类**"],[4885,"**切换**：用两侧按钮、← 和 → 或滑动，在对话中的所有图片之间切换。"],[5365,"**刚刚完成** 列出最近 10 个调用，标明 **已回答** 或 **失败**。"],[4842,"**删除**：先确认，然后永久删除对话、其全部消息以及只属于它的附件。其中正在进行的回复会先被停止，它的工具启动的所有后台命令也会停止。"],[4590,"**删除**：确认 **删除这个账号？** 后，凭据从 `config.json` 和运行中的账号池中移除。重新登录即可恢复。"],[4608,"**剩余**"],[4083,"**动效**：页面之间用 View Transitions 淡入淡出；标签页和筛选沿共享的水平轴滑动（`AxisPanes`）；列表-详情的详情区在条目之间纵向移动（`shared-axis-y`）；一个视图替换另一个时淡入淡出（`FadeSwap`），Playground 中一个对话替换另一个时也是如此；切换 Playground 中某条消息的版本时，该消息及其后的内容沿水平轴滑动（`components/chat/VersionPanes.vue`，基于 `AxisPanes`），上方的内容保持不动；一排控件中出现和消失的控件（输入框里的推理强度和审批芯片、上下文圆环）连同旁边的间距一起展开和收起宽度（`chip-row`、`chipRowHooks`），其他控件随之滑动，较长的模型名称逐渐收窄而不是跳变；文字变化的芯片平滑过渡到新宽度（`useMorphWidth`）；列表项使用 `list` 动效。**设置 › 外观 › 动画**（或系统的“减少动态效果”）把所有过渡换成简短的淡入淡出。"],[5168,"**动画**"],[2231,"**协议转换**：其他渠道先把 Messages 转换成内部的 Chat 格式。文字、图片、系统提示、工具、思考都能转换，但只有原生上游才支持的功能（MCP 连接器、容器、`context_management`、服务器端工具、`task_budget`、非文本文档等）会返回 `400`，消息中写明是哪个字段。"],[5204,"**单日**（今天）"],[5207,"**单日**（过去某天）"],[4993,"**单次请求可尝试的账号数**"],[5032,"**压缩阈值（占窗口的百分比）**"],[4945,"**压缩阈值**"],[2230,"**原生转发**：账号所在的渠道本身提供 Messages 接口（例如 `anthropic`），请求只替换模型名后原样转发，系统提示数组、内容顺序、签名、缓存标记、`context_management`、结构化输出以及将来的新字段都交给上游校验；`anthropic-*` 请求头和查询参数也会带上。上游的错误（状态码、响应体、`request-id`、`retry-after`、`anthropic-ratelimit-*` 等头）原样返回。"],[4129,"**参考项目**：协议和行为的来源是几个外部仓库的本地克隆，它们被 `.gitignore` 排除，不是运行时依赖，见下文参考项目。"],[3923,"**只在 POSIX 上运行的测试**：Playground 的 shell 与后台命令测试在 Windows 上跳过（`pytest.mark.skipif(os.name == \"nt\", ...)`）；需要切换本地时区的用量测试在没有 `time.tzset` 的平台上跳过。"],[4695,"**可用**"],[4673,"**可用性**"],[4681,"**可用性**：做过探测后出现，只列出已经出现过的结论，以及 **未探测**；**全部状态** 恢复。"],[4314,"**后台命令**"],[5056,"**后台命令**"],[4190,"**后台定时任务。** 凭据续期（每 30 分钟）和每日签到随服务器启动，日志里会各有一行。还会在后台向 PyPI 查询是否有新版本。这三项都可以关闭，见配置。"],[4081,"**回复**：`ui/Markdown.vue` 按块渲染回复（流式输出时只有正在写的块会变，已画好的图表或上方打开的预览不受影响）。模型文本不可信：原始 HTML 保持为文字；数学公式交给不带 `trust` 的 KaTeX；Mermaid 以 `strict` 模式绘制，首次用到时加载（`ui/mermaid.ts`），并按源码和主题缓存；`html` 代码块只在请求时预览，放在 `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` 且 CSP 禁止联网的 `iframe` 中；其他网站上的媒体要等用户点击，除非浏览器偏好设置为始终加载（`ui/markdownRich.ts`）。任何标记了 `data-view` 的元素都通过 `useImageViewer` 在 `ImageViewer` 中打开。"],[4901,"**回复开始时**：对话达到窗口的 85%（`playground.compact_threshold`），或剩余空间已不足以容纳回复；"],[4902,"**回复的两轮工具调用之间**：让长时间运行的智能体任务得以继续；"],[5465,"**固定端口**：客户端需要固定地址时，用 `--strict-port`（或配置 `server.strict_port: true`），此时只尝试请求的端口，被占用就以退出码 3 结束。"],[7667,"**国际站**：`options.base_url` 设为 `https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4` 可以把整个渠道切到 api.z.ai。"],[4082,"**图层**：浮在页面上的东西（对话框、侧边面板、菜单、打开的选择器）都通过 `ui/layers.ts` 叠放：后打开的画在上面；Esc 和点击外部只关闭最上层；模态层打开时，页面和它下面的层都设为 `inert`；层关闭后把焦点还给打开它的元素。"],[4937,"**图片模型**"],[5020,"**图片模型**"],[4078,"**图表**：数据系列按固定顺序使用 `--app-chart-1` 到 `--app-chart-8` 这八个经过色盲校验的颜色槽；图表带图例和悬停 / 聚焦提示。"],[4711,"**在 Playground 中打开**：用这个模型新开一个 Playground 对话，推理强度为 **自动**。当前对话已有内容时不会被覆盖，而是另开新对话。见 Playground。"],[4894,"**在新对话中分支**（在回复上）会把对话截至这条回复的内容复制到一个新对话并打开它（提示“已在新对话中打开”）。新对话沿用标题、模型和推理强度，以及原对话的审批模式；原对话保持不变。想让一段对话朝两个方向发展、又不想来回切换版本时，可以用它。"],[4697,"**地区受限**"],[4710,"**复制模型 id**：把 id 复制到剪贴板，粘贴到客户端的 `model` 中。"],[5182,"**复制配置路径** 把配置文件的路径复制到剪贴板。没有设置工具访问密钥时还有 **API 文档** 按钮，打开服务器自带的接口文档（`/docs`）。数据目录的位置和其中的文件见数据目录与路径；命令行中可以用 `hoshimi config path` 查看配置文件的路径。"],[160,"**失败时保留旧的**：拉取失败时保留上一次成功的目录，30 秒后再试。从未成功过的渠道使用它内置的后备列表；后备列表只是历史数据，不代表这些模型现在可用。"],[4472,"**始终允许** 会在此对话的剩余时间里（直到服务重启）不再询问，在 **自动审查** 下也不再经过审查模型。需要每次检查的操作，请选择 **允许**。"],[4418,"**始终允许**：运行这次调用，并且在此对话中运行同类调用时不再询问。“同类”指同一个工具开关，且工作区内和工作区外分开计算：始终允许工作区内的编辑，并不允许工作区外的编辑。这一许可持续到服务重启，删除对话时也会被清除。"],[872,"**字段**：运行中服务器的 `/openapi.json` 列出每个接口的完整结构，网页界面的类型也由它生成。"],[4380,"**完全访问**"],[4471,"**完全访问** 不经询问运行所有调用，包括对工作区外文件的编辑。"],[4379,"**完全访问**（`full`）"],[4070,"**实时数据**：`stores/live.ts` 维持唯一一条到 `GET /api/v1/stats/live` 的连接，它驱动顶栏的实时调用面板、**用量** 页面和 **概览** 页面的卡片。连接用 `fetch` 读取（`api/sse.ts`），因为 `EventSource` 不能在请求头里带访问密钥。REST 仍是事实来源：一次调用结束会使用量和渠道的查询失效并重新请求；断线后以 1、2、4、8、15、30 秒的间隔重连，并从新的快照开始。"],[4197,"**实时活动** 按钮：显示正在进行的调用数，点开是今天的 Token、调用次数、缓存命中率，以及正在进行和刚刚完成的调用。旁边是主题按钮，在 **浅色**、**深色**、**跟随系统** 之间切换"],[5362,"**实时活动**：没有调用时是一个活动图标；有调用正在进行时变成转圈的图标并显示数量（**N 个调用进行中**）。点开是实时活动面板："],[5467,"**实际地址在哪里**：终端打印的 `SERVER_READY url=…`；数据目录里的 `server.json`（主机、实际端口、URL 和进程 PID，服务器退出时删除）；以及 **设置 › 访问 › 监听地址** 中的 **正在监听 …**。"],[4426,"**审查中…**"],[4438,"**审查已拒绝**"],[4485,"**审查模型**"],[5074,"**审查模型**"],[5305,"**客户端 HTTP 请求 / 返回**：请求方法、路径、请求头、状态码和 JSON 或 SSE 正文。"],[598,"**客户端中途断开不算失败**：调用方在回复过程中断开，网关确实提供了服务，这条记录算作成功。"],[5108,"**密钥** 部分。两种密钥相互独立，留空则对应的接口不校验密钥："],[5166,"**对比度**"],[5038,"**对话自身使用的模型**"],[5076,"**对话自身使用的模型**"],[4525,"**就绪**"],[4577,"**就绪**"],[4377,"**工作区**"],[4491,"**工作区**"],[5082,"**工作区**"],[4479,"**工具**"],[5043,"**工具**（`playground.tools`，默认全部开启，对所有对话生效）："],[4482,"**工具何时先询问**"],[5070,"**工具何时先询问**"],[5065,"**工具如何运行**："],[5112,"**工具访问密钥**"],[4440,"**已停止**"],[4909,"**已停止**"],[4529,"**已关闭**"],[4550,"**已启用** 开关写入 `config.json` 的 `providers.<id>.enabled`，立即生效。关闭后该渠道不再参与服务，它的模型也从目录中消失；账号仍保留在配置中，重新开启即可恢复。给关闭的渠道添加账号会自动重新开启它。"],[5295,"**已回答** 或 **失败**"],[4436,"**已拒绝**"],[297,"**已经向调用方输出了内容的请求，绝不会自动重放**，以免同一段回答出现两次。"],[4614,"**已见响应**"],[4581,"**已过期**"],[4978,"**常规** 部分："],[4410,"**应用这些更改？**"],[4841,"**归档**：把对话收起来而不删除。列表底部的 **已归档的对话** 显示归档内容；在其中选 **恢复** 可以取回对话，在已归档的对话中发送新消息也会让它回到列表。**返回对话列表** 回到普通列表。归档当前打开的对话会开始一个新对话。"],[7668,"**思考**：没有菜单的文本模型不改动调用方的请求；Z1 和 V-Thinking 这类本身就是思考模型的，使用预算阶梯控制。"],[7631,"**思考**：级别写在信封的 `parameters` 里（`enable_thinking`，effort 型模型另加 `reasoning_effort`）。关闭需要两个信号；没有 `disabled` 分支的模型只发开关，因为它会拒绝 `reasoning_effort: \"none\"`。泄漏的 `<thinking>` 标签与 DSML 工具调用标记会被清理；只产出标记、没有正文也没有工具调用的回合会作为可重试错误上报，而不是当作已完成。"],[4949,"**总结模型**"],[5036,"**总结模型**"],[2168,"**所有命令共用同一份配置。** 每条命令都读取数据目录里的 `config.json`（路径由 `hoshimi config path` 打印），与当前工作目录无关。Web UI 读写的也是这个文件。数据目录可以用 `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` 换到别处，见环境变量。"],[5366,"**打开用量** 跳到 **用量** 页。"],[4400,"**拒绝**：卡片显示 **审查已拒绝**，展开后显示“*模型* 已拒绝 · 高风险 — *理由*”。模型会被告知理由，并被告知不要绕过它：不能换个办法、间接执行或改用其他工具达到同样目的；只有找到明显更安全的替代做法，或你在了解风险后明确批准，才能继续；否则它会停下来询问你。"],[4419,"**拒绝**：跳过这次调用。模型会被告知你拒绝了它，除非你要求否则不要再试；卡片显示 **已拒绝**。"],[4647,"**指定代理**"],[5141,"**指定代理**"],[348,"**按地址识别站点**，而不是按预设名：账号写了 `preset: sambanova` 却把 `base_url` 指向别处，读到的就不是 SambaNova 的目录，不会套用它的规则。不在预设地址表中的地址（包括你自己的中继）不做过滤。"],[5255,"**接口**"],[7808,"**接口** 一栏列出客户端要用的地址（`/v1/chat/completions`、`/v1/responses`、`/v1/messages` 等），每行都可以一键复制。"],[4162,"**接口契约**"],[4847,"**推理强度**：只有支持推理级别的模型才显示。**自动（服务端默认）** 不发送级别，由模型和供应商决定；选择其他项则作为请求的 `reasoning_effort` 发送。各供应商如何对应这些级别见模型行为。"],[4667,"**提供商**"],[4680,"**提供商**：只看某一个提供商（**全部提供商** 恢复）。"],[5282,"**提供方 / 账户**"],[5251,"**提供方**"],[4534,"**搜索供应商**：按渠道 id 或名称搜索。"],[4838,"**搜索对话**：边输入边按标题筛选列表。"],[4679,"**搜索模型**：按模型 id、提供商或显示名称搜索。"],[5296,"**搜索调用**：在模型、提供方、账户、错误代码、错误信息和结束原因中搜索（不区分大小写）。"],[5180,"**数据库**"],[4189,"**数据目录。** 服务器在数据目录里创建 `hoshimi.db`（用量、签到记录、探测结果和 Playground 对话）和 `server.json`（正在运行的服务器的地址和 PID）。数据目录的位置见数据目录，也显示在 **设置 › 关于** 中。"],[5176,"**数据目录**"],[4164,"**文档**"],[4401,"**无法判断**：一次审查最多 90 秒。如果审查失败（站点出错、太慢，或回答不是一个结论），调用不会被拒绝，而是像 **先询问** 一样停在 **等待批准** 等你决定，卡片上注明“自动审查无法判断，因此询问你 — *原因*”。"],[5278,"**时间**"],[5300,"**时间**、**模型**、**提供方**、**账户**、**接口**、**推理强度**、**响应方式**（**流式** 或 **整体**）、**尝试账户数**（轮换过几个账户）、**结束原因**。"],[5246,"**明细** 按四种方式分组，用标签页切换："],[4583,"**暂停中**"],[4712,"**暂无模型**：还没有任何可用的渠道。到渠道页登录一个免费站点或添加 API 密钥，然后点刷新。全新安装时 OpenCode Zen 和 Kilo 无需账号即可使用，见匿名渠道。"],[4412,"**更改工作区外的文件？**"],[4612,"**更新于**"],[4620,"**服务器错误**"],[4703,"**未知**"],[4531,"**未设置**"],[4128,"**本站**：本站取代了仓库原来的 `docs/` 目录，是 Hoshimi 唯一的文档。用户能看到的改动（命令、选项、配置键、端点、界面）要同时更新对应页面，中文和英文都要改，见文档站。"],[4610,"**来源**"],[5170,"**来自其他网站的图片和视频**"],[4882,"**来自其他网站的媒体。** 加载图片会让提供它的网站知道你正在阅读，而且地址中可以夹带对话内容，因此回复引用的其他网站上的图片、视频或音频，会先显示为一个注明网站的按钮（“加载来自 example.com 的图片”）。直接写在回复中的媒体（`data:` 地址）会立即显示。如需始终加载，在 **设置 › 外观** 中把 **来自其他网站的图片和视频** 设为 **始终加载**。"],[4069,"**查询**：`src/api/queries/` 按领域封装 Vue Query，查询键集中在 `queries/keys.ts`，层级结构，使某个前缀失效就使其下所有键失效。4xx 的 `ApiError` 不重试，其他失败最多重试 2 次；窗口获得焦点时不自动重新请求。"],[5167,"**标准**（默认）、**中**、**高**"],[4933,"**标题模型**"],[5017,"**标题模型**"],[4248,"**概览 › 接口**"],[4225,"**概览**"],[5337,"**概览**"],[4207,"**概览** 和 **设置 › 关于** 中的 **API 文档** 按钮只在没有设置工具访问密钥时出现：`/docs` 是一个普通页面，无法带上浏览器里保存的密钥。设置了密钥时，用带 `Authorization: Bearer <tool-access-key>` 的请求获取 `/openapi.json`，见 API 参考。"],[4720,"**概览** 是打开界面时的第一页，一眼看清网关现在的状态。页面从上到下分为 **今日**、**接口**、**渠道** 和 **服务器** 四部分；想看更多细节时，各部分都有按钮跳到对应的页面。"],[2410,"**概览** 页的 **接口** 区块列出各个接口地址，可以直接复制"],[4195,"**概览**、**模型**、**渠道**、**用量**、**Playground**；**设置** 在导航栏底部。窗口较窄时导航栏变成底部的标签栏。有渠道需要处理时，**渠道** 上会显示数字角标"],[5115,"**模型 API 密钥**"],[4665,"**模型 id**"],[4228,"**模型**"],[5249,"**模型**"],[5280,"**模型**"],[5339,"**模型**"],[416,"**模型** 页"],[2416,"**模型** 页，或下文的 curl 命令"],[4661,"**模型** 页列出网关此刻能回答的每一个模型 id，也就是客户端在请求的 `model` 字段中可以填写的值。模型来自所有已启用的渠道：各站点自己公布的模型列表，加上渠道和账号配置中声明的模型。想让某个模型出现在这里，先在渠道页给它的提供商登录或添加账号。"],[465,"**模型** 页和 **渠道 › 网络** 会显示目录失败的原因、已知的 HTTP 状态码、目标主机和处理建议。HTTP 200 仍可能表示返回内容不是有效的模型列表。404/405 时检查 API 地址；如果上游不提供模型列表接口，可在账号中手动填写模型 ID。同一渠道的另一个账号请求成功不会清除本轮失败提示，完整刷新成功后才会清除。界面和目录失败日志不包含原始响应正文、完整请求 URL 或密钥。"],[5372,"**模型**、**Playground** 和 **设置** 中的模型选择器共用同一份模型目录。目录以流的方式加载：先显示缓存中的模型，各提供商再分别补上自己的结果，加载中显示 **正在加载供应商：已完成/总数**。某个提供商失败或超时（20 秒）时会列出它和原因，并保留已有的模型，点 **重试** 再加载一次。详见模型。"],[7585,"**模型**：`MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview`、`MiniMax-M3`、`MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed`、`MiniMax-M2.7`。M3.1 系列必须使用自适应思考，适配器在未指定级别时也会打开；M2.7 没有声明级别，调用方的级别不会转发。"],[7653,"**模型**：`sn-sensenova-6-8-flash`、`sn-glm-5-3`、`sn-kimi-k3`、`sn-deepseek-v4-1-flash` 等固定列表。"],[7637,"**模型**：CodeBuddy 回退列表 16 个（hy4/hy3、deepseek-v4、glm-5.x、kimi、minimax-m3）；WorkBuddy 23 个（含 `default-model` 等别名、gpt-5.x、gemini-3.5-flash、glm、kimi）。WorkBuddy 会按模型家族切换 User-Agent。"],[7619,"**模型**：两个站点的模型表不同。国际版 17 个（`auto`、`ultimate`、`performance`、`efficient`、`smodel`、`cmodel`、`qmodel_38max` 等），国内版 14 个（含国内独有的 `q37fmodel`、`gm51model`）；把一个站点独有的 ID 发给另一个站点必然失败。"],[7630,"**模型**：从 `algo/api/v2/model/list` 实时发现。对外 ID 是目录 `display_name` 去掉空白（`Auto`、`Qwen3.8-Max`、`DeepSeek-V4-Pro` 等），上游 key（`auto`、`qmodel_38max`、`dmodel`）只在请求内部传递。上下文取目录中最大的可选值（常见 1M），输出上限 131072，思考菜单来自各模型自己的 `thinking_config`。能力查询会先刷新目录，再读取思考菜单，因此发现成功时，首次 `/v1/models` 响应和管理目录就会包含实时的 `efforts` 与 `effort_default` 字段；后续读取复用模型缓存。两个版本的静态回退表不同。"],[7643,"**模型**：从站点的内置模型列表发现（排除 `-VL` 模型），失败时回退到 `GLM-5.x`、`deepseek-v4*`、`openpangu-2.0-*` 等。"],[5815,"**模型**：从网关的 `/v1/config` 读取推理地址和模型列表。账号的 `gateway` 字段可以替换默认网关 `https://radius.pi.dev`。"],[7662,"**模型**：从账号的模型目录读取，或在账号中用 `models` 声明。"],[7666,"**模型**：优先读取实时目录（账号余额能覆盖的其他模型也会出现）。目录不可达时回退到 7 个免费 ID：`glm-4.7-flash`、`glm-4.5-flash`、`glm-4-flash-250414`、`glm-z1-flash`、`glm-4.6v-flash`、`glm-4.1v-thinking-flash`、`glm-4v-flash`。"],[7575,"**模型**：只有一个 `gemini-3.8-flash`，思考级别 `low`、`medium`、`high`、`tiered`（未指定时为 `medium`）。级别决定思考预算，并作为后缀拼到上游模型名上。"],[7590,"**模型**：回退列表包括 `DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Official`、`Doubao-Seed-2.1-Pro`、`glm-5.2`、`kimi-k3` 等。TRAE 只提供上下文长度表，不提供思考菜单，调用方的 `reasoning_effort` 原样转发。"],[4846,"**模型**：服务端提供的任意模型。换模型时推理强度会重置为自动。"],[4903,"**模型以请求过长为由拒绝时**：压缩对话后重新发送请求；仍然过长时，再截短较长的工具输出发送一次。即使关闭了自动压缩也会这样处理；"],[4744,"**模型列表**"],[7632,"**模型繁忙**：`10605` 且 `serviceAvailable` 是调度器的答复。ready 的请求按提示延时重发（有次数上限，并换新的 `request_id`）；真正排队的请求作为带等待时间的限流返回，交由调用方调度。"],[5306,"**模型输入 / 输出**：渠道转换前的输入，以及网关标准化后的输出分块。Playground 后台的每轮模型调用也会记录这些内容。"],[5364,"**正在进行（N）** 为每个调用显示一张卡片：模型、提供方 / 账户（还在选账户时显示 **正在选择账户…**）、接口、推理强度、尝试过的账户数，一条 **等待中**、**思考中**、**回答中** 的进度条，以及 **首字延迟**、**输出 Token**（在站点报告最终数量之前是按已输出文本的估算，带 ≈）和 **tok/s**。"],[4729,"**正在进行**"],[7628,"**正文编码**：对话正文使用 Qoder 自定义 Base64（`Encode=1`）——替换字母表、`$` 补位、三段块重排。`region/endpoints` 的响应也是同一编码。"],[4911,"**此回复失败。** 及原因"],[5150,"**每日签到**"],[7621,"**注意**：官方客户端走加密的 WASM 推理路径，Hoshimi 使用公开的 OpenAI 兼容端点，该端点可能返回 `503`。请求头、模型和续期行为一致，不代表推理效果与官方客户端完全相同。"],[7657,"**注意**：登录时生成的 `uuid` 和 `firstKeyfrom` 会随续期请求发送，不要从账号中删除，否则续期失败。"],[7580,"**注意**：适配器在调用方的系统提示词之前加上 ZCode 官方客户端的身份说明和环境说明，并在第一条用户消息前插入日期提醒。调用方的系统提示词仍然保留，排在这些内容之后。"],[5163,"**浅色**、**深色**、**跟随系统**（默认）。顶栏的主题按钮也可以切换"],[4191,"**浏览器。** 大约一秒后浏览器打开 `http://127.0.0.1:10600`，地址随即变成 `http://127.0.0.1:10600/#/overview`。页面地址都在 `#` 之后，可以直接收藏，例如 `#/playground`、`#/settings?tab=access`。"],[7625,"**浏览器登录（仅国际版）**：不加 `--manual` 的 `hoshimi login qodercli` 会打开 Qoder 设备授权页并轮询授权结果，同一会话仍可粘贴 PAT，两者先到先用。国内版没有设备流程。浏览器凭据不含 PAT，因此续期走 `{center}/algo/api/v3/user/refresh_token`，而不是重新交换。"],[4543,"**添加账号**"],[5814,"**添加账号**：`hoshimi login radius`（设备码登录，令牌可续期），或在 **添加账号** 中填 API 密钥。"],[7665,"**添加账号**：在 bigmodel.cn 控制台创建 API 密钥，然后在 **渠道** › **Zhipu GLM (BigModel)** 中 **添加账号**，或写入 `config.json`。"],[4231,"**渠道**"],[5341,"**渠道**"],[4246,"**渠道** → 选择站点 → **登录** 或 **添加账号**"],[412,"**渠道** 页"],[5354,"**渠道** 页中的 Kilo 渠道"],[327,"**渠道** 页显示读数：10% 及以下为红色，25% 及以下为琥珀色，过时的读数标为 **（旧）**。"],[4516,"**渠道** 页管理模型从哪里来。一个渠道就是一个提供商：免费站点（如 Cline、TRAE、Qoder）、云服务（如 Azure、Bedrock、Vertex）、本地服务（如 Ollama、LM Studio），或者 `agg` 聚合账号。每个渠道下可以有多个账号，网关在账号之间轮换。各提供商的区别和选择方法见渠道概念。"],[2137,"**渠道的密钥变量。** `hoshimi stations` 的 **Key env** 一列（如 `ZENMUX_API_KEY`）以及其他上游工具惯用的密钥变量，Hoshimi 都不读取。渠道的凭据只来自 `config.json` 中的账户，避免出现第二个来源。"],[3921,"**渠道适配器**：用 `httpx.MockTransport` 构造适配器的客户端，检查请求的地址、头和体，以及 `stream_raw` 产出的分片类型。例子见渠道适配器。"],[5274,"**点明细中的一行，下面的调用记录就只显示这一行的调用**；记录上方出现一个带名称的标记，点它取消筛选。"],[4757,"**版本**"],[5174,"**版本**"],[5294,"**状态**"],[5290,"**用时**"],[4234,"**用量**"],[5343,"**用量**"],[5358,"**用量** 页中的某一天"],[5356,"**用量** 页的 **30 天** 范围"],[414,"**用量** 页的调用列表"],[5197,"**用量** 页记录经过网关的每一次调用：用了多少 Token、缓存命中多少、首字延迟和生成速度、由哪个渠道的哪个账号回答、是否失败。数据保存在数据目录的 `hoshimi.db` 中，重启后仍在。用量是如何记录和统计的，见用量统计。"],[5001,"**用量历史** 部分："],[4541,"**登录**"],[7636,"**登录**：`hoshimi login buddy` 或 `hoshimi login workbuddy` 打开外部登录页，网关轮询登录状态，不需要本地回调。"],[7569,"**登录**：`hoshimi login cline` 默认走 WorkOS 设备授权，然后向 Cline 注册换取站点令牌。令牌带 `workos:` 前缀保存，每次请求原样发送。"],[7641,"**登录**：`hoshimi login codearts` 打开华为云门户授权页，回调到本机 10000 以上的随机端口（门户拒绝更低的端口），换取令牌时附带 DPoP 证明；回调等待最长 5 分钟，支持手动粘贴回调地址。"],[7660,"**登录**：`hoshimi login codex` 打开 OpenAI 授权页，回调固定到本机 `localhost:1455`（这是 Codex 客户端注册的回调地址），该端口必须空闲；同一时间只能进行一次 Codex 登录。支持手动粘贴回调地址。"],[7574,"**登录**：`hoshimi login gemini` 打开 Google 授权页，回调到本机 `localhost` 的临时端口；支持手动粘贴回调地址。登录时把公开桌面客户端的 `client_id` 和 `client_secret` 一并存入账号，续期不需要额外配置。`options.client_id` / `options.client_secret` 可以覆盖它们。"],[7656,"**登录**：`hoshimi login lobsterai` 打开 `lobsterai.youdao.com` 门户，回调到本机临时端口；支持手动粘贴回调地址。"],[7647,"**登录**：`hoshimi login loomy` 在本机启动一个页面显示微信二维码，扫码确认即可。首次使用的微信账号需要在同一页面绑定手机号（获取并填写短信验证码）。页面只在 `127.0.0.1` 上提供，需要用本机浏览器打开。"],[7584,"**登录**：`hoshimi login minimax` 使用 `account.minimax.cn` 的设备码，同时校验 PKCE。"],[7618,"**登录**：`hoshimi login qoder` 或 `hoshimi login qodercn` 打开 `qoder.com` / `qoder.cn` 的设备授权页，网关轮询结果，不需要本地回调。登录时生成一个 `machine_id`，续期请求会带上它，账号要一直保留它。"],[7624,"**登录**：`hoshimi login qodercli --manual`（或 `qodercli-cn`）打开账号的集成页面并等待粘贴个人访问令牌。令牌在 https\\://qoder.com/account/integrations（国际版）或 https\\://qoder.com.cn/account/integrations（国内版）创建。网页界面中 **登录** 会显示同样的粘贴框，**添加账号 → 个人访问令牌** 则直接保存令牌。导出 `QODER_API_KEY` / `QODER_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` / `QODER_PAT`（国内版为 `QODERCN_*`）时，渠道无需交互即可登录。"],[7652,"**登录**：`hoshimi login raccoon` 打开站点的微信扫码页，由网关轮询结果，不需要本地回调。"],[7589,"**登录**：`hoshimi login trae` 打开 `www.trae.cn` 的登录页，站点把令牌直接回调到本机，端口优先 18080，被占用时换一个空闲端口；支持手动粘贴回调地址。"],[7578,"**登录**：`hoshimi login zcode` 由站点中转完成，用智谱账号授权，不需要本地回调，适合远程服务器。登录时生成并保存一个固定的 `device_mid`。"],[7570,"**登录方式**：渠道详情的 **网络** 部分有 **Cline 登录方式**，可选 **设备码（SDK）**（默认）或 **浏览器（扩展）**，对应 `providers.cline.options.client_profile` 的 `sdk` 和 `extension`。扩展方式在本机 48801–48811 端口中找一个接收回调，支持手动粘贴回调地址。新账号记录登录时的方式，切换选项只影响之后的登录。"],[5095,"**监听地址**"],[5090,"**监听地址** 部分（副标题 **重启后生效。**）："],[2438,"**直接写 `id`**，如 `big-pickle`。Hoshimi 按渠道顺序找第一个提供这个模型的渠道。只启用了一个渠道时，目录里没有的模型名也会原样发给它。"],[4645,"**直连**"],[5139,"**直连**"],[4545,"**立即续期**"],[4595,"**立即续期** 和 