rs; system language detection"],[4798,"Enter"],[12619,"Enter"],[14859,"Enter an **API key** if the local server requires one, otherwise leave it blank; restrict the models in **Model IDs** if you want. Click **Save account**."],[12961,"Enter an HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 address in **Proxy URL** and click **Save**; **Clear** goes back to automatic"],[12469,"Enter an HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 address in **Proxy URL** and click **Save**; **Clear** goes back to inheriting"],[13315,"Enter the **API key**. Leave **Account ID (optional)** blank to let the gateway name the account, then click **Save account**."],[12022,"Enter the key in **Tool access key**."],[10348,"Entry"],[11784,"Environment"],[9860,"Environment variables"],[10064,"Environment variables"],[11646,"Environment variables"],[10312,"Environment variables (auto mode)"],[10631,"Error at start"],[8414,"Error code and a short explanation on failure"],[9604,"Error codes and statuses:"],[8422,"Error explanations are kept to one line of at most 160 characters, with anything shaped like a key (`Bearer …`, `sk-…`, random strings of 32 characters or more, and so on) replaced with `***`. An upstream error that carries a status is recorded only as `upstream returned HTTP <status>`, without the upstream's body in this summary (the separate payload detail can retain it); error frames inside a stream keep their explanation, shortened and masked by the same rules."],[10876,"Error message"],[9520,"Error shapes"],[8518,"Errors"],[10026,"Errors"],[10159,"Errors"],[10947,"Errors"],[11122,"Errors and account rotation"],[9390,"Errors found before the question is kept (no model, an unknown `parent_id` or attachment) are a plain `400` or `404`, not a stream."],[9658,"Errors in the stream"],[10188,"Errors on `/v1` use OpenAI's shape, and the SDK raises the matching exception (`openai.NotFoundError`, `openai.BadRequestError` and so on):"],[8666,"Errors the gateway raises itself (validation, routing, conversion) use Anthropic's shape, with `error.type` following the status (see API overview)."],[9111,"Errors: a JSON body `{\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"detail\": {}}` with `400` (`invalid_input`), `404` (`not_found`) or `409` (`conflict`)."],[4802,"Esc"],[12623,"Esc"],[12708,"Esc or **Close** closes it."],[4887,"Esc 或 **关闭** 关闭查看器。"],[12743,"Even the compacted conversation is too long: start a new chat, or branch from an earlier message"],[8640,"Event"],[8998,"Event"],[8676,"Every /api/v1 management endpoint the Web UI uses: app information, settings, providers and accounts, the model catalogue, availability probes, credential renewal, balances and check-in, sign-in, usage statistics, with each endpoint's method, purpose and authentication."],[8655,"Every 15 seconds while waiting on the upstream, only between complete events"],[9644,"Every account of the provider says the model does not exist"],[8287,"Every account of the upstream said this model does not exist (404, 410, or a body that clearly says so), so for 10 minutes the gateway stops sending requests for it; three such answers within 10 minutes keep it that way for the rest of the run. Once the upstream is back, clear the record with `POST /api/v1/models/unavailable/reset` or restart the server. The rules are in Model and account behaviour."],[10113,"Every call, failed ones included, appears on the **Usage** page with its error and the provider and account that served it."],[8253,"Every channel is turned off, the two keyless ones included. Enable one (`hoshimi config set providers.kilo.enabled true`) or add an account to a channel."],[13576,"Every channel on this page needs your own cloud account. Pick the channel ID that matches the upstream endpoint, protocol, credentials and plan; a similar model name does not make credentials interchangeable. For example, `gemini` is Code Assist (see Free stations), `google` is the Gemini Developer API and `google-vertex` is Vertex AI; `amazon-bedrock` and `bedrock-mantle` are two services configured separately."],[8423,"Every channel's usage is first normalized to OpenAI's fields, then recorded:"],[11216,"Every chunk `stream_raw` yields is a dictionary with a `type` key. Whether the upstream speaks OpenAI Chat, Anthropic Messages, Gemini or TRAE SOLO, the adapter turns it into these:"],[12702,"Every code block, diagram and SVG has a toolbar for a head: an icon for what it holds (code, a command, a diff, a diagram, an image, a page), its language (**Python**, **Bash**…, or **Text** when the block names none), and its buttons, with **Copy code** last. HTML written directly in a reply (outside a code block) is shown as text."],[12196,"Every command (`shell`, `exec_command`, and `write_stdin` when it types), every file change, and reading anything outside the workspace"],[9703,"Every command takes these two options; the tables leave them out:"],[9881,"Every command, `serve` included, reads both."],[13003,"Every config key is in Configuration file."],[9233,"Every conversation uses the tools `playground.tools` turns on; a conversation has no tools of its own. (`tools_on` and `tools_off`, which older clients send, are ignored.)"],[8487,"Every counter, chart and call record is cleared; this cannot be undone. Calls in flight are still recorded when they end."],[8757,"Every date with usage"],[9861,"Every environment variable Hoshimi reads: its own HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR and HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL, the standard variables behind the default data folder and proxies, the credential variables the cloud SDKs read, the variables set for the Playground's commands, and the ones it deliberately ignores."],[8664,"Every error uses Anthropic's shape:"],[12794,"Every field **saves on its own** as it changes; there is no overall save button. Switches and selections save at once, text and number fields when you leave them (or press Enter), and list fields each time a value is added or removed. A save shows **Saved**; a field that needs a restart shows **Saved · Takes effect after a restart.** An invalid value shows the reason and leaves the configuration unchanged."],[9685,"Every hoshimi command: what it does, its arguments and options with their defaults, its output, the --json fields and examples, taken from each command's --help and the source."],[11672,"Every kind of check in Hoshimi: the pytest layout and shared fixtures, how provider and route tests are written, the Web UI's Vitest rule tests, the generated-type check, check_layout.py for sideways overflow in real browsers, and how CI runs them."],[8230,"Every log line (written to stderr; there is no log file). `HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG hoshimi serve` or `hoshimi serve --debug` adds detail"],[12779,"Every model call the Playground makes is recorded in Usage like any other call, under its own origin: `playground` for replies, `playground-title` for titles, `playground-vision` for image descriptions, `playground-compact` for compaction summaries and `playground-review` for automatic reviews of tool calls."],[12719,"Every model has a **context window**: how much of a conversation it can read at once. The ring beside the send button shows how much of it is left; press it, or type `/status`, for the details. The window is the one the model's station lists. When a station refuses a request as too long and names its real limit, that limit is used from then on."],[13159,"Every model you can call: search, abilities, context length, availability probes, and a shortcut to try one in the Playground"],[9553,"Every other path"],[11922,"Every page's root, the `.body` of `AppDialog` and `SideSheet`, and `DataTable`'s `.row` use `var(--app-scroll-lane)` in `padding-inline-end`"],[11136,"Every provider (a \"channel\" in the Web UI) is a `Provider` subclass in `hoshimi/core/providers/`: it holds the provider's accounts and options, knows how to send one turn upstream with one account, and turns the upstream stream into **normalized chunks**. The shared parts, account rotation, retries, cooldowns and the catalogue cache, live in the base class; an adapter writes only what is particular to its station."],[8485,"Every record has a sequence number `seq` that never repeats, even after the statistics are cleared, so it is safe as a paging cursor."],[10596,"Every request (WebSockets included) goes through these four checks in order. The first failure answers the request at once; nothing reaches upstream:"],[10320,"Every request Hoshimi sends upstream (model catalogues, inference, login, token refresh, balances, check-in) picks its route from a network policy: direct, or through a proxy. There is one global default and each channel can override it. This page shows how to write these policies, when they apply, and where to look when something fails."],[9575,"Every request passes these checks, in this order, before it reaches an endpoint. A request that fails one gets:"],[10875,"Every save (Web UI, API, `hoshimi config set`) and every start (`hoshimi serve`, `hoshimi check`) validates the whole configuration first; when it fails, the file is left as it was. The possible errors:"],[11763,"Every scrolling area in the Web UI scrolls in one direction (`.app-scroll` down, `.app-scroll-x` sideways, such as code blocks, tables and the stepper), so a sideways scrollbar anywhere else is a layout bug. The unit tests can only read the source; `scripts/check_layout.py` finds these bugs in real browsers."],[11913,"Every scrolling area scrolls through `.app-scroll`; see below"],[11025,"Every service that holds the settings object (renewal, check-in, login, update checks, the network client) is pointed at the new one, so none of them later writes the old configuration back over the file."],[10494,"Every setting and the channel accounts' credentials"],[11639,"Every statement must be backed by the code; when old documentation or memory disagrees with the code, the code wins. What cannot be confirmed is left out."],[12053,"Every station and service you can connect. The filter above switches between **All**, **In use**, **Needs attention**, **Not set up** and **Off**; choose a channel and its accounts, today's usage, allowance and network settings open beside the list, with a **Sign in** or **Add account** button"],[9654,"Every stream is Server-Sent Events (`text/event-stream`). Once the response headers are out, the status is fixed at `200`, and a later failure can only be reported inside the stream; do not judge the outcome by the status alone:"],[10357,"Every target"],[10673,"Everyday use"],[11558,"Everything CI checks: `lint`, `typecheck-py`, `test-py`, `test-web`, `typegen-check`"],[14925,"Everything else defaults to Chat. The account's `protocol` or `options.model_protocols` overrides this."],[8690,"Everything the Web UI does goes through these endpoints, and scripts can call them directly. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600/api/v1`."],[8176,"Evidence"],[8877,"Exact filters; `origin` is `chat`, `responses`, `messages`, `classify`, `playground` and so on"],[10285,"Example"],[15538,"Example channel IDs"],[11134,"Example: Kilo's device-code login"],[11050,"Exception"],[11255,"Exception"],[6103,"Existing custom agg accounts continue to work."],[13922,"Existing custom agg accounts continue to work."],[6010,"Existing minimax is the Agent account service; retain its ID."],[13829,"Existing minimax is the Agent account service; retain its ID."],[11053,"Exit code"],[9967,"Exit codes"],[8611,"Expanded from this request's own `tools` into the tool's definition as text; a reference to an undeclared tool is refused"],[7388,"Experiential Labs"],[15207,"Experiential Labs"],[8458,"Expired call records are pruned on a write, at most once a minute. A change to `server.stats_keep_days` applies from the next pruning."],[10864,"Expiry time (Unix time in milliseconds or seconds, as a number or string). `expire_time`, or an ISO date in `expiry`, are also read. A renewable account with no recorded expiry is renewed every round"],[10136,"Explanation"],[8534,"Extension fields are not check