t_quota` and `overloaded_error` also use shared recovery. An untyped HTTP 429 is temporary throttling unless the response explicitly reports an exhausted quota."],[8686,"Start"],[12588,"Start a chat"],[12137,"Start a command that keeps running, read its output, type into it, stop it"],[12647,"Start a new chat"],[11764,"Start a server first (`hoshimi serve` or `python scripts/dev.py dev`), ideally with a conversation in the Playground, so the chat list, the editor and the menus have something to open. The script:"],[8747,"Start a sign-in"],[8733,"Start an availability round"],[12877,"Start commands that keep running (servers, watchers), read their output, type into them and stop them"],[10072,"Start Hoshimi and add an account on a provider with a Messages endpoint (such as an Anthropic API key) on the **Channels** page; see Channels."],[7825,"Start the login"],[15615,"Start the server"],[9711,"Start the server: the OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible API plus the Web UI."],[8390,"Start time"],[15602,"Start with the anonymous lanes, which are on by default and need no account."],[8242,"Start-up, `hoshimi check` and `hoshimi config set` validate the configuration first, with messages such as `network.proxy is required in proxy mode` or `playground.compact_threshold must be between 0.5 and 0.95.`. Each is explained in the validation section of Configuration file."],[12138,"Starting one, or typing into one, only in **Automatic review** and **Ask first**"],[12243,"State"],[12344,"State"],[12396,"State"],[10220,"Stateless"],[11602,"Static files copied to the output as they are"],[8175,"Station"],[15291,"Station"],[13306,"Station presets"],[8719,"Station presets an `agg` account can name"],[13440,"Station rules (chat-model filters, free marks, capability tables) are matched by the `base_url` address, not the `preset` name: an account that says `preset: sambanova` but points `base_url` elsewhere does not get SambaNova's rules. A custom address gets no station rules at all."],[15310,"Station-mediated link, no local callback"],[13310,"Station-specific handling"],[8163,"Stations pi-free reached with an API key are accounts of the `agg` channel in Hoshimi. Name the station with `preset` instead of writing its address:"],[8224,"Stations refusing images or tools"],[8305,"Stations that need a local callback listen on `127.0.0.1`: Codex always uses port 1455 (a busy port gives `codex: cannot bind the local callback port 1455: …`; `codex: another login is already in progress` means another Codex login has not finished), and Cline's browser method uses 48801–48811 (`cline: no available callback port (48801–48811)`). Close whatever holds those ports and retry."],[15289,"Stations that need a local callback listen only on `127.0.0.1` (or `localhost`) for the duration of the sign-in, never on a public interface. When the browser is on another machine, paste the callback with `--manual` or the Web UI's **Authorization code or callback URL**. The one flow without manual input (Loomy) has to be finished in a browser on the same machine."],[8155,"Stations that need a login: sign in again"],[8745,"Stations that offer an interactive sign-in"],[8165,"Stations that sign in through a browser, such as Cline, Qoder and ZCode, need one new login with `hoshimi login <channel>` or **Sign in** in the Web UI; see Free stations."],[9823,"Stations with an interactive login: `anthropic`, `buddy`, `cline`, `codearts`, `codex`, `eac`, `gemini`, `github-copilot`, `kilo`, `kimi-coding`, `lobsterai`, `loomy`, `meta`, `minimax`, `openai`, `openrouter`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `qodercli`, `qodercli-cn`, `raccoon`, `radius`, `trae`, `workbuddy`, `xai`, `zcode`."],[11142,"Stations with their own protocol, authentication or quirks (Cline, TRAE, ZCode, Qoder, MiniMax, Gemini, CodeBuddy, Kilo, OpenCode…)"],[9578,"Status"],[9606,"Status"],[8255,"Status and code"],[8203,"Status classification"],[12108,"Steer a reply while it works"],[9101,"Steering"],[5584,"StepFun"],[13403,"StepFun"],[90