other"],[11321,"Supported authentication, such as `(\"api_key\",)` or `(\"api_key\", \"oauth\")`"],[7992,"Supports tool calls; `null` means unknown"],[12863,"Switch"],[12965,"Switch"],[12119,"Switch (in Settings)"],[11026,"Switching `server.check_updates` starts or stops the update timer at once."],[12325,"Switching a channel on and off"],[13507,"Switching the channel off on the **Channels** page does the same. To turn it back on, set `enabled` to `true` or delete the entry."],[10103,"Symptom"],[10135,"Symptom"],[10475,"System"],[10659,"System"],[9866,"System variables Hoshimi also reads"],[13066,"Tab"],[9179,"Take back an attachment not yet sent"],[12152,"Takes a patch in the Codex `apply_patch` format, so a model that knows the tool from Codex knows it here:"],[10915,"Takes effect"],[11294,"Takes images, thinks, supports tools (`tools` is `None` when unknown)"],[11088,"Taking `POST /v1/chat/completions`:"],[11304,"Taking the Zhipu GLM provider (`providers/zhipu.py`), an OpenAI-compatible station, as the example:"],[10970,"Talks to the server over HTTP only"],[10539,"Task"],[11527,"Task"],[12593,"Temporary chats"],[10449,"Temporary limits such as `1002`, `1039`, `1041`; account quotas such as `1008`, `2056`; authentication errors `1004`, `2049`. Supports `base_resp.status_code`; unknown nonzero values remain errors"],[15454,"Tencent CodeBuddy (`buddy`, `copilot.tencent.com`) and WorkBuddy international (`workbuddy`, `www.workbuddy.ai`) share one protocol on two hosts."],[15339,"Tencent CodeBuddy / WorkBuddy international"],[11748,"Test"],[11671,"Testing"],[11832,"Tests"],[11747,"Tests sit next to the files they test (`*.test.ts`). Besides the component, store and query tests, a few suites check rules that apply everywhere:"],[8593,"Text"],[12676,"Text files"],[7862,"That string"],[8448,"The **24 hours** and single-day views"],[8451,"The **7 days**, **30 days** and **90 days** views"],[13179,"The **Access** tab of **Settings**"],[12391,"The **Accounts** section lists each account of the channel:"],[12028,"The **API reference** button on **Overview** and under **Settings › About** appears only while no tool access key is set: `/docs` is a plain page and cannot send the key saved in the browser. With a key set, fetch `/openapi.json` with `Authorization: Bearer <tool-access-key>`, see API reference."],[13094,"The **Calls** section lists every call in the range, newest first; scrolling down loads older ones. When the range runs to now, calls that finish join the top of the list."],[8233,"The **Channels** page"],[12337,"The **Channels** page manages where models come from. A channel is one provider: a free station (such as Cline, TRAE, Qoder), a cloud service (such as Azure, Bedrock, Vertex), a local server (such as Ollama, LM Studio), or `agg` aggregator accounts. A channel can hold several accounts, and the gateway rotates between them. How providers differ and how to choose is in Providers."],[8148,"The **Channels** page shows the reading: red at 10% or less, amber at 25% or less, and stale readings marked **· old**."],[12842,"The **Context** section, what happens as a Playground chat nears its model's context window:"],[12371,"The **Enabled** switch writes `providers.<id>.enabled` in `config.json` and applies at once. Switched off, the channel no longer serves and its models leave the catalogue; its accounts stay in the configuration and come back when you switch it on. Adding an account to a channel that is off switches it back on."],[15627,"The **Endpoints** section lists the addresses clients use (`/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/v1/messages` and more), each with a copy button."],[10231,"The **Endpoints** section of the **Overview** page lists each endpoint with a copy button"],[12797,"The **General** section:"],[12927,"The **Keys** section. The two keys are independent; leaving one empty turns off key checks for its APIs:"],[12909,"The **Listening address** section (subtitle **Takes effect after a restart.**):"],[12018,"The **Live activity** button: shows how many calls are running, and opens today's tokens, calls and cache hit rate with the calls running now and just finished. Next to it, the theme button cycles **Light**, **Dark** and **System**"],[8488,"The **Live activity** panel in the top bar shows the calls in flight (**Waiting**, **Thinking**, **Answering**, **Calling tools**), today's totals and the calls that just finished. It reads a server-sent event stream:"],[12614,"The **Model** menu in the composer lists every model the server advertises; type to search when the list is long. The first model is picked when nothing is chosen yet. From the Models page you can also open the Playground on one model, which starts a new chat with it."],[15629,"The **Model** picker under the message box has already chosen the first model in the catalogue; click it to search for and pick another."],[8237,"The **Models** page"],[12482,"The **Models** page lists every model id the gateway can answer for right now: the values a client may put in a request's `model` field. They come from every enabled channel: the model lists the stations publish, plus the models declared in channel and account configuration. To make a model appear here, sign in or add an account for its provider on the Channels page first."],[10262,"The **Models** page shows whether each model reads images, reasons, calls tools and which effort levels it has; see Models."],[10237,"The **Models** page, or the curl command below"],[12611,"The **Playground** is a chat app built into the Web UI. It talks to models through the same gateway your clients use, so it is the quickest way to try a model, check an account, or see exactly what a request looks like. Chats are kept on the server, in the data folder, so they outlive the page and the process and come back from any browser."],[12829,"The **Playground** section, how the Playground talks to models:"],[12807,"The **Requests** section, limits applied to every request the gateway accepts:"],[12423,"The **Today** section shows the channel's **Tokens**, **Calls**, **Cache hit** and **Failed** for today (the server's local day)."],[12820,"The **Usage history** section:"],[13016,"The **Usage** page records every call that goes through the gateway: how many tokens, how much was read from cache, time to first token and generation speed, which account of which channel answered, and whether it failed. The data is kept in `hoshimi.db` in the data folder and survives a restart. How usage is recorded and counted is in Usage statistics."],[13278,"The `--config` option and the `HOSHIMI_CONFIG` environment variable are gone, and a configuration file in the working directory is neither read nor migrated. Before starting the new release, move the old file to the path that `hoshimi config path` prints."],[9761,"The `--json` fields:"],[9789,"The `--json` shape:"],[10250,"The `/api/*` management API, the Web UI, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`"],[11149,"The `agg` aggregator"],[12389,"The `agg` aggregator's form is different: under **Station**, pick a station from the searchable list, or choose **Custom address…** and enter the station's OpenAI-compatible root in **Base URL**; then the **API key**. `hoshimi stations` lists the stations; see Aggregator accounts."],[9832,"The `config` commands read and write `config.json` in the data folder. Keys are dotted, such as `server.port`, `security.allow_cidrs` or `providers.kilo.enabled`. Every key is listed in Configuration."],[9482,"The `Content-Type` decides how it is kept: `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, `image/webp` or `image/gif` as an image; any `text/*` type, or `application/json`, `xml`, `yaml`, `x-yaml`, `javascript`, `x-sh`, `sql` or `toml`, as UTF-8 text. Anything else, or an empty body, is a `400`. The server keeps what it is given: scaling images down and extracting PDF text are done by the Web UI before upload. A model is sent at most 200,000 characters of a file's text."],[8173,"The `default`, `fast` and `pro` routing selectors pi-free builds locally for LLM7 are not added: they are not the station's live model list, and the probe of the time did not show they could be used anonymously. This is a historical design reason, not a report on the endpoint's current health."],[11503,"The `dev` extra holds pytest, Ruff, ty, build and the official Anthropic SDK (the Messages regression tests use it). To cover the cloud providers' code as well, add `google` (`google-auth[requests]`) and `bedrock` (`boto3`): CI's type checks and tests install `.[dev,google,bedrock]`."],[10483,"The `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` environment variable moves it anywhere (`~` is expanded and the path is made absolute). The server and every command find the data directory through this variable, so for `hoshimi config`, `hoshimi login` and the rest to work on the same data, set the same value wherever you run them:"],[10667,"The `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` environment variable moves the whole data directory; the configuration is always `<data directory>/config.json`. When the file does not exist, every default applies. The other files in the data directory are described in Data directory and migration."],[9971,"The `hoshimi` command starts the server, and without a browser it can also check the configuration, list channels and models, sign into free stations and change settings. `python -m hoshimi` is exactly the same as `hoshimi`."],[10639,"The `Host` header the proxy forwards must be a loopback name or the listening address (such as `127.0.0.1:10600`), or the Host check refuses the request (`400 bad_host`)."],[9041,"The `limit` query parameter (1–1000) returns the first `limit` models and caps the wait for providers to refresh their catalogues at two seconds: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while the refresh continues in the background. Claude Code's model discovery uses `?limit=1000`. Without `limit`, the full catalogue is returned."],[9043,"The `model` of a request is resolved like this:"],[15234,"The `nvidia` channel connects to NVIDIA's hosted NIM inference service (`https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1`) over OpenAI Chat Completions. An account needs only an NVIDIA API key."],[11282,"The `on_route(provider_id, account_id, attempt)` callback of `stream_using` fires when an account yields its first chunk, so usage records the account that actually answered."],[11834,"The `package.json` scripts (run with `bun run <script>` in `hoshimi/webui`, or through `scripts/dev.py`):"],[8632,"The `request-id` response header equals the message `id` (`msg_…`)."],[8936,"The `usage` details depend on what the upstream reports; with no usage from the upstream every count is `0`."],[13031,"The 24 hours before"],[13557,"The account accepts any one of `api_key`, `access_token` or `token`."],[15238,"The account also accepts `access_token` in place of `api_key`, and `models` on the account declares a model list in place of the live catalogue; the channel option `options.base_url` replaces the default address. This upstream key is a different thing from the gateway's own model API key and management key; see Security."],[15576,"The account appears under **Accounts**. Adding an account also switches a disabled channel back on."],[11269,"The account cools down for `policy_block_seconds`, without renewal; next account"],[11266,"The account cools down: for the `Retry-After` header's time, else the reset time in the error body, else `quota_hold_seconds`; next account"],[10874,"The account fields and options specific to each channel (such as `base_url`, `preset` and `model_specs` for `agg`) are on the pages under Providers."],[10860,"The account id shown in the UI, usage statistics and logs. Defaults to `<channel>-<index>`"],[12392,"The account id."],[7886,"The account is neither the bundled relay nor has a `base_url`"],[7898,"The account was changed or removed during the login"],[13643,"The account's `protocol` field."],[7841,"The account's credential decides the mode:"],[15586,"The account's name, used in the UI, usage records and logs. When omitted the gateway names it (a login produces names like `cline-1a2b3c`; an unnamed entry is named by position, like `<id>-0`)."],[13321,"The account's name."],[13161,"The accounts of every provider (free stations, cloud services, local servers): sign-in, API keys, renewal, check-in, allowance and network route"],[11214,"The accounts one turn may use, in order; all of them by default, narrowed by `agg` to the accounts that list the model"],[15240,"The adapter reads the model list live and excludes recognised non-chat tasks: embeddings (`embed`), rerankers (`rerank`), `nvclip`, reward scorers (`-reward`), detectors (`-detector`), document parsers (`nemotron-parse`) and `gliner`. This is a task filter, not an outage list."],[13630,"The adapter translates messages, supported images, tool calls and results, usage and thinking signatures; a `thinking` object in the request body is passed upstream as an additional model field. Not every Bedrock model supports every feature, and model access is still decided by your AWS account."],[11034,"The address actually bound and the port asked for; the Settings page uses them to say \"the port was taken, so another was used\" or \"restart needed\""],[9751,"The address is written to `server.json` in the data folder, the line `SERVER_READY url=<address>` is printed on standard output, and `Hoshimi running on <address>` is logged. When listening on `0.0.0.0` or `::`, the printed address uses `127.0.0.1`."],[12917,"The address the server binds; by default only this machine can connect"],[13302,"The agg aggregator"],[15552,"The agg aggregator"],[13553,"The anonymous free pool is protected by no credential at all, and the upstreams behind the free models may log prompts. Do not send sensitive content through it."],[13515,"The anonymous lane aligns with captured OpenCode v2.2.1 requests. In a 2026-10-29 live check of `deepseek-v4.1-flash-free`, default Python/httpx returned `FreeUsageLimitError`; Python returned 200 after aligning both TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 cipher lists and ordering with Bun. This does not reproduce Bun's entire TLS fingerprint. Other network exits and future quota remain subject to upstream responses."],[10211,"The anonymous lane also declares the `read` and `shell` tools the upstream requires. A call to a tool the client did not declare never reaches the client: Hoshimi tells the model the tool is unavailable and lets it carry on answering."],[10210,"The anonymous lane derives a session id per conversation from `session_id`, `conversation_id` or `user` in the request body, in that order, and from the first user message when none is set. Two separate conversations that open with the same message share a session."],[13525,"The anonymous lane maps `exec_command`, `write_stdin` and `kill_session` to `terminal_execute`, `terminal_send` and `terminal_stop`, avoiding the upstream's `FreeUsageLimitError` rejection of that tool combination. Descriptions, parameters and execution behavior are preserved. History and forced choices use the same mapping, and responses restore the caller's original names. Numeric suffixes resolve collisions with existing caller tools. API-key accounts do not use this mapping."],[9483,"The answer is the attachment: `id`, `kind`, `name`, `mime`, `size`, `width`, `height`."],[10274,"The Anthropic SDKs, Claude Code"],[11967,"The API and the command line start from the same place: `hoshimi.core.context.build_services()` builds every service once into a `Services`. `core` does not know who calls it: `tests/core/test_architecture.py` makes sure it imports none of FastAPI, Starlette, Typer, Click, Uvicorn or Rich, and never refers to `hoshimi.api` or `hoshimi.cli`. Architecture starts from that rule."],[11544,"The API and Vite together; see above"],[11516,"The API server's port"],[10946,"The app factory"],[12187,"The approval mode decides which calls need approval, and who gives it: the review model or you. New chats start with **Settings › Tools › How tools run › When tools ask first**; each chat can choose its own."],[13122,"The arrows at the top right of the sheet (or the ↑ and ↓ keys) step to the **Newer call** and **Older call**."],[14858,"The authentication method is **Local server (optional key)**. **API base URL (optional)** is pre-filled with the default address; change it if your server is on another port."],[7878,"The authorization link expired; sign in again"],[7880,"The authorization was not completed in time"],[9326,"The automatic review denied that many of the reply's calls (3 in a row, or 10 in all), so it was stopped"],[11208,"The balance or quota window; returns a `BalanceOutcome` or `None`"],[8548,"The body goes out unchanged except that `model` becomes the upstream model name (`count_tokens` also drops `stream`). System arrays, content order, opaque signatures, tools, cache markers, `context_management`, structured output and future fields are all left for the upstream to validate."],[8917,"The body is a standard Chat Completions object. The fields Hoshimi reads itself:"],[12717,"The body is built on the server exactly as the reply was sent: the system prompt first, files inline, images as `data:` URLs (or as their descriptions, for a model that cannot read them), `reasoning_effort` when one was chosen, and the tool definitions with `tool_choice` when the chat has tools on. For a reply that used tools, it is the first round's request. Set `HOSHIMI_API_KEY` to your model API key, or drop the header when the server has none (see Access and security)."],[9081,"The body sent to `POST /v1/classify`:"],[11614,"The body starts with a short paragraph, then `##` sections."],[12657,"The box reads \"Ask anything — this chat won’t be saved\" while you are in one."],[10383,"The browser's own network settings"],[11506,"The built `dist/` ships in the wheel as package data. When `hoshimi serve` runs from a checkout with no `dist/index.html`, the server logs 