gram** the drawing again. It opens at its own size, or smaller to fit the column, but never below 60%, where its words would be too small to read; a frame shows at most 480 pixels of its height. A diagram larger than its frame fades out at the edges where there is more: drag it about, or scroll it sideways. Zoom it with Ctrl or ⌘ and the wheel, a pinch, or the head's **Zoom out** / **Zoom in** buttons; the percentage between them shows its size, and a click on it shows it at its actual size. **Fit to window** shows the whole diagram, and the arrows open it in the image viewer. A plain wheel still scrolls the chat. A diagram that cannot be drawn shows why, above its code"],[12377,"The dialog ends with **This sign-in expires at …**."],[9030,"The display name; equal to `id` when unknown"],[11706,"The docs site's tests and type-check; see Documentation site"],[11566,"The documentation site's tests and type-check"],[10351,"The domain and all its subdomains"],[10353,"The domain on that port"],[7823,"The EAC co-paid channel: enabling it with the bundled relay and a GitHub authorization, the worker and direct relay modes, account fields for your own relay, request signing, and common errors."],[10503,"The EAC GitHub authorization token, login name, avatar and save time"],[11000,"The effective configuration (`config.json` plus command-line overrides)"],[8962,"The effort level"],[8927,"The effort level; see \"Reasoning effort\" below"],[12783,"The eight tabs of the Settings page: General, Tools, Access, Security, Network, Automation, Appearance and About, what each field does and the config key behind it."],[11002,"The enabled providers and their HTTP clients; routes model names to providers"],[8653,"The end"],[11594,"The English version of the same page"],[11331,"The environment variable the reference project reads the key from; a record only, Hoshimi does not read it"],[10612,"The error body is `{\"code\": \"…\", \"message\": \"…\", \"detail\": {}}`; `/v1/messages` and `/v1