entication method**."],[14898,"The key, sent as `Authorization: Bearer` (an Anthropic API key is sent as `x-api-key`). `access_token` or `token` are also accepted. An account without a credential cannot be saved."],[13327,"The key, sent as `Authorization: Bearer`. `access_token` or `token` are also accepted."],[9571,"The keys are independent and each guards its own paths; a key that is not set means its paths check no key."],[10203,"The keys of `models` are Hoshimi model ids (an `id` from `/v1/models`, or `provider/model`); each `name` is what OpenCode displays. The models listed here appear in OpenCode's model list."],[8792,"The keys themselves are never returned."],[13173,"The Kilo channel on the **Channels** page"],[13075,"The kind of API the call came through; see below"],[11653,"The labels in `hoshimi/webui/src/i18n/en.ts` on English pages and in `zh-CN.ts` on Chinese pages, in bold"],[8048,"The ladder ceiling is lowered further by the model's output limit and by a smaller `max_tokens` from the caller, but never below 512; so with an explicit level, a caller limit below 512 is raised to 512. For menu models the minimum is 1."],[11894,"The language preference defaults to `auto`, which follows the browser's first language (`zh*` is Simplified Chinese, `ja*` Japanese, anything else English) and updates when the system language changes."],[11006,"The last availability verdict per model"],[12407,"The last renewal failed; the next round tries again"],[10521,"The latest"],[8004,"The latest availability probe verdict"],[8833,"The latest availability verdict, or `null` if never probed"],[8731,"The latest availability verdicts"],[8240,"The latest network result per channel and operation; see Network and proxies"],[8723,"The latest outcome of each kind of network operation per provider"],[10525,"The latest per model"],[7860,"The latest token in `eac-user.json`, read on every request, so a new login applies at once"],[11995,"The layered Python + Vue skeleton Hoshimi follow