src/`."],[11478,"The Web UI: bun"],[7983,"The Web UI's **Models** page and the Playground load the catalogue through `GET /api/v1/catalog/stream` (SSE): cached results come first, then each channel's fresh result as it arrives. At most 8 fetches run at once; a round waits at most 20 seconds, marks unfinished channels as timed out and keeps the models already received. The standard `/v1/models` stays plain JSON."],[7908,"The Web UI's **Settings** › **About** also shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**."],[10487,"the Web UI's **Settings** › **About** shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**;"],[10671,"The Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages, or `PATCH /api/v1/settings`"],[9107,"The Web UI's Playground does everything through these routes, so a script can do the same: keep conversations, stream replies, run the tools and answer their approvals. Everything a model is sent (the system prompt, file text, image descriptions, earlier tool calls) is put together on the server; a client only says what to add and where."],[11984,"The Web UI's TypeScript types are generated from the server's OpenAPI document (`src/api/schema.d.ts`) and committed; CI regenerates them and fails on a difference. A change to a management API model means running `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and committing the result."],[13110,"The whole call"],[10936,"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL."],[12632,"The whole conversation scrolls as one. A tool's output, a compaction summary and a question being edited scroll on their own when they are long; once one reaches its top or its end, scrolling on in the same direction (the wheel, a trackpad or a swipe) moves the conversation instead of stopping there."],[8923,"The whole conversation; Hoshimi keeps no 