ream. Their body looks like `{\"code\": \"…\", \"message\": \"…\", \"detail\": {}}`. An OpenAI-shaped `{\"error\": {…}}` is an error from upstream or from routing instead; see the sections below."],[13529,"These IDs use the thinking menus declared by the reference implementation; other IDs follow the shared capability table (see Model behaviour)."],[15501,"These key-billed services also support `hoshimi login`; see their pages for details:"],[9745,"These options apply to this start only and are not written to `config.json`. An empty string for `--access-token`, `--model-api-key` or `--default-model` has no effect; the configured value is kept."],[12978,"These options are kept in the current browser and affect only it:"],[8539,"These provider options (in `providers.<id>.options`) adjust the behaviour:"],[11987,"These repositories sit as local clones in the repository root, to compare protocols and behaviour against. They are all in `.gitignore`: they never enter this repository and Hoshimi does not depend on them."],[14868,"These services' addresses, protocols and catalogue endpoints are built in, so an account needs only a key."],[15257,"These translations make requests acceptable to NIM; they are not full OpenAI feature parity. Whether a request succeeds is finally decided by the key's permissions, quota and model access."],[8520,"These two endpoints are compatible with Anthropic Messages and serve clients such as the Anthropic SDKs and Claude Code. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600` (clients add `/v1/messages` themselves), authenticated with the model API key sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer` (see API overview). Usage examples are in Anthropic SDK."],[9933,"These variables must be in the environment of the process that runs Hoshimi, which matters especially for a system service. The account formats are in Cloud platforms."],[10021,"Thinking and effort"],[7996,"Thinking can be switched off"],[13533,"Thinking can be switched off"],[8023,"Think