ol access key and the model API key each protect and how to send them; how the client network, Host and origin checks work; and how to open the gateway to your LAN safely."],[12859,"What these do in the Playground is in Playground."],[10975,"What this buys: the domain logic can be tested and reused without a server, and the domain exceptions (`hoshimi/core/errors.py`) are mapped to HTTP responses by the API and to exit codes by the command line, while `core` stays out of it."],[10215,"What you need"],[10214,"What you need to point an SDK, curl or a coding agent at Hoshimi: the Base URL, which key to send, how to write model names, which API to use, and the conventions for streaming, reasoning effort and tool calls."],[12728,"What you see"],[12000,"What you see after starting Hoshimi for the first time: what appears in the data folder, the layout of the interface, signing in when an access key is set, the two anonymous channels that are on by default, and where everything is."],[12044,"What you see the first time"],[3575,"wheel 和 sdist 的输出目录"],[7936,"When"],[8999,"When"],[9353,"When"],[11449,"When"],[14862,"When `api_key` (or `access_token`, `token`) has a value it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer`; otherwise no auth header is sent."],[10014,"When `config.json` cannot be parsed, every command that reads the configuration (including `serve`) refuses to run, and first copies the file to `config.json.corrupt-<timestamp>`; the error message gives the copy's path. Fix or delete `config.json` and try again. The file's location and format are in Configuration."],[10912,"When `config.json` is not valid JSON (or not a JSON object), the server refuses to start. It first copies the file to `config.json.corrupt-<UTC time>` and names that copy in the error message. Fix or remove `config.json`, then start again."],[13301,"When `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is set, the data folder is wherever it points. `hoshimi config path` prints the full path of the configuration file; the folder it is in is the data folder."],[9048,"When `model` is absent, `server.default_model` is used (**Settings** › **General** › **Default model**, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`)."],[8243,"When `server.host` is `0.0.0.0` or a LAN address, a tool access key and `security.allow_cidrs` are required, or the server refuses to start (exit code 4). Follow \"Opening the gateway to your LAN\" in Access control, or set `server.host` back to `127.0.0.1`."],[11379,"When a `v<version>` tag is pushed, the build job requires the tag to match `hoshimi/version.py` (`0.5.0` goes with `v0.5.0`) and fails otherwise."],[10640,"When a browser opens the Web UI through the public name, writes such as saving settings or sending a message carry the public `Origin`, which differs from the forwarded `Host`, and are refused (`403 bad_origin`). Add the public address (such as `https://hoshimi.example.com`) to `security.allow_origins`."],[8282,"When a catalogue fetch fails, the gateway keeps the last good catalogue and retries after 30 seconds; the **Models** page says **Catalogue unavailable or timed out: …. Existing models are retained.** A loading round waits at most 20 seconds and marks slow channels as timed out; refresh a little later."],[8119,"When a channel has no account left to try at all (all need a login or are held), the answer is `502`: `Provider '…' exhausted all accounts.`"],[8086,"When a channel has several accounts, a request starts with the first usable one, skipping accounts that need a login or are held out of rotation. After a failure, the kind of failure decides what happens next:"],[8311,"When a channel request fails, the message looks like `<channel>: <category>; <advice>`, with the same categories as `kind` in the network diagnostics:"],[10334,"When a configured proxy cannot be reached, the request fails. It **never** falls back to a direct connection."],[12720,"When a conversation nears the window, it is **compacted**: a model writes a summary of the conversation so far (the goal, the decisions and why, what is done and still to do, the files involved, the next step), and from then on the model reads that summary, with your latest messages kept word for word, in place of everything before it. The conversation itself stays on screen. A line marks where it was compacted; press it to read the summary."],[8340,"When a model cannot read images (`vision` is `false` in its capabilities), the Playground has the **Image model** (`playground.vision_model`) describe the image in words first, and says above the reply **The image “…” was described by …, because this model can’t read images.** When no model can read it, or the **Image model** is **Off**, it says **The image “…” was left out: no model could read it.**"],[8343,"When a model does not support tool calls, or the upstream refuses `tools` before the reply starts (an error mentioning tool, tool_choice or function call), the Playground retries without tools and says **… can’t call tools, so it answered without them.** Pick a model that supports tools (**Tools** on the **Models** page). Turning tools on and the approval modes are covered in Playground tools."],[8303,"When a model is saturated (such as CodeBuddy's `14003`, \"model busy\"), the gateway returns the upstream's message without rotating: every account would get the same answer. Use another model or try later."],[8341,"When a model should read images but the upstream refuses the image before the reply starts (an error mentioning image, vision, multimodal and the like), the Playground retries once with descriptions and says **… refused the image, so it was sent as a description.**"],[10068,"When a model's provider has a Messages endpoint of its own (the `anthropic` provider, for example), Hoshimi forwards the request unchanged except for the model name, and the upstream handles every field Claude Code sends. Models on other providers go through protocol conversion, and recent Claude Code versions send things the conversion does not support. Tested locally with Claude Code 2.1.308 (`claude -p`), converted models answered:"],[8284,"When a new list suddenly has fewer than half the models, the old list is kept for one cycle and the log says `the catalogue came back at N of M models (likely a partial answer)`; if the next cycle agrees, it is accepted and the log says `accepting it as the station's own answer`."],[12384,"When a provider has several ways to authenticate, choose one under **Authentication method** first, such as Bedrock's **API key**, **AWS access keys**, **AWS profile**, **AWS default credentials**; Vertex's **API key**, **Google default credentials**, **Google service account file**; EAC's **Bundled EAC relay (GitHub sign-in)**, **Custom EAC worker relay**, **Direct EAC Bearer relay**."],[9653,"When a request body does not match an endpoint's schema, `/v1/messages` answers `400` (`Invalid Messages request body.`) and other endpoints answer the framework's default `422` with `{\"detail\": [...]}`."],[10254,"When a request carries both `Authorization` and `x-api-key`, `Authorization` wins."],[10261,"When a request has no `model`, Chat Completions and Responses use **Default model** from **Settings** › **General** (config key `server.default_model`, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`). Messages always requires `model`."],[7866,"When adding an EAC account on the **Channels** page you can pick the bundled relay, a custom worker relay or a direct relay. Or write it in the configuration:"],[11211,"When an account has a native Anthropic Messages endpoint, its URL and headers; `/v1/messages` then passes requests through whole"],[8628,"When both are present, `output_config.effort` wins. For models whose upstream protocol is Messages, `thinking`, `output_config` and `metadata` are passed through."],[10316,"When changes apply"],[10654,"When changes take effect"],[13168,"When channels need a hand (a new login, an expired token, an account held out of rotation, an allowance about to run out), the **Channels** icon shows how many."],[10102,"When Claude Code does not recognise a model id it prints a notice that it assumes a 200k context window; that notice comes from Claude Code itself."],[8117,"When every account has been asked and the last failure was recoverable (not credentials, quota, policy or a missing model), the gateway waits and tries the pool again, at most twice. The wait is `Retry-After` or the body's reset time when given, capped at 8 seconds; `Retry-After: 0` means at once. Otherwise it is random (a ceiling starting at 0.25 seconds that doubles, up to 8 seconds)."],[11279,"When every account has been tried and the last error is the kind that time may change, the pool makes up to `backoff_retries` more passes: it waits for the time the upstream named (at most `backoff_max_seconds`), or a random wait (full jitter) when none was named. Once content has gone out, it never retries."],[11285,"When fetching fails, the previous result is kept and fetching is retried after 30 seconds; with no earlier success, `fallback_models()` is used."],[10638,"When Hoshimi listens on loopback and a reverse proxy on the same machine forwards to it:"],[10534,"When Hoshimi runs as a system service, the service manager collects the logs (for example `journalctl`); see Installation."],[9896,"When it is not set, the data folder is:"],[9911,"When it is read"],[10669,"When it takes effect"],[10629,"When listening on a non-loopback address without the prerequisites, the server refuses to start:"],[10604,"When listening on loopback, the `Host` header is a loopback name or the listening address (DNS-rebinding protection)"],[9560,"When missing or wrong"],[7939,"When models are listed or a bare model id is looked up (including opening the **Models** page or the Playground, and `hoshimi check`), then cached for 5 minutes"],[8661,"When none is declared, or the native endpoint answers `404`, `405` or `501`, Hoshimi returns a local estimate with the header `x-hoshimi-token-count: estimate`. The estimate approximates from the UTF-8 size of `system`, `messages`, `tools` and `tool_choice` (about one token per 3 bytes, at least 1), accepts native document and tool blocks, and runs no tokenizer."],[12503,"When nothing matches, the page says **No models match**."],[8347,"When old JSON records were imported after an upgrade, this file could not be read; it was renamed aside and that record started empty. Nothing else is affected; delete it if you do not need it."],[12963,"When one channel needs a different route, **Per-channel routes** takes you to the Channels page, where the channel's **Network** section overrides it. See Network and proxies."],[15594,"When only one channel is enabled, an unknown ID is passed to it unchanged."],[10238,"When port 10600 is taken, the server moves on to the next free port; use the address it prints at start-up. **Listening address** under **Settings** › **Access** shows the port in use."],[10913,"When saved from the Web UI or the management API:"],[9882,"When set, all of Hoshimi's data moves to this folder together:"],[10173,"When streaming, read it from `chunk.choices[0].delta` with `getattr(delta, \"reasoning_content\", None)`. `reasoning_effort` takes `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, or a model's own level name; the **Models** page lists each model's levels, and OpenAI-compatible API has the mapping."],[10344,"when that variable is empty, `ALL_PROXY`;"],[8306,"When the browser and Hoshimi are on different machines, the callback cannot reach Hoshimi. Use `hoshimi login <channel> --no-open --manual`: open the printed link in any browser, finish there, and paste the address the browser ended on (or the authorization code) back into the terminal. Not every station supports manual input."],[15285,"When the browser is not on the machine running Hoshimi, paste the address the browser finally lands on into **Authorization code or callback URL** and click **Submit code**."],[13527,"When the caller sets `tool_c