re"],[11138,"Where"],[12013,"Where"],[15539,"Where accounts come from"],[8007,"Where capabilities come from, highest priority first:"],[12610,"Where chats are kept"],[12900,"Where commands run when the model names no shell. **Automatic** is bash (`sh` without it; PowerShell on Windows, `cmd` without it), and its help text shows the one in effect (\"Now bash\"). The menu lists only the shells installed here; a model can still ask for any other of them"],[10643,"Where config.json lives, how to change it, and every key: type, default, meaning, validation rules, and when each change takes effect."],[10569,"Where credentials are kept"],[13649,"Where each provider definition comes from, its endpoint and protocol, how it authenticates, and how far Hoshimi covers it. Generated."],[10463,"Where Hoshimi keeps its configuration, database and other files, what each holds and for how long, where the logs go, and how to back up, reset and migrate from older versions."],[9495,"Where the conversation is compacted, and the room kept for a reply"],[10464,"Where the data directory is"],[10644,"Where the file is"],[7830,"Where the GitHub authorization token comes from"],[10805,"Where the tools work; `~` is expanded. Empty means `<data directory>/workspace`"],[11356,"Where the version lives, how the wheel gets the built Web UI and is checked, what each of the four CI workflows does, how one push publishes a new version to PyPI and GitHub, and how the docs site is deployed."],[11396,"Where the wheel and sdist go"],[12006,"Where things are"],[10228,"Where to find it"],[8227,"Where to look"],[8352,"Where tokens and cache counts come from"],[12904,"Where tools start, and the only folder whose files they can edit. The help text shows the path in effect"],[11168,"Whether a default availability probe asks about this provider's models"],[13490,"Whether a model answers depends on the upstream's current models, quota and service state, and can differ by the region your network exits from. This page describes how the adapters work, not a promise about upstream availability."],[8776,"Whether a tool access key / model API key is set"],[8827,"Whether availability depends on region"],[13461,"Whether availability depends on the network exit's region."],[11298,"Whether calling it costs nothing; three-way, with `None` for \"the station did not say\""],[13447,"Whether it is a thinking model."],[11329,"Whether it is implemented; unimplemented ones are not registered"],[8400,"Whether it succeeded"],[8705,"Whether PyPI has a newer release"],[8232,"Whether the configuration reads and validates, and which channels and how many accounts would run"],[13445,"Whether the model accepts image input."],[8835,"Whether the model is held out (the station answered 404/410 on every account)"],[8398,"Whether the response was streamed"],[8829,"Whether the station says it is free; `null` when it says nothing"],[9036,"Whether thinking can be disabled"],[11302,"Whether thinking can be switched off, whether the region matters"],[8825,"Whether thinking can be turned off"],[8778,"Whether this request comes from the server's own machine"],[11038,"Whether to serve the Web UI (`hoshimi serve --no-ui` and the tests pass `False`)"],[13102,"Which account of which channel answered"],[10218,"Which API to use"],[12390,"Which fields each cloud service needs is in Cloud services and Local and compatible endpoints."],[12687,"Which model describes images is the **Image model** setting. **Automatic** takes the first model in the catalogue that reads images, skipping any the last availability probe found unavailable or region-blocked. **Off** never asks: the image is left out and the reply says so. You can also pick one model."],[10315,"Which requests are covered"],[10309,"Which route Hoshimi takes to upstream stations: environment proxies, direct or a configured proxy, per-channel overrides, which requests are covered, and how to read the network diagnostics."],[10012,"While `serve` runs, Ctrl+C shuts the server down cleanly: it ends long-lived connections such as the live usage stream first, then exits."],[12223,"While a call is reviewed, its card shows **Reviewing…** and the reply's foot line **Reviewing *tool*…**. Review time counts as the reply's own working time; time waiting for you is left out of \"Worked for\"."],[12685,"While a description is being written the reply shows \"Reading the image with *model*…\"."],[12652,"While a reply is running only `/status`, `/permissions` and `/new` run; the others say why they can't. A slash followed by something that is not a command, such as `/etc/hosts`, is sent as a message."],[12727,"While a reply runs, a line at its foot says what it is doing (writing, running or reviewing a tool, compacting the context) and for how long, second by second. The clock stops while a tool call waits for your approval; time the review model takes counts. When the reply ends, **Worked for 1m 23s** (or **Stopped after**, **Failed after**) stays beside its actions; point at it to see when it started and ended."],[12279,"While a reply with tools is running, you can add to it without stopping it. The box reads \"Add to what it’s doing…\"; type and press Enter (or the button, now **Send to the reply under way**)."],[12512,"While a round runs the button reads **Probing…**, and clicking again does not start a second one. When it ends you see **Probe round finished** and the list updates."],[9587,"While bound to a loopback address, `Host` is not `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1` or the bound address"],[13058,"While calls are running, **Running now (N)** appears under the tiles with a card per call, the same as Live activity in the top bar."],[10616,"While listening on a non-loopback address (such as `0.0.0.0`) there is no Host check; access is controlled by the network allowlist and the keys. `security.allow_hosts` (**Allowed hosts**) is saved and shown, but this version's check does not read it."],[15635,"While no model API key is set, `api_key` can be any value; once one is set, requests must send `Authorization: Bearer <model-api-key>`."],[11522,"While the API restarts, Vite's proxy prints at most one \"API is not answering\" line every 5 seconds and answers requests with HTTP 502 and `{\"code\": \"api_unreachable\", ...}`, instead of a screen full of connection errors."],[10615,"While the server listens on a loopback address (`127.x.x.x`, `localhost`, `::1`), the request's `Host` header (without its port) must be `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1` or the listening address itself; anything else gets `400 bad_host`. This stops a malicious web page from using DNS rebinding, pointing an outside domain at `127.0.0.1` to reach your gateway."],[12417,"While timed renewal is on, the Channels page refreshes every 30 seconds, so renewal results show up by themselves."],[10100,"While waiting on the upstream, a streaming response gets a `ping` event every 15 seconds, only ever between complete events."],[10039,"While waiting on the upstream, Hoshimi inserts a `ping` event between complete events every 15 seconds; the SDK skips it."],[12939,"Who may connect. Press Enter after each value, or paste several at once (separated by spaces or commas); the × on a value removes it."],[9937,"Why"],[11907,"Why"],[9284,"Why a reply failed"],[8412,"Why it ended"],[13480,"Widening the catalogue with an API key"],[2080,"Windows"],[2660,"Windows"],[2844,"Windows"],[5478,"Windows"],[9901,"Windows"],[10481,"Windows"],[10665,"Windows"],[13297,"Windows"],[10780,"Windows only: in `auto` mode, use the system proxy when no environment proxy is set"],[10313,"Windows system proxy"],[2492,"Windows 系统代理"],[2096,"Windows，没有设置 `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` 时"],[7930,"With **Daily check-in** on, it runs 30 seconds after the server starts and then every 24 hours, using calendar days in Beijing time (UTC+8) to decide whether today is done. Accounts are checked in one after another, never in parallel. The **Channels** page has **Claim now** and **Check in all**."],[13019,"With **Day**, a day navigator appears: the arrows step to the **Previous day** and **Next day**, and the button between them (**Today**, **Yesterday** or a date) opens a calendar. Days with usage are shaded by how many tokens they had; days after today, or before the first recorded day, cannot be chosen."],[12413,"With **Settings › Automation › Credential renewal** on (the default), the gateway starts 30 seconds after launch and goes over every account with a refresh token every 30 minutes, renewing those whose token expires within the hour or that record no expiry at all. The renewed token is written back to that account in `config.json`."],[13288,"With `--host` set to `0.0.0.0` or a LAN address, anyone who can reach this machine could spend your upstream accounts. Hoshimi refuses to start until both a tool access key (`server.access_token`) and allowed networks (`security.allow_cidrs`) are configured. The full procedure is in Security."],[9774,"With `--json`, the exit code is 0 even when no channel is enabled."],[9752,"With `--open`, the address is opened in a browser a moment later."],[9826,"With `--open`, the link opens in a browser; if no browser can be opened, you are asked to visit it by hand."],[8639,"With `\"stream\": true`, each event is sent as two lines, `event: <type>` and `data: <json>`:"],[10070,"with `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1`: `400 <provider>: Messages roles must be user or assistant; use top-level system.` (this version puts a `system`-role message inside `messages`)"],[10080,"With `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY=1`, Claude Code asks the gateway for its model list to fill the model picker. Hoshimi waits at most two seconds on the `GET /v1/models?limit=1000` it sends: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while discovery finishes in the background, and each entry carries a `display_name`."],[10361,"With `network.system_proxy` set to `true` (**Use Windows system proxy when no environment proxy exists** in the Web UI), on Windows, `auto` mode reads the system proxy settings (including their exception list) when no environment proxy was found. The option has no effect on other systems."],[8129,"With `server.auto_checkin` on, the first check-in round runs 30 seconds after start, then one every 24 hours. Days are calendar days in Beijing time (UTC+8); once an account has checked in for the day (or the station says it already has), the day is not repeated. Accounts are checked in one after another, never in parallel, to avoid tripping the stations' risk controls. Every outcome, scheduled or manual, joins a 365-day history."],[7923,"With a bare model id, the gateway takes the first channel in its built-in order that lists it, and `/v1/models` shows only that entry. To choose the channel, write `channel/model`, such as `kilo/<model id>`."],[13558,"With a credentialed account, the catalogue includes every chat model the account can see; `options.free_only: true` keeps it to free models."],[8017,"With a level, there are three cases:"],[13439,"With a single station you need no declarations. With several, use `models` to pin IDs to the right account, so a request does not land first on a station that does not know the ID."],[9678,"With a tool access key set, both addresses require it: opening them in a browser gives `401`, and the buttons are hidden. Fetch the OpenAPI document with the header:"],[12367,"With accounts: runs a renewal round for this channel"],[10618,"With an `Origin` header, it must equal the page's own origin (`http://` or `https://` plus the request's `Host`), or be listed in `security.allow_origins`, or `allow_origins` must contain `*`."],[13494,"With an account"],[11525,"With an API already running elsewhere, `python scripts/dev.py web-dev` starts only Vite. It proxies to `http://127.0.0.1:10600` by default; for an API at another address, set the `HOSHIMI_BACKEND` environment variable to it first (for example `http://127.0.0.1:10601`).