upied slots. Lower limits take effect as existing streams finish. Cancelling a queued native Messages request prevents dispatch. Changing accounts or credentials clears account-specific temporary waits while retaining provider and model waits."],[9839,"Without `--json`, the JSON is coloured and the last line is the configuration file's path."],[14860,"Without `base_url` the default address is used; an account can be just an `id`."],[8840,"Without `models`, or with an empty list, every model of the providers that need probing is probed. The answer is the same snapshot plus `started` (whether a new round actually began; `false` while one is already running, as rounds do not stack) and `unresolved` (model names that could not be resolved). What probes mean is in Model and account behaviour."],[9846,"Without a configuration file, the readable keys are those the defaults have (the entries under `network`, `server` and `security`)."],[8015,"without a level the body is sent as is, and the caller's own `max_tokens` is kept. The Playground's **Auto (server default)** sends no level."],[8053,"Without a model list, the probe covers `opencode`, `nvidia` and `agg`, the channels whose listings cannot tell availability. Kilo's free list is already filtered upstream and is not in the default round."],[13281,"Without a Web UI build, the server logs a warning and serves the API only. The development setup (dev dependencies, a hot-reloading UI) is in Development setup."],[8803,"Without an `id`, one of the form `<provider>-<n>` is generated; an existing `id` answers `409`; an unknown provider answers `404`."],[10619,"Without an `Origin` header, if the browser sent `Sec-Fetch-Site`, it must be `same-origin` or `none`."],[7865,"Without an authorization the relay answers `401 AuthorizationRequired`; the gateway reports `eac: the relay demands this install's GitHub authorization (set the account's user_token)` and does not renew or rotate accounts over it."],[24,"worker"],[7845,"worker"],[